window.SUNO_SONGS = [{"id":"001","slug":"ryu-no-uta","title":"龍の歌","titleNote":"","album":"《梦》","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 5-39","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"132","length":"about 3:30","style":"Epic Japanese symphonic power metal with folk touches at 132 BPM in D minor. A powerful male tenor sings in Japanese, low and restrained in the verses, then heroic and open-throated in the chorus, holding the last note of every line. Palm-muted rhythm guitars and double-kick drums drive the verses, taiko drums and a low shakuhachi answer the vocal phrases, and in the chorus a male choir, twin lead guitars and a string orchestra open wide. Dark mythic mood of a dragon crying over night mountains, bittersweet yet triumphant. The song ends on a held vocal note and one final taiko hit. Polished wide stereo mix, vocal-forward balance.","exclude":"English vocals, female lead vocal, rap, autotune, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, acoustic ballad, lo-fi, children choir, spoken intro, reggae","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, low taiko heartbeat and a distant shakuhachi over a cold wind drone, then strings swell upward, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | male lead, low and restrained, slightly behind the beat, one breath per line, palm-muted guitars and taiko only]\n龍が叫ぶ夜の空、\n古き闇に夢が溶ける、\n刃の響き時を裂いて、\n魂叫ぶ白い月。\n\n[Verse 2 | same voice a little brighter, snare and bass enter, shakuhachi answers after every second line]\n山河の音風が運ぶ、\n戦士たちの悲しい歌、\n昨日の影背負いながら、\n未来に進む赤い目。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | full heroic voice, open vowels held at line ends, male choir doubles the lead, twin guitars and strings soar, taiko on every downbeat]\n龍の翼広げ、\n星屑舞い上がる、\n不滅の魂よ、\n永遠に響け。\n\n[Verse 3 | back to the restrained lead, double-kick drums enter, tension climbing, strings in long notes]\n川の流れ永遠に続く、\n命の歌草を揺らす、\n金属の響き夜を照らし、\n心震える古き夢。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | even bigger than before, lead belts the high notes, choir and guitars in harmony, same melody as the first chorus]\n龍の翼広げ、\n星屑舞い上がる、\n不滅の魂よ、\n永遠に響け。\n\n[Bridge | half-time feel, drums drop out, lead almost spoken then rising, blades of guitar tremolo, one long crescendo]\n刃の光影を裂く、\n鼓動響く地平の先、\n夢と現実交わる時、\n龍の歌が未来を描く。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, full band and choir ring out, guitars fade first, strings hold a chord, last taiko hit, then silence]\n[End]","notes":["原稿没有 intro/outro 标签，已补；第二段 [Verse] 改为 Verse 2/3 编号，两遍副歌文字完全一致以鼓励旋律重复。","刃 可能被读成 は 或 やいば；若读错，用 v6 歌词精修只替换那一个词，不要整首重抽。","每个主歌 4 行、副歌 4 行，音节数在 7-11 之间，132 BPM 下不会挤；副歌前加了 [Break] 给歌手换气。"]},{"id":"002","slug":"awa-awa","title":"沫沫沫沫沫","titleNote":"","album":"（沫沫沫沫沫）","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 42-90","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"94","length":"about 3:30","style":"Melancholic Japanese dream pop at 94 BPM with glassy bubble-like synth plucks and shimmering reverb guitar. A breathy female vocalist sings in Japanese close to the microphone, almost whispered in the verses and opening into layered harmonies in the chorus, unhurried and slightly behind the beat. A soft sub bass and a light sidechained pad breathe underneath, a dry kick and rim click enter in the chorus, and a music-box melody twinkles between phrases. Nostalgic and bittersweet, like watching soap bubbles drift away in morning light. Ends on a fading synth bubble. Vocal-forward, airy, spacious mix.","exclude":"male vocals, rap, screaming, heavy distortion, metal, trap hi-hats, orchestral brass, English vocals, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, glassy synth pluck motif over a soft pad, a music box answers, room for breathing, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | breathy close-mic female voice, sparse arrangement, only pad and pluck, one breath at every comma, unhurried]\n目を開けると、太陽が部屋に差し込む、\n新しい一日に、君が浮かぶ、\nぼんやりとした笑顔が、心に響き、\n僕の人生に、希望が宿る。\n\n外に出て、そよ風と踊る、\nけれど突然、割れた鏡が傷をつける、\n見つけたのは僕自身、\n壊れた僕の姿、\n泡のように砕け散り、\n虹のように瞬く。\n\n[Chorus | voice opens up with layered harmonies, kick and bass enter, bubbles of synth bounce on each repeated word, wide and warm]\n泡よ、泡よ、数えきれぬ泡よ、\n見えない数の泡よ、\n離れて、離れて、何度も離れて、\n君は何度も去っていく。\n\n夢幻、夢幻、無限の夢幻、\nその夢に僕は浸る、\n愛してる、愛してる、愛してる、\nもう一度君に言いたいよ。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to whispered close-mic voice, soft kick stays, sparse guitar harmonics, fragile and tender]\nもう一度、過去で君に会った、\n変わらない美しさ、その声は変わらず、\n君の手を握りたい、笑顔を忘れないように、\nでもできない、届かない。\n\n君の香りが、僕を包む、\n僕の忠誠は君のために、\n僕の愛は泡のように、\n美しい光を放つ、\n僕の愛は泡のように、\n儚くも淡い色彩。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the whole mix is filtered and swells, one beat of full silence, then the full band and bubbles burst back in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest and brightest version, lead belts softly over stacked harmonies, glassy arpeggios, same melody as the first chorus]\n泡よ、泡よ、数えきれぬ泡よ、\n見えない数の泡よ、\n離れて、離れて、何度も離れて、\n君は何度も去っていく。\n\n夢幻、夢幻、無限の夢幻、\nその夢に僕は浸る、\n愛してる、愛してる、愛してる、\nもう一度君に言いたいよ。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, bubbles pop one by one, pad fades, music box plays the intro motif once, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原文全角空格已改成「、」做呼吸点（全角空格会让 Suno 跳行）；[drop] 改成明确的\"2 小节静默+全员进入\"描述。","夢幻/無限 都读 むげん，是双关，若读成 ゆめまぼろし 用歌词精修改读音即可。","副歌「泡よ、泡よ」重复结构较密，已在每个重复词后加逗号，Style 里写了 unhurried，避免抢拍。"]},{"id":"003","slug":"suisei-mushi","title":"酔って生夢死","titleNote":"","album":"（酔って生夢死）","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 93-160","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"112","length":"about 3:20","style":"Dark neon synth-rock at 112 BPM with a nocturnal city-pop sourness. A male vocalist sings in Japanese with a smoky, slightly drunk baritone, restrained and spoken-like in the verses, shouting and ragged in the chorus. Driving analog bass, tight live drums with a gated snare, pulsing neon synth arpeggios and an angular clean guitar carry the verses, while the chorus adds distorted rhythm guitars and gang vocals. Hazy, decadent, self-destructive mood of walking a crowded city at night, free and hopeless at once. Ends with the synth arpeggio looping alone and cutting off. Wide stereo mix with punchy low end.","exclude":"female lead vocal, orchestral strings, acoustic folk, reggae, ballad, children choir, English vocals, lo-fi hiss, opera","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, neon synth arpeggio and gated drums fade in, sub bass pulses on the downbeat, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | male baritone, half-spoken and weary, bass and drums tight, synth arpeggio quiet, one breath per line, behind the beat]\n新しい日が始まる、\n人混みの街を歩く、\n酔いしれた夜景の中、\n高慢な心を蝕んでいく。\n\nまだ聞いている、考えてる、\nまだ歩き続け、夢見てる、\nただ遠い故郷は、\nまるで私を見捨てたよう。\n\n[Bridge | chant section, the lead shouts the city and the parenthesized lines are the crowd answering in gang vocals, hard drums, synth stabs]\n都市、\n都市、\n（ネオン）\n（飲もう！）\n都市、\n都市、\n（酔わせて！）\n（この時代に！）\n\n[Chorus | brighter and wide, ragged shouting lead, gang vocals double the title line, distorted guitars join, drums push forward but vocals stay on the beat]\n酔生夢死の人生、\n酒で狂った意識、\n自由を放つ生の中、\n欲望で魂を解き放つ。\n\n酔生夢死の人生、\n殺戮で満たす意識、\n自由を放つ生の中、\n絶望で自分を縛る。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the weary baritone, drums thin out to kick and hat, guitar harmonics, darker and more intimate]\n全てを捧げて、\n罪を償う運命、\n牢獄から逃れようと、\nこの海原で一人漂う。\n\n私は人間の画家、\n私は地獄のピアニスト、\n太陽は私のために踊り、\n月は私にバイオリンを奏でる、\nああ、何度も繰り返す、\nいつもこんな風に。\n\n[Bridge | chant section again, same call and answer, a little louder, synth stabs sharper]\n都市、\n都市、\n（ネオン）\n（飲もう！）\n都市、\n都市、\n（酔わせて！）\n（この時代に！）\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of silence, then a heavy synth bass hit and full band slam back in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, colder and more desperate, gang vocals louder, guitars distorted, same melody as the first chorus]\n酔生夢死の人生、\n酒で狂った意識、\n自由を放つ生の中、\n欲望で魂を解き放つ。\n\n酔生夢死の人生、\n殺戮で満たす意識、\n自由を放つ生の中、\n絶望で自分を縛る。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars stop, the neon synth arpeggio loops alone for four bars, then cuts off abruptly, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["bridge 的「都市/都市/（ネオン）/（飲もう！）」是一唱一和的顺序问答，所以括号保持独立成行（紧跟主唱），并在段落标签里写明括号行是人群应答。","酔生夢死 读 すいせいむし；若被读成「よってせいむし」就用歌词精修只改这一处。","副歌两个对比（欲望/绝望）靠标签里的\"brighter / colder\"区分，歌词两遍保持完全相同。"]},{"id":"004","slug":"yume-no-sennen","title":"夢の千年","titleNote":"","album":"（夢の千年）","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 163-197","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"86","length":"about 3:30","style":"Atmospheric cinematic Japanese alternative rock at 86 BPM that builds slowly from a quiet verse to an anthem. A female alto sings in Japanese, hushed and airy in the verses, then clear, wide and soaring in the chorus with sustained line endings. A clean arpeggiated electric guitar and a low cello carry the verses, a brushed kick and soft toms enter in the pre-climb, and the chorus opens with layered harmonies, driving drums, distorted guitars and a string section. Mystical mood of an ancient wind, a dragon's shadow and a thousand-year night under the stars, lonely yet determined. Ends with the guitar arpeggio alone and one long reverb tail. Spacious, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, metal screaming, English vocals, autotune, comedy, spoken word","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, clean arpeggiated guitar alone with long reverb, a low cello joins on bar five, distant wind texture, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | hushed female voice, airy and close, guitar arpeggio only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n僕の心は暗闇、\n夢見るは千年夜、\n星空の下で霧、\n静けさの中叫ぶ。\n\n[Verse 2 | same voice a little stronger, cello enters, brushed kick starts, an old voice echoing from below the earth]\n大地の底から響く、\n古き声が呼ぶ、\n奇怪な力感じる、\n運命の鎖裂く。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | voice opens wide and soars, line endings held long, layered harmonies, full drums and distorted guitars enter, strings swell]\n自由を求めて、\n古代の風に乗る、\nこの運命を超えて、\n夜空へと飛び立つ。\n\n[Verse 3 | drops back to hushed voice, guitar and sparse toms only, the dragon's shining scales in shadow]\n龍の影が踊る、\n光る鱗が輝く、\n鷹の目を持つ、\n僕らの魂震える。\n\n[Bridge | building, voice rising from whisper to full tone, drums return with a snare roll, strings climb, one long crescendo]\n時を超えて巡る、\n勇気の火を灯す、\n痛みと共に生きる、\n永遠の道を進む。\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest and brightest version, lead belts the high notes over stacked harmonies, drums and guitars at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\n自由を求めて、\n古代の風に乗る、\nこの運命を超えて、\n夜空へと飛び立つ。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, full band falls away, guitar arpeggio alone, last chord rings with long reverb, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿没有 intro/outro，补了慢热型结构：clean 吉他分解 → 弦乐 → 全乐队；第二个 Chorus 前用 Bridge 的渐强过渡。","句子都很短（4-9 字），所以 BPM 放低到 86 并用 [Break] 留白，不必靠 [Silence] 标签。"]},{"id":"005","slug":"huakuang","title":"画框","titleNote":"","album":"《书中书》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 203-271","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"76","length":"about 3:40","style":"Dark chamber art-pop with a slow trip-hop beat at 76 BPM in C minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female alto sings low and dreamy, close to the microphone, half-whispered in the verses and opening into a fuller, slightly bitter voice in the chorus, with a hummed second voice answering her phrases. A prepared piano and a low cello carry the verses, a dusty brushed kick and snare fade in under the bridge, and the chorus adds warm sub bass, a wide string pad and a sharp cymbal swell. Eerie, elegant and claustrophobic mood of a world locked inside a picture frame, wet paint and an endless night. Ends on the piano with one last cello note. Vocal-forward mix with deep reverb.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, heavy distortion, upbeat dance beat, autotune, children choir, male lead vocal","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, prepared piano and a low cello, a soft paintbrush-scratch texture, brushed trip-hop beat fades in on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | female alto, low and dreamy, close-mic, piano and cello only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat, parenthesized lines are quiet hummed answers]\n画框禁锢着一个世界，\n一个虚幻而不可触及的世界，\n桌上的颜料是鲜红的血，\n画布的恶臭盖过世间的一切。\n（嗯……）\n\n画框拥抱着一个世界，\n一个梦幻而又温暖的世界，\n它不会在末日里毁灭，\n也不会在现实里破裂。\n（嗯……）\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, a call and answer: the lead sings the single word and a soft layered voice answers in the parenthesized line, brushed beat only]\n画框，\n（禁锢了我）\n画笔，\n（涂抹着我）\n请你，\n（擦去了我）\n还要，\n（着色了我）\n\n[Chorus | fuller bitter voice, warm sub bass and string pad enter, kick and snare steady, cello answers after each pair of lines, line endings held]\n画中的人儿想出来，\n画外的人儿门不开，\n你在画中耍无赖，\n我在画外称精彩。\n\n画中的你们恩恩爱爱，\n画外的我们相互加害，\n他在画中认了栽，\n她在画外落了败。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the hushed voice, piano and cello, a little more tense, parenthesized lines are quiet hummed answers]\n画框品尝着一个世界，\n世界懦弱地磕头拜谢，\n蓝色的幻景在眼前重叠，\n精灵问我他们是否体贴。\n（嗯……）\n\n画框勒索了一个世界，\n还有一个不会黯淡的夜，\n人们哭泣狂欢着道别，\n用笔画下自己的罪孽。\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, same call and answer as before, brushed beat only, slightly louder]\n画框，\n（禁锢了我）\n画笔，\n（涂抹着我）\n请你，\n（擦去了我）\n还要，\n（着色了我）\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, cymbal swell and filtered strings, one beat of full silence, then the whole band and strings land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and bitter, doubled by a whispered layer, strings and sub bass at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\n画中的人儿想出来，\n画外的人儿门不开，\n你在画中耍无赖，\n我在画外称精彩。\n\n画中的你们恩恩爱爱，\n画外的我们相互加害，\n他在画中认了栽，\n她在画外落了败。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, strings fall away, piano repeats the intro motif alone, one last low cello note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["「（嗯……）」是接在主唱后面的顺序应答，保持独立成行；bridge 的「画框/（禁锢了我）」同理是一问一答，没有合并成一行。","原稿 [drop] 改成明确的静默一拍 + 全乐队进入；最后一遍 Chorus 标为 Final Chorus。","可能读错：着(zhe)、还(hái)、落(luò)；读错就用歌词精修只换那个字的同音字。"]},{"id":"006","slug":"wheel-of-destiny","title":"The Wheel of Destiny","titleNote":"","album":"《命运之轮》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 276-325","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"84","length":"about 3:30","style":"Hypnotic dark synth-pop with dream-pop haze at 84 BPM in A minor. A female alto sings in English, hushed and breathy in the verses and lifting into a wide, airy chorus with layered harmonies, unhurried and slightly behind the beat. A slowly rotating analog arpeggio, a deep warm bass and soft clock-like percussion carry the verses, and the chorus adds a wide pad, a gated snare and a shimmering lead synth that circles back on itself. Dreamlike and fatalistic, like a great wheel turning in the dark. Ends on the arpeggio slowing down until it stops. Vocal-forward mix with spacious reverb.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, screaming, heavy metal guitars, trap hi-hats, country, acoustic folk, orchestral brass, children choir","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a slow rotating arpeggio alone, a soft clock-tick percussion enters on bar five, deep bass swells underneath, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | hushed breathy female voice, arpeggio and bass only, one breath per line, behind the beat, sparse and hypnotic]\nSpinning quietly, turning so slow,\nSilent motions, where shadows glow.\nThe fading remnants remain in the past,\nDreams like bubbles vanish so fast.\n\nI am watching, you are listening,\nTime sings of love that's everlasting.\nEchoes of fate resound and call,\nTelling me everything, I feel it all.\n\nTouching the shore where doubt is found,\nI won't forget the first time we were bound.\n\n[Break | arpeggio holds one note, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | voice lifts wide and airy, layered harmonies, gated snare and wide pad enter, lead synth circles around the vocal, line endings held]\nSpinning, spinning, round and round,\nThe wheel of fate is turning down.\nStilling, stilling, it comes to rest,\nThe universe stirs deep in our chest.\n\nSinging, singing, through the night,\nThe endless loop repeats its flight.\nForgetting, forgetting, all that's known,\nLet the world lead me to my fall, alone.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the hushed voice, arpeggio and bass, heartbeat kick added, more urgent and fragile]\nMotionless heartbeats, trapped in a maze,\nStruggling silently in a daze.\nA kiss, a tear, rips through my mind,\nYearning so wild, lost in time.\n\nYou are speaking, I am listening,\nGods sing of life that's shimmering.\nEchoes of moments, soft and bright,\nTelling me everything, I feel the light.\n\nTouching the shore that lies ahead,\nPlease don't forget, let my soul be led.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the machinery stops, filtered pad swells, one beat of full silence, then the whole band returns together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, lead belts softly over stacked harmonies, full drums and bright synth, same melody as the first chorus]\nSpinning, spinning, round and round,\nThe wheel of fate is turning down.\nStilling, stilling, it comes to rest,\nThe universe stirs deep in our chest.\n\nSinging, singing, through the night,\nThe endless loop repeats its flight.\nForgetting, forgetting, all that's known,\nLet the world lead me to my fall, alone.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and pad fall away, the rotating arpeggio slows down note by note until it stops, one low bass tone, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["主歌是 10 行的长段，原文不能删，所以按 4+4+2 拆成三个小节并用空行换气；副歌句尾逗号/句号交替。","原稿里 [Drop] 后直接接 Chorus，现在写成 2 小节的\"齿轮停转 + 一拍静默\"，再进入最后的副歌。"]},{"id":"007","slug":"eternal-return","title":"Eternal Return","titleNote":"","album":"（Eternal Return）","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 328-363","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"108","length":"about 3:20","style":"Cosmic synth-pop with an anthemic indie-rock lift at 108 BPM in E minor. A warm male tenor sings in English, intimate and clear in the verses, then open-chested and soaring in the chorus with long held vowels at the ends of phrases. Pulsing analog bass, a shimmering octave arpeggio and tight live drums drive the verses, and the chorus adds big reverb snare, wide supersaw pads, bright clean guitar and layered group harmonies. Romantic, vast and hopeful mood of two souls reborn again and again through stars and time. Ends on the arpeggio fading into a long shimmering pad. Polished wide stereo mix, vocal-forward.","exclude":"female lead vocal, rap, growl, metal distortion, country, lo-fi, spoken word, trap hi-hats, orchestral brass","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, shimmering octave arpeggio over a deep pad, kick and bass enter on bar five, a rising synth sweep, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | warm male tenor, intimate and clear, bass and drums tight, arpeggio quiet, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nPoincare returns in cosmic waves,\nThrough stars and dust our love behaves.\nEternal circle skies unfold,\nMolecular secrets left untold.\n\n[Verse 2 | same voice, a little brighter, clean guitar enters, hi-hat opens up, building toward the chorus]\nRebirth dances in the night,\nAtoms sparkle in the light.\nLife's a cycle round we spin,\nTo find each other once again.\n\n[Chorus | open-chested and soaring, long held vowels at line ends, big reverb snare and supersaw pads, group harmonies stack behind the lead]\nEvery turn we're born anew,\nThrough time and space my love for you.\nInfinite stages we perform,\nIn the dark we find our form.\n\n[Bridge | half-time feel, drums drop to kick only, whispered lead over arpeggio and pad, then a snare roll lifting back up]\nGalaxies whisper our names,\nIn celestial endless games.\nFate reweaves our bonded souls,\nIn this cosmos we console.\n\n[Verse 3 | lead returns tender, bass groove alone under it, the last two short lines are spaced with a held beat of silence between them]\nAstral tides keep hearts aligned,\nReincarnation in our mind.\nStars reshuffle,\nBreaths restart,\nTimeless passion in our heart.\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, lead belts the high notes over stacked harmonies, full band at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\nEvery turn we're born anew,\nThrough time and space my love for you.\nInfinite stages we perform,\nIn the dark we find our form.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums stop first, arpeggio and pad ring out and fade into a long shimmering tone, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿没有 intro/outro，已补；Verse 3 的「Stars reshuffle / Breaths restart」是两个短句，各自带逗号形成顿挫。","Poincare 读 /pwæ̃kɑːreɪ/，若读成英式 poin-care，用歌词精修只改这一个词的拼写即可。"]},{"id":"008","slug":"toukasha","title":"窃火者","titleNote":"","album":"《第二封情书》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 369-446","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"68","length":"about 4:40","style":"Cinematic Mandopop rock ballad at 68 BPM in B minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male tenor sings with a tender, devout, slightly husky tone, intimate and nearly spoken in the verses, then rising to a wide, aching and sustained chorus where he holds the end of each line. A felt piano and a low cello carry the verses, soft brushed drums and a warm bass enter in the second half, and the chorus opens into a string orchestra, big reverb drums, a distant choir and a slow soaring electric guitar. Reverent, romantic and vast mood, a lover as a sacred light above an endless sea of ash, like a lighthouse in the dark. Ends on the piano alone with one long string note. Vocal-forward, wide cinematic mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune, female lead vocal, fast tempo, shouting","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, felt piano alone with long reverb, a low cello joins on bar five, a distant wind texture, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 4, male tenor, intimate and nearly spoken, piano only, one breath per line, behind the beat]\n若非直面你的瞳孔，\n我几乎忘却自己双眼的散光，\n夜晚的车灯汇聚，\n光团在身前发散，\n若星海闪耀，\n有如银河坠陨人间，\n可它们却不及与你对视之刹那的万分之一。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 4, same hushed voice, cello holds long notes under the piano]\n星辰是拙劣的模仿者，\n于你睁眼时自惭形秽，\n大海借鉴了它们的浩瀚，\n天空模仿着它们的清澈，\n就连宇宙本身，\n也在臣服中效仿它们的深邃，\n圣洁光芒充盈尘世、洗涤污秽、抚慰我心。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 4, voice slightly warmer, soft brushed drums and a warm bass enter, slow and steady]\n当万物终焉，\n天地将借由你的瞳色浸染自身，\n待冰河逆流，\n众生将裹挟你的温度冉冉重生，\n你的心火炽热而温柔。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 4 of 4, voice lifting, strings swell slowly, the last line is sung with awe and a held final word]\n溢出灵魂，\n流向每一条干涸的水道，\n又悄然绽放在世界之巅，\n众神中的一员匆匆一瞥，\n于是高加索山有了一位窃火者。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | wide, aching and sustained voice, full string orchestra and big reverb drums enter, distant choir behind, electric guitar soars slowly, line endings held long]\n我是最忠实的信徒，\n在光阴破碎、神启喧扰的人间，\n觐见永恒中唯一的奇迹，\n跪求虚无中缥缈的怜悯，\n若生命有意义，\n那它应受你应允，\n若岁月有痕迹，\n则你为其流动之痕迹，\n当我挣脱归墟的漩涡，\n脱离终焉的寂灭，\n你是无尽灰烬海之上唯一的亮光，\n似灯塔指引迷茫的船只，\n如引力叙说既定的方向。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the hushed tender voice, piano and cello only, drums gone, intimate and slow]\n你知道，\n当我看向晚霞，\n并不只是在看晚霞，\n而是借由这些天穹在宇宙的幽灵，\n搭建一条与你相见的桥梁，\n你也知道，\n当我想你，\n也不仅仅是在是思念你，\n而是同样屈服于无穷概率与不可达之领域间，\n你存在于此刻的证明。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, strings rise and the voice swells with each line, brushed drums return, building toward the climax]\n当群星啜泣，\n当夕阳凝望，\n当天幕披上名为“黄昏”的薄纱，\n霞光会如血海激荡在穹顶，\n而那粉色的，\n会化作心底最轻柔的内衬。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings and choir swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then the whole orchestra and drums land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest and most devoted version, lead sings at full power with aching sustained notes, orchestra, choir and guitar at the peak, same melody as the first chorus]\n我是最忠实的信徒，\n在光阴破碎、神启喧扰的人间，\n觐见永恒中唯一的奇迹，\n跪求虚无中缥缈的怜悯，\n若生命有意义，\n那它应受你应允，\n若岁月有痕迹，\n则你为其流动之痕迹，\n当我挣脱归墟的漩涡，\n脱离终焉的寂灭，\n你是无尽灰烬海之上唯一的亮光，\n似灯塔指引迷茫的船只，\n如引力叙说既定的方向。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, orchestra and drums fall away, piano plays the intro motif alone, one long string note holds, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["第一段共 26 行，原文不能删，所以拆成 4 个小节（Verse 1 part 1-4），每节一个独立演出指示+空行，防止后半段被赶拍。","原稿 [Chorus] 前没有空行、第二遍 Chorus 前的 [drop] 描述为空，现已补成明确的\"静默一拍 + 全乐队进入\"。","可能读错：觐(jìn)见、归墟(xū)、啜(chuò)泣、冉(rǎn)冉、应允；读错用歌词精修换同音字，不要整首重抽。","文件1后半段那份无标签的纯文本重复稿（448-500 行）是同一首的整理版，已核对文字一致，未单独处理。"]},{"id":"009","slug":"fire-thief-en","title":"Fire Thief (English Ver.)","titleNote":"原稿无标题，是《窃火者》的英文版，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"《第二封情书》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 502-570","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"72","length":"about 4:00","style":"Ethereal cinematic dream-pop ballad at 72 BPM in D minor. A female alto sings in English, hushed and intimate in the verses, then wide, aching and sustained in the chorus with long held line endings and layered harmonies. A soft felt piano and a shimmering reverb guitar carry the verses, a slow brushed kick and warm bass enter in the second half, and the chorus opens into strings, big reverb drums and a distant choir. Reverent and romantic mood of someone kneeling before a lover's eyes, brighter than stars, with a lighthouse glowing over a sea of ash. Ends on the piano alone with one long string note. Vocal-forward, wide cinematic mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, screaming, country, autotune, spoken word, fast tempo","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, felt piano alone, a shimmering guitar harmonic joins on bar five, distant wind texture, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | female alto, hushed and close-mic, piano and soft guitar only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nIf not for meeting your two pupils deep,\nI might forget the secrets my own eyes keep.\nThe way night traffic's bright and blinding stream,\nBecomes a scattered, astrological dream.\n\nA thousand headlights blur into a haze,\nA galaxy that shines in my flawed gaze.\nIt’s like the Milky Way has fallen near,\nBut pales the moment that your eyes appear.\n\n[Chorus | voice opens wide and aching, line endings held long, strings and a warm pad enter, brushed drums steady, harmonies stack in the last two lines]\nYour eyes, where all the stars forget to shine,\nThey hide their face before a light so divine.\nThe endless ocean just reflects their grace,\nThe sky just steals the clearness from that space.\nAnd even the universe, in silent awe,\nSurrenders to their depth, their perfect law.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the hushed voice, piano and cello, brushed kick added, tender and slow]\nWhen all of creation meets its final days,\nThe world will tint itself in your eyes’ haze.\nWhen glaciers flow back up the mountain high,\nAll life reborn will feel your warmth nearby.\n\nYour heart-fire, both so tender and so bright,\nIt overflows your soul with gentle light.\nIt blooms upon the world's most lonely peak,\nA god once glanced, and made Prometheus weak.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then drums, bass and strings land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Chorus | stronger and wider than the first, big reverb drums, choir behind, same melody as the first chorus]\nYour eyes, where all the stars forget to shine,\nThey hide their face before a light so divine.\nThe endless ocean just reflects their grace,\nThe sky just steals the clearness from that space.\nAnd even the universe, in silent awe,\nSurrenders to their depth, their perfect law.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down to piano and whispered voice, a fragile spoken-sung line, then strings rise slowly]\nAnd you know, when I watch the sunset burn,\nIt's not for fading, golden light I yearn.\nI use those ghosts of color in the blue,\nTo build a fragile bridge that leads to you.\n\nAnd you know, when you occupy my mind,\nIt's more than just a memory I find.\nIt’s proof that you exist, against the void,\nA single truth in worlds that were destroyed.\n\n[Chorus | full power, voice wide and bright, drums and choir at full, same melody as the first chorus]\nYour eyes, where all the stars forget to shine,\nThey hide their face before a light so divine.\nThe endless ocean just reflects their grace,\nThe sky just steals the clearness from that space.\nAnd even the universe, in silent awe,\nSurrenders to their depth, their perfect law.\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, the new words, devoted and trembling, piano and strings only, voice soft but full of emotion]\nI am the one most faithful, your believer,\nIn this loud world, a reverent receiver.\nBefore the only miracle, I kneel,\nAnd beg for mercy from what feels so real.\nIf life has meaning, it's by your decree,\nIf time has marks, those marks were made by thee.\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, drums and choir return, voice swells to full power and holds the last line long]\nWhen I escape the endless, swirling grey,\nAnd from the final darkness break away,\nAbove the sea of ash, you are the one,\nA lighthouse shining when the day is done.\nLike gravity, your truth will see me through,\nAnd in the end, will guide me home to you.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, orchestra and drums fall away, piano plays the intro motif alone, one long string note holds, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿最后一个 [Chorus] 文字与前三遍不同（是「I am the one most faithful」），已改标为 Final Chorus 并拆成 2 个小节，前三遍副歌文字保持完全一致。","原稿 [drop] 描述为空，现写成明确的静默一拍 + 弦乐与鼓一起进入。"]},{"id":"010","slug":"my-angel","title":"my angel","titleNote":"","album":"《第二封情书》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 577-623","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"70","length":"about 3:40","style":"Haunting dark synth-pop ballad at 70 BPM in F-sharp minor. A female voice sings in English, soft and fragile in the verses, then aching and full in the chorus with long sustained line endings and a breath of vibrato at the ends. A soft piano with gentle strings opens the song, a deep warm synth bass and a slow muted kick carry the verses, and the chorus adds big reverb drums, wide strings and a glowing pad. Cold, tender and longing mood of someone waiting forever in a frozen land for an angel who left. Ends on the piano with one fading string note. Vocal-forward, spacious mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, EDM drop, screaming, country, fast tempo, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, soft haunting piano with gentle strings, a distant synth pad breathes underneath, slow and cold, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | soft fragile female voice, close-mic, piano and strings only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nMy angel, have you forgotten the day we met?\nMy angel, do you remember the first gaze we set?\nMy angel, perhaps you don’t wish to recall,\nThe moment we spoke, before the world could fall.\n\nYouth and passion, they’ve all drifted far away,\nBut here I stand, with thoughts I cannot sway.\nI wait, though time may steal my heart's sweet song,\nI still hold on, though the night feels so long.\n\n[Chorus | voice aching and full, long held line endings, big reverb drums and wide strings enter, pad glows behind, harmonies in the last two lines]\nLike a blade in the cold, you tore me apart,\nLeaving me with pieces of a shattered heart.\nBut if you’d want me, I’d give my blood to the sky,\nWriting a letter, with no tears, just a sigh.\n\nIf I could, I’d trade my soul with the devil’s hand,\nJust to guard you, in this frozen land.\nWillingly, forever I’ll stay,\nLoving you, come what may.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the soft fragile voice, piano and a muted kick, cold and intimate]\nThe days of youth are gone, so far they’ve flown,\nBut the memories linger, though we’re both alone.\nYour cold touch, it cuts, but I still feel the burn,\nFor your love, I wait, hoping you'll return.\n\nI’d trade the stars, just to hear your voice,\nAnd with every breath, I would still rejoice.\n\n[Bridge | the bass drops in with a deep emotional synth swell, drums pause, voice stays close and trembling, the last two lines rise slowly]\nIf you’d come back, I’d wait a lifetime more,\nFor you to walk through that open door.\nThrough the storms, through the endless night,\nI’ll stand alone, but I’ll be alright.\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and bright, drums, strings and pad at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\nLike a blade in the cold, you tore me apart,\nLeaving me with pieces of a shattered heart.\nBut if you’d want me, I’d give my blood to the sky,\nWriting a letter, with no tears, just a sigh.\n\nIf I could, I’d trade my soul with the devil’s hand,\nJust to guard you, in this frozen land.\nWillingly, forever I’ll stay,\nLoving you, come what may.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, strings and drums fall away, piano plays the intro motif alone, one last fading string note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 [Instrumental Intro] 和 [Drop] 后面的括号是制作说明（\"Soft, haunting piano…\" / \"Bass drops…\"），括号会被 Suno 当成歌词唱出来，已移进方括号并扩写；这两段文字不再出现在歌词里。","原稿 [Drop] 下面其实带有 4 行唱词，不是纯器乐，所以改标为 Bridge，并写明\"低音合成器落下、人声保持脆弱\"。"]},{"id":"011","slug":"inji","title":"印记","titleNote":"","album":"《第二封情书》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 628-675","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"72","length":"about 3:30","style":"Warm Mandopop acoustic ballad at 72 BPM in G major, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male tenor sings soft and sincere, close to the microphone in the verses, then opening into a clear, bittersweet and sustained chorus with a touch of breath at the ends of phrases. A fingerpicked nylon guitar and a soft felt piano carry the verses, a muted kick and warm upright bass enter in the bridge, and the chorus adds strings, brushed drums and a gentle electric guitar echo. Nostalgic, tender mood of a glance that left a mark on a whole life, longing like a rainbow after rain scattering in the wind. Ends on the guitar alone with a long reverb tail. Vocal-forward, natural warm mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, female lead vocal, screaming, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, fingerpicked nylon guitar alone, a soft felt piano answers on bar five, gentle room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | soft sincere male tenor, close-mic, guitar only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n只是不经意间的一瞥，\n余光中的身影就被记忆刻写，\n一天天又一年年，\n挥之不去的容颜，\n总是伴我每个深夜。\n\n[Bridge | piano joins the guitar, upright bass enters softly, voice a little warmer and lifting at the end of each pair of lines]\n你走过的道路，\n枯萎花木为你复苏，\n你看过的风景，\n黑暗时刻仍然光明。\n\n[Chorus | clear bittersweet voice, long held line endings, strings and brushed drums enter, electric guitar echoes the vocal phrase]\n在我的，人生中，\n你留下不可磨灭的印记，\n无法避免在你目光中沉溺，\n转眼间，就成空，\n如那雨后的长虹，\n所有思念散在了风中。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the soft voice, guitar and a light piano, a little more yearning]\n只是不经意间的一瞥，\n余光中的身影就被记忆刻写，\n一天天又一年年，\n挥之不去的容颜，\n总是伴我每个深夜。\n\n[Bridge | piano and bass, voice warm and lifting, strings begin to swell]\n你说过的话语，\n是那最动人的歌曲，\n你每一次微笑，\n写尽了青春的美好。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then drums, bass and strings land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and bright, full strings and drums, same melody as the first chorus]\n在我的，人生中，\n你留下不可磨灭的印记，\n无法避免在你目光中沉溺，\n转眼间，就成空，\n如那雨后的长虹，\n所有思念散在了风中。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and strings fall away, nylon guitar plays the intro motif alone, long reverb tail, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["副歌「在我的 人生中」「转眼间 就成空」中间的空格改成逗号做呼吸点；两遍 verse 文字完全一致，便于旋律复用。","原稿的 [drop] 描述为空，现写成\"一拍静默 + 弦乐与鼓同时进入\"。副歌行数少（6 行），不会赶拍。"]},{"id":"012","slug":"sunset","title":"Sunset","titleNote":"","album":"《第二封情书》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 678-716","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"Off","bpm":"76","length":"about 3:20","style":"Warm indie-folk love song at 76 BPM in G major. A male tenor sings in English, gentle and close to the microphone in the verses, then open and glowing in the chorus with a soft female harmony floating above him. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar and a warm upright bass carry the verses, a soft brushed snare and a light piano enter in the chorus, and a lap steel plays long glowing notes between phrases. Tender, golden-hour mood of two people leaning on each other at sunset, time standing still. Ends on the guitar alone with a long ringing chord. Natural warm mix, vocal-forward.","exclude":"rap, screaming, distortion, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, metal, heavy synths, autotune, spoken word","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, fingerpicked acoustic guitar alone, a lap steel glows in on bar five, soft evening room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | gentle male tenor, close-mic, guitar and upright bass only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nThe sun sets low, the light ascends,\nYou lean on me, your heart my friend.\nI kiss your brow, so soft, so sweet,\nThe world is still, time’s gentle beat.\n\nStars fall quietly from the skies,\nThe evening’s glow, a soft surprise.\nThe sunset, endless in its grace,\nLove, the source of life’s embrace.\n\n[Chorus | open glowing voice, soft female harmony above, brushed snare and light piano enter, lap steel answers each pair of lines]\nIn this moment as the sun will go,\nLet me take your hand once more and hold.\nThe cycle of the universe will break,\nAll things will bow to hearts awake.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the gentle voice, guitar and bass, a little closer and warmer]\nThe twilight fades, the night arrives,\nI taste your breath, the way it thrives.\nYou linger near my warming skin,\nTime rewinds, where we begin.\n\nThe seasons turn back to our spring,\nThe galaxy witnesses our wedding ring.\nThe earth holds every word I say,\nAs love’s embrace guides our way.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everyone plays softly and stops together, one beat of silence, then the full band returns gently, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice open and warm, both harmonies together, full band, same melody as the first chorus]\nIn this moment as the sun will go,\nLet me take your hand once more and hold.\nThe cycle of the universe will break,\nAll things will bow to hearts awake.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, band falls away, guitar alone, lap steel holds one glowing note, last chord rings out, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 [Drop] 为空，且这首是温柔的民谣，不适合 EDM 式 drop，所以写成\"全员轻轻停一拍再进入\"的温柔版本。","副歌只有 4 行，重复两遍，文字完全相同；情绪柔和，Max Mode 可关以省积分。"]},{"id":"013","slug":"mieru","title":"看得见","titleNote":"","album":"（看得见）","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 721-808","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"80","length":"about 4:00","style":"Dreamy Mandopop R&B with a hazy electronic pulse at 80 BPM in A minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female vocalist sings airy and tender, close to the microphone, with unhurried relaxed phrasing and a slight breath at the ends of lines, floating into soft layered harmonies in the chorus. A warm Rhodes piano, a rounded sub bass and a slow soft snare carry the verses, a glassy synth pad and a faint guitar echo open up the bridge, and the chorus adds a gentle four-on-the-floor kick and shimmering vocal doubles. Wistful, intimate mood of someone remembering a smile in a foggy rainbow-colored memory. Ends on the Rhodes alone with the pad fading. Vocal-forward, soft spacious mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, screaming, heavy distortion, metal, fast tempo, trap hi-hats, male lead vocal, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, warm Rhodes piano alone, a soft synth pad breathes in on bar five, light rain texture, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | airy female voice, close-mic, relaxed phrasing, Rhodes and sub bass only, a breath at every comma, slightly behind the beat]\n淡薄云雾，朦胧沙尘，迷离晴天白云，\n漫步小桥流水，回荡遥望，都市人群，\n暖意不觉散开，溢向四方，难以追寻，\n心结难解，心火难熄，唯有空留残韵，\n于幻境中，孤影独行，\n听回音中的低吟，\n（愿安宁）\n\n[Bridge | very soft and slow, voice almost whispered, one note of pad per line, drums pause, space after every line]\n岁月匆匆，\n谁与共，\n旧日彩虹，\n已然冰封，\n暗淡的缤纷，\n在消融，\n情愫暗涌，\n回忆无穷。\n\n[Chorus | voice floats up with layered harmonies, gentle kick enters, parenthesized lines are soft close answers sung just after the lead line]\n你的每一次微笑，\n（我看得见）\n你的每一句情话，\n（在我耳边）\n你的每一次心跳，\n（如此亲切）\n你的每一缕秀发，\n（再靠近些）\n\n[Verse 2 | tender spoken-sung voice, the chain of short words is sung in small groups with a breath after each comma, Rhodes and bass, slow]\n做过错过，走过路过，记过忘过爱过，\n看我听我，吻我拥我，念我知我伴我，\n困惑迷惑，跌落坠落，落寞懦弱闪烁，\n诺言不多，心绪衰弱，漠看渐散轮廓，\n大多往昔对我来说，\n如斑驳墙边花开花落，\n打一束灯火，\n华光自天际陨落，\n（丢魂魄）\n\n[Bridge | very soft and slow again, near-whispered voice, pad only, a pause after every line]\n盼望归来，\n无论何种姿态，\n自清自在，\n九重天之外，\n地底深埋，\n她亲手挖开，\n芬芳仍在，\n只需一丝忍耐。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little brighter, parenthesized lines are soft close answers sung just after the lead line]\n你的每一次微笑，\n（我看得见）\n你的每一句情话，\n（在我耳边）\n你的每一次心跳，\n（如此亲切）\n你的每一缕秀发，\n（再靠近些）\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, pad and Rhodes swell, one beat of full silence, then the full band returns together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and tender, stacked doubles, kick and bass full, parenthesized lines are soft close answers sung just after the lead line]\n你的每一次微笑，\n（我看得见）\n你的每一句情话，\n（在我耳边）\n你的每一次心跳，\n（如此亲切）\n你的每一缕秀发，\n（再靠近些）\nhoo~\n我始终，\n（在你的身边）\n我永远，\n（伴随你每一天）\n我不会，\n（许下任何诺言）\n因为我的存在，\n（基于你的容颜）\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and pad fall away, Rhodes plays the intro motif alone, last note rings, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这首最容易抢拍：verse 的 14 字长句和「做过错过走过路过…」连珠句，已按 4-4-6 字词组加逗号作为换气点，BPM 放到 80，并在 Style 写了 unhurried / relaxed phrasing。","副歌的「（我看得见）」「（在我耳边）」是接在主句后面的顺序应答，保持独立成行，并在标签里写明是柔声应答。","若 verse 2 的连珠句仍然挤，用 v6 分段编辑只重做那一段，并把 Variety 保持 Off。"]},{"id":"014","slug":"storm","title":"Storm","titleNote":"","album":"《罪恶世界》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 812-889","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"150","length":"about 3:20","style":"Stadium hard rock with power-metal energy at 150 BPM in E minor, sung in English. A male vocalist sings with a raspy, powerful tenor, gritty and spoken-shouted in the verses, then wide, fierce and sustained in the chorus with raw high screams between lines. Palm-muted chugging rhythm guitars, a galloping bass and double-kick drums drive the verses, the chorus opens with big open chords, a soaring lead guitar, gang vocals and crashing cymbals, and a howling wind and thunder texture runs underneath. Furious, godlike mood of a storm that tears through the sky and sweeps the world away. Ends with a crashing power chord and wind fading out. Punchy, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, lo-fi, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, rap verses, spoken word, children choir, reggae","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, howling wind and distant thunder, a lone palm-muted guitar riff builds, drums enter with a fill on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | gritty spoken-shouted male voice, palm-muted guitars and kick, each shouted word lands on the beat, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nSand! So much sand!\nIt spreads through Heaven’s land.\nI walk from Hell, to Eden I go,\nWith flames of hell still in tow.\n\nTornadoes tear through the air,\nI’ll destroy all that’s there.\nI rage and I roar,\nI’ll crush your pride, down to the core.\n\nNothing can stop me now,\nAh!\nI’m going insane!\nWow!\nI'm off the chain!\nHa!\nI hold it all in my hand,\nAnd I'll bury this land!\n\n[Chorus | wide fierce voice, big open chords, gang vocals double the shouted lines, lead guitar soars, high screams land in the gaps between lines, parenthesized lines are shouted by the gang]\nLet the storm take the world by storm!\nLet me own it, let it transform!\nI’m the furious god of war,\nOn Olympus, I soar!\n(Woah!)\nLook into my eyes!\nHear my mighty cries!\n(Ahhhhh! Ahhh! Wah wah wah!)\nStorm! (Storm!)\nWow!\nThe storm’s about to swarm!\n(Storm!!)\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the gritty shouted voice, guitars palm-muted, drums half-time, menacing]\nGreat winds! Such great winds!\nTornadoes sweep through the sins.\nI fall from Heaven, into Hell’s flame,\nGod's power leaks from His name.\n\nThe hand of God saves us all,\nI (Ah!)\nI (Wow!)\nI (Howl!)\nI’ll destroy your cities tall,\nI’ll crush your pride, break the wall.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, the shouts get faster and wilder, drums double-time, leave half a beat of air between every shouted line]\nNothing can stop me now,\nAh!\nKill me now!\nI’m insane!\nKill you all!\nSave me now!\nWow!\nThat’s how!\nOh!\nI’m off the chain!\nHa!\nNothing else remains!\nIt’s all mine!\nI hold it all in my hand,\nLook at me!\nI’ll bury this land!\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, wind and thunder stop on one beat of full silence, then the whole band slams back in with a crashing power chord, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, lead screams the high notes, gang vocals at full volume, double-kick at full speed, same melody as the first chorus, parenthesized lines are shouted by the gang]\nLet the storm take the world by storm!\nLet me own it, let it transform!\nI’m the furious god of war,\nOn Olympus, I soar!\n(Woah!)\nLook into my eyes!\nHear my mighty cries!\n(Ahhhhh! Ahhh! Wah wah wah!)\nStorm! (Storm!)\nWow!\nThe storm’s about to swarm!\n(Storm!!)\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars end on a crashing power chord, wind and thunder carry on alone and fade out, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["「Ah! / Wow! / Ha!」是夹在句子之间的顺序呐喊，保持独立成行；「I (Ah!)」这种行内括号保持原样。","Verse 2 后半是连续短喊叫，已拆成 part 1 / part 2 两个小节，part 2 标明\"每个喊叫之间留半拍\"，减少黏成一团。","原稿 [Drop] 描述为空，现写成\"风暴声急停一拍，再全员重击\"。"]},{"id":"015","slug":"zui","title":"罪","titleNote":"","album":"《罪恶世界》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 892-946","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"124","length":"about 3:30","style":"Heavy Chinese alt-metal with rapped verses at 124 BPM in D minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist raps in a low, gritty, spoken-shouted voice in the verses, then roars and sings with raw sustained high notes in the chorus while a gang of voices shouts echoes behind him. Down-tuned chugging guitars, a heavy bass and tight punchy drums drive the verses, a dark synth drone hangs underneath, and the chorus adds wide distorted power chords, crash cymbals and layered shouted crowd vocals. Guilty, weary and furious mood about inherited original sin and a city drunk on desire. Ends on a final heavy chord with feedback. Punchy, dark, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, lo-fi, comedy, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, dark synth drone and slow tom hits, a down-tuned guitar riff builds, full drums enter on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, low gritty rapped voice, guitar chug and kick only, each line lands on the beat with a short breath after it, slightly behind the beat]\n是谁说的，\n我们生来便有罪，\n有着与生俱来的原罪，\n沉醉在这欲望的都市烂醉，\n疲惫的身躯，劳累了身心，不得安慰。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same voice, bass and drums thicker, tension building]\n一而再再而三向后退，退到深夜里的黑，\n最终又是谁，当了偷窃时光的贼，\n岁月把恶毒藏进我的心内，\n或许我不配，于是我在沉睡中假寐。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | roaring sustained voice, wide distorted power chords, gang vocals are layered into the same line as the bracketed echoes, crash cymbals on every downbeat]\n罪（罪）（罪！）\n与生俱来的原罪，（罪！）\n带不走甩不掉的罪，（罪！）\n我们每个人都有罪，\n每个人都有罪，（有罪！）\n最罪的罪坠醉追不回！（最最罪的罪！）\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the low gritty rap, breath after each comma, drums half-time, menacing]\n贪嗔痴爱恨，生死情仇不分，\n一次次相互间封印了心门，\n圆滑的灵魂长出的尖棱，\n真叫他人难以触碰，\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, faster and angrier, drums double-time, shouts land on the downbeat with half a beat of air between them]\n是神？是人！还是我们（你们！）（他们！）\n太狠，太恨！太深！爱的太深！罪更深！\n等得到等不到还是在等，\n肯不肯坑不坑又如何不过是落叶归根！\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then a heavy guitar and bass hit with full drums, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, roaring high notes, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus, bracketed echoes are shouted by the crowd]\n罪（罪）（罪！）\n与生俱来的原罪，（罪！）\n带不走甩不掉的罪，（罪！）\n我们每个人都有罪，\n每个人都有罪，（有罪！）\n最罪的罪坠醉追不回！（最最罪的罪！）\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums stop, guitar holds one heavy chord with feedback, synth drone fades last, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["副歌里的「（罪！）」「（有罪！）」「（最最罪的罪！）」是同时叠加的呐喊回声，已并入上一行行尾（v6 括号=叠唱），不再单独成行；文字顺序未变。","verse 2 的连珠句「贪嗔痴爱恨生死情仇不分」按语义加逗号做换气点；「是神？是人！还是我们（你们！）（他们！）」行内括号保持原样。","可能读错：偷窃(qiè)、贼、假寐(mèi)、坑(kēng)、落叶归根。"]},{"id":"016","slug":"dushi","title":"都市","titleNote":"","album":"《罪恶世界》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 949-1016","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"92","length":"about 3:40","style":"Dark cinematic Chinese hip-hop with industrial rock edges at 92 BPM in F minor, rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male rapper delivers a low, gritty, controlled flow in the verses, almost spoken and menacing, then shouts the hook in the chorus with gang vocals behind him. A distorted sub-bass 808, a slow heavy kick and snare, a gritty industrial guitar loop and a cold string drone carry the verses, and the chorus adds wide distorted guitars, crowd shouts and crashing cymbals. Lonely and vengeful mood of a hunter walking a sleepless neon city at night, scarred and unbroken. Ends with the guitar loop alone and one last 808 hit. Dark, punchy, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, EDM drop, lo-fi, comedy, autotune, smooth jazz","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, cold string drone and a distant siren, an industrial guitar loop starts, 808 and a slow kick enter on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | low gritty rapped voice, controlled and menacing, 808 and kick only, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n我是个行走于暗夜的猎人，\n穷凶极恶之徒务必锁好房门，\n我将竖立一座座方石做的坟，\n你们的尸骨将留下受害者的刻痕。\n\n我是个闪烁在影子中的猎人，\n我的心是扎进地底的树根，\n我在工作时从来感受不到疼，\n除非乌鸦愿意给我一个吻。\n\n[Bridge | chant section, the lead barks each word and the crowd echo is layered inside the same line, hard snare on every word]\n猎人（猎人！）\n伤痕（伤痕！）\n报恩（报恩！）\n灭门（灭门！）\n\n[Chorus | shouted hook, wide distorted guitars, gang vocals double the lead, crash cymbals, half a beat of air between each pair of lines]\n走过了路翻过了山，\n踏遍每一个不眠的夜晚，\n蹚过了河游过了海，\n为什么还是这样不自由也不自在，\n\n刺穿了天跺碎了地，\n恶魔被迫交出自己的秘密，\n盗窃了神也抢劫了人，\n我无依无靠还他妈一事无成。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the low controlled flow, strings added to the drone, darker and more intimate]\n我是个飞翔在星河的猎人，\n沉默的月亮见证了我的隐忍，\n它不会委屈也不会发声，\n只有坑洞诉说着深仇大恨。\n\n我是个厮杀于角落的猎人，\n把刀枪送给这炽热的不夜城，\n所有的老鼠都能听见我的歌声，\n路边的石子全都能感受到我的奔腾。\n\n[Bridge | chant section again, same bark and layered echo, louder, snare harder]\n猎人（猎人！）\n伤痕（伤痕！）\n报恩（报恩！）\n灭门（灭门！）\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then 808, guitars and full drums slam in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, shouted hook at full power, gang vocals louder, same melody as the first chorus]\n走过了路翻过了山，\n踏遍每一个不眠的夜晚，\n蹚过了河游过了海，\n为什么还是这样不自由也不自在，\n\n刺穿了天跺碎了地，\n恶魔被迫交出自己的秘密，\n盗窃了神也抢劫了人，\n我无依无靠还他妈一事无成。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and 808 stop, the guitar loop plays alone for four bars, one last 808 hit, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["bridge 的「猎人（猎人！）」等是同时叠加的呐喊回声，已并入同一行（v6 括号=叠唱）。","副歌里连续的\"了…了…\"排比很密，已在每个半句后面留逗号并在标签里要求 \"half a beat of air\"。","含粗口「他妈」，按原稿保留。"]},{"id":"017","slug":"sniper","title":"Sniper","titleNote":"","album":"《甩狙战神》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1021-1065","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"140","length":"about 3:10","style":"Dark cinematic trap-rock at 140 BPM with a half-time feel, rapped and sung in English. A male vocalist raps with a confident, cold, menacing flow in the verses, almost whispered and precise like a sniper's breath, then sings and shouts the chorus with a gritty, sustained voice and gang vocals behind. Booming 808 bass, a slow heavy snare, sparse hi-hat rolls and a gritty detuned guitar loop carry the verses, a distant gunshot echo and a cold synth pad hang in the air, and the chorus adds distorted power chords and crowd shouts. Cold, lethal, legendary mood of a ghost hidden in forest leaves and desert sand. Ends with one gunshot echo and silence. Punchy, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, lo-fi hiss, children choir, comedy, jazz","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, cold synth pad and a distant wind, a detuned guitar loop starts, a slow 808 enters on bar five, one distant gunshot echo on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | cold precise rapped voice, almost whispered, 808 and a sparse snare only, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat, parenthesized words are low spoken ad-libs]\nHidden in the forest leaves, so deep,\nBuried under desert sands, they creep.\n(Oh!)\nYou'll never pin my location down,\nMy clues, unseen, will make you frown.\nA flick of wrist, the bullet bends,\nAs I leap, the silence descends.\n\n[Break | beat stops, one beat of silence, rapper breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | sung and shouted, gritty and sustained, distorted power chords enter, gang vocals double the title lines, drums hit hard on every downbeat]\nLook into my eyes,\nHear my gunfire cries.\nI'm the ace sniper, ghost unseen,\nEach bullet hits where your forehead's been.\nEvery breath I take's a reaper's sign,\nI taste your blood, your dignity's mine.\nYes,\nI'm the only legend here, divine.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the cold precise rap, 808 and snare with a rolling hi-hat added, slightly more aggressive, parenthesized words are low laughed ad-libs]\nSwallowing schools in the ocean's heart,\nSpewing endless flames, tearing apart.\n(Ha ha!)\nMy moves, elusive, can't be tracked,\nMy aim's precise, it's a proven fact.\nI throw my knife, it shatters your guard,\nTowards my target, I tread hard,\nEverything crushed under my feet.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then 808 and guitars slam in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, shouted at full power, gang vocals louder, same melody as the first chorus]\nLook into my eyes,\nHear my gunfire cries.\nI'm the ace sniper, ghost unseen,\nEach bullet hits where your forehead's been.\nEvery breath I take's a reaper's sign,\nI taste your blood, your dignity's mine.\nYes,\nI'm the only legend here, divine.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums stop, the guitar loop plays alone for four bars, one distant gunshot echo, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 intro 下面有个空的 [] 标签，会让 Suno 误读，已删除；「(Oh!)」「(Ha ha!)」是句间的顺序笑喊，保持独立成行。","140 BPM 但写了 half-time feel，实际人声走 70 BPM 的律动，避免英文 rap 行尾赶拍。"]},{"id":"018","slug":"the-young-man","title":"The young man","titleNote":"","album":"《甩狙战神》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1068-1103","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"Off","bpm":"138","length":"about 3:00","style":"Anthemic arena rock with a pop-punk drive at 138 BPM in A major, sung in English. A male tenor sings bright, fearless and slightly raspy, confident and punchy in the verses, then wide and shouted in the chorus with a crowd of gang vocals chanting the title line. Crunchy rhythm guitars, a melodic driving bass and big live drums carry the verses, the chorus adds soaring lead guitar, handclaps and stadium reverb, and a rolling thunder texture opens the bridge. Heroic, youthful mood of a young legend walking alone under the stars with a smile that cuts and a will of steel. Ends on a big sustained power chord. Bright, wide, punchy mix, vocal-forward.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, rap verses, EDM drop, lo-fi, country, spoken word, jazz","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a rolling thunder texture and a single clean guitar line, drums crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | bright confident male tenor, crunchy guitars and driving bass, punchy drums, a short breath after every line, on the beat]\nThrough storms he strides without a fear,\nHis steps break dawn, the dark draws near.\nIn every fight, he stands supreme,\nWith fate and power as his theme.\n\n[Chorus | wide shouted voice, open chords, soaring lead guitar, gang vocals chant the title line, handclaps on the backbeat, crowd echo layered into the last line]\nHe’s a fierce and fearless young man,\nWith eyes that pierce the sky’s wide span.\nEach second stronger than the last,\nHe moves ahead, leaving the past.\n\nHe’s a wild and daring young man,\nAll foes will bow to his command.\nHe is a legend! (A legend!)\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the bright punchy voice, bass and drums tight, guitars palm-muted, a little more determined]\nUnder stars, he walks alone,\nWith glory and might that he has grown.\nA smile that cuts, a will of steel,\nNo force can bend what he makes real.\n\n[Bridge | drums pause, rolling thunder and a single tremolo guitar, voice rises from steady to shouted over four lines, snare roll into the last chorus]\nThunder echoes where he walks,\nThe world awakens as he talks.\nHis path ignites with light and flame,\nA legend rises, none the same.\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice shouted at full power, gang vocals louder, same melody as the first chorus, crowd echo layered into the last line]\nHe’s a fierce and fearless young man,\nWith eyes that pierce the sky’s wide span.\nEach second stronger than the last,\nHe moves ahead, leaving the past.\n\nHe’s a wild and daring young man,\nAll foes will bow to his command.\nHe is a legend! (A legend!)\n\n[Outro | 4 bars, band lands on a big sustained power chord, thunder rolls away, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["「(A legend!)」是叠加在同一句上的回声，已并入「He is a legend!」同一行。","原稿 [Drop] 下面带 4 行唱词，不是纯器乐，所以改标为 Bridge（\"雷鸣\"段），并写明鼓暂停、吉他铺开。","歌词短，结构紧凑，Max Mode 可关。"]},{"id":"019","slug":"sishui-liunian","title":"似水流年","titleNote":"","album":"《孤独症患者》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1109-1158","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"76","length":"about 4:10","style":"Nostalgic Mandopop folk-rock at 76 BPM in G major, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male voice sings warm, slightly husky and honest, close to the microphone and almost spoken in the verses, then opening into a wide, aching and sustained chorus with long held line endings. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar and a soft piano carry the verses, a harmonica answers between phrases, a warm bass and brushed drums enter in the second verse, and the chorus adds strummed guitars, strings, big reverb drums and layered backing harmonies. Wistful, homesick mood of a musician remembering lost years, fireflies in a forest and a guitar that leads him back home. Ends on the guitar alone with one harmonica note. Vocal-forward, natural warm mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, screaming, autotune, female lead vocal","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, fingerpicked acoustic guitar alone, a soft piano joins on bar five, a lonely harmonica phrase on the last two bars, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, warm husky male voice, close-mic, guitar and piano only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n再写不出那样的歌曲，\n心灵与人生的共鸣似已离去，\n再遇不见那场迷离双眼的大雨，\n可为何那份模糊仍在我身前延续。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same voice, a little warmer, harmonica answers after each pair of lines]\n我梦到过刻骨铭心的爱恋，\n许下的承诺直达世界的终焉，\n我唱过青葱岁月峥嵘的理想，\n午夜孤泣的吉他领我重回故乡。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, voice lifting gently, warm bass enters, soft brushed drums begin]\n我偶遇过亿万萤火虫漂泊的森林，\n它们是黑暗中摇曳无定的光明，\n我弹奏过彩虹编织的琴弦，\n白云跳着舞蹦到我面前。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | wide aching voice, long held line endings, strummed guitars and strings enter, big reverb drums, backing harmonies stack in the last two lines]\n逝去的归来吧，爱过的回来啊，\n当初的那道身影是否还属于她，\n看过的重现吧，听过的回荡啊，\n带我引我回到那个家。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 3, back to the close honest voice, guitar and piano, bass and brushed drums stay, a little more weary]\n再记不起当初的那张容颜，\n炽热的情意似乎早已变迁，\n再无法回到的那些年，\n他们是否仍孤守在岁月的起点。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 3, more inward, almost spoken, guitar alone with the harmonica]\n我听过深夜时分自己灵魂的呢喃，\n矛盾与执念在心底最深处纠缠，\n我写过的情愫如浪起时的波澜，\n拍打在岸边最终只得轻叹。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 3 of 3, voice rising with pain, drums return, strings swell slowly]\n我镌刻过恒久持续的不甘，\n再度抚摸我的手指仍旧莫名发颤，\n我品味过枯萎的白花一瓣又一瓣，\n它们如刀割把我一次次摧残。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then drums, bass and strings land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, strongest version, voice wide and aching, full band and strings, same melody as the first chorus]\n逝去的归来吧，爱过的回来啊，\n当初的那道身影是否还属于她，\n看过的重现吧，听过的回荡啊，\n带我引我回到那个家。\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, the new words, voice breaks open on the high notes then holds the last line long, band at full power]\n爱过的再爱啊，恨过的又恨啊，\n愁肠百结的我如今在哪啊，\n触碰的消散吧，拥抱的淡化啊，\n我苦啊累啊还能哭出来吗。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and strings fall away, guitar plays the intro motif alone, one harmonica note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["两段主歌各 12 行，原文不能删，已按 4+4+4 拆成 part 1-3，各自带演出指示，防止后半被赶拍。","副歌「逝去的归来吧，爱过的回来啊」原稿已有逗号，保留；第二遍副歌多出的 4 行放在同一个 Final Chorus 里并要求\"愈唱愈开\"。","可能读错：还(hái)属于、重现(chóng)、一瓣又一瓣；读错用歌词精修只换那个字。"]},{"id":"020","slug":"bing","title":"病","titleNote":"","album":"《孤独症患者》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1161-1226","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"122","length":"about 4:00","style":"Manic Chinese art-punk and alt-rock at 122 BPM in E minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist sings with a strained, urgent, slightly cracked voice, half-spoken and shaky in the verses, then wide, ragged and sustained in the chorus with gang vocals shouting the key word. Angular jangly guitars, a driving melodic bass and tight live drums carry the verses, a warped carnival-like organ wobbles in the background, and the chorus adds distorted power chords, crash cymbals and layered crowd shouts. Unhinged but tender mood of a person who sees upside-down skies, upside-down rainbows and his own double waving at him, the whole world sick. Ends on a single distorted chord and a faint laugh of feedback. Raw, punchy, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, ballad, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, lo-fi, autotune, female lead vocal, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a wobbling carnival organ and an angular guitar line, bass enters on bar three, drums crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, strained half-spoken male voice, bass and guitar tight, drums sparse, a breath at every comma, slightly behind the beat]\n看看这颠倒的天地，听听这黑白不分的潮流，\n荒诞的人世间，等着谁来拯救，\n蒙着心，封闭了自身，关紧了心门，\n看不清数不清的苦恼，怎么也说不出口。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same shaky voice, drums fuller, organ wobbles louder]\n深夜独自抑郁，抚摸自己的伤痕，\n放不下的执念，缠绕我无边无际的祈求，\n画笔在空中画出太阳，\n画笔在地上画下月亮。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, voice rising, snare gets harder, building toward the chorus]\n一条条彩虹倒挂在眼中，\n蒸发后的色彩，弥漫梦中的朦胧，\n发起了疯，跳起了舞，\n期望如此，能够覆盖我恒久的麻木。\n\n[Chorus | wide ragged sustained voice, distorted power chords, gang vocals shout the key word, crash cymbals, the bracketed words are crowd echoes layered on the same line]\n我们每个人都有病，\n活在这个荒诞的世界，明天看不清，过往记不清，\n可我还在听，还在走着不停，\n啊，我这颗破碎又顽固的心，\n我们每个人都有病，\n握不住自己的命，碰不到幻象中的安定（安静！）\n有病（有病）（有病）\n有病！\n病！\n病的不轻！（啊！）\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 3, voice small and shaky again, bass and a single guitar, the friend inside the body whispers, drums nearly gone]\n我看到从我身体里走出的朋友，\n他对我招招手，\n他说你就是我，我就是你，\n我知道你所有的秘密，\n我知道你埋葬的奇迹。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 3, the parenthesized lines are whispered hallucinated voices, each one a quick hissed whisper after the previous line, nothing else playing]\n（嘘！）\n（快看！）\n（他们打算害你！）\n（小心！）\n\n[Verse 2 | part 3 of 3, voice cracks upward, drums return, guitars distorted, rising to the chorus]\n破碎的镜子，破碎的我，\n破碎的灵魂，破碎着堕落，\n破碎着堕入冷漠干枯的荒漠，\n漫无边际的黑暗潮水将我淹没，\n期待着，祈祷着，判决着，审判着，\n我在这，我在这（我在这我在这）（还在这）\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then the full band and organ crash back in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice ragged and loud, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus, the bracketed words are crowd echoes layered on the same line]\n我们每个人都有病，\n活在这个荒诞的世界，明天看不清，过往记不清，\n可我还在听，还在走着不停，\n啊，我这颗破碎又顽固的心，\n我们每个人都有病，\n握不住自己的命，碰不到幻象中的安定（安静！）\n有病（有病）（有病）\n有病！\n病！病！\n病的不轻！（啊！）\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums stop, the carnival organ wobbles alone, one distorted chord, a faint feedback laugh, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["括号处理：副歌里「（有病）」「（啊！）」「（还在这）」是叠加回声，已并入上一行；verse 2 里「（嘘！）（快看！）（他们打算害你！）（小心！）」是幻听的顺序低语，保持独立成行并在标签里注明。","verse 1 共 12 行，按 4+4+4 拆成 3 个小节；长句按语义加逗号换气，防止\"一口气念完\"。","「（安静！）」夹在副歌一行的末尾，原样保留。"]},{"id":"021","slug":"huanzhe","title":"患者","titleNote":"","album":"《孤独症患者》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1229-1305","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"84","length":"about 4:30","style":"Emotional Chinese alt-rock ballad at 84 BPM in B minor that builds from a hush to a roar, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist sings raw, honest and slightly hoarse, close to the microphone and almost spoken in the verses, then wide, broken and sustained in the chorus with a second voice echoing the key words. A clean electric guitar with long delay and a soft piano carry the verses, a warm bass and brushed drums enter in the second half, and the chorus adds a heavy snare, wall-of-sound guitars, strings and layered backing vocals. Proud, solitary and aching mood of a gifted loner who calls his loneliness an incurable disease. Ends on the piano with one distant guitar note. Vocal-forward, wide cinematic mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune, female lead vocal, fast tempo","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, clean guitar with long delay, a soft piano joins on bar five, a faint computer-fan hum, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, raw honest male voice, almost spoken, guitar and piano only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n有时我坐在电脑前，\n透过屏幕翻阅世间的一篇篇，\n数不清的作废的诺言，\n数不清的遗忘了的脸，\n二十多年是否寻觅到真正的知己，\n或许到头来仍然只有我自己。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same voice, slightly harder, warm bass enters, brushed drums begin]\n天赋是把利刃，\n割伤了握住它的每一个人，\n不求命运不信鬼神不拜天地，\n只坚定天上地下唯我独尊的道理。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, voice rising, the two repeated lines are sung with a small pause between them, strings enter softly]\n我开始染病，\n染上名为孤独自傲的绝症，\n我开始犯病，\n对着浩瀚无垠的宇宙尘封了心门。\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | wide broken sustained voice, heavy snare and wall of guitars, strings swell, bracketed words are a second voice echoing on the same line, long held line endings]\n我是个孤独症患者，（患者）（患者）\n孤独症患者，（孤独症患者）（孤独症患者）\n让我一个人留在这，\n把遗言镌刻等眼泪成河，\n我是个孤独症患者，（孤独症患者）（患者）\n孤独症患者，（孤独症）（患者）\n让我一个人留在这，\n把遗言镌刻等眼泪成河。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the raw hushed voice, guitar and piano, bass and brushed drums stay, a little more fragile and bitter]\n开始发了疯，继续发着癫，\n就这样空虚度过一年又一年，\n岁月在我身上留存的伤痕，\n哈哈，我只想说一点都不疼，\n我在唱我在跳，我在风雨中招摇，\n我在哭我在笑，我在入梦时舞蹈，\n没有药，没有救我的人，\n没有，没有，什么也没有。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, voice rising with pain, drums harder, strings climbing, the final lines are sung with a pause after each]\n我开始染病，\n染上名为孤独自傲的绝症，\n我开始犯病，\n对着浩瀚无垠的宇宙尘封了心门，\n开始犯病，\n开始犯病，\n治不了的病，\n无药可救的病患，\n我是孤独症患者。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then drums, guitars and strings land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice broken open on the high notes, backing voices at full volume, wall of guitars, same melody as the first chorus, bracketed words are echoes on the same line]\n我是个孤独症患者，（患者）（患者）\n孤独症患者，（孤独症患者）（孤独症患者）\n让我一个人留在这，\n把遗言镌刻等眼泪成河，\n我是个孤独症患者，（孤独症患者）（患者）\n孤独症患者，（孤独症）（患者）\n让我一个人留在这，\n把遗言镌刻等眼泪成河。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars fall away, piano plays the intro motif alone, one distant guitar note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["副歌里「（患者）（孤独症患者）」都是同一句上的回声，已并入上一行（v6 括号=叠唱），两遍副歌的括号位置完全一致。","verse 1 共 14 行、verse 2 共 17 行，已分别拆成 3 和 2 个小节；「我开始染病 / 我开始犯病」的叠句保持原顺序。"]},{"id":"022","slug":"dark","title":"dark","titleNote":"","album":"《尽头》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1310-1358","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"74","length":"about 3:50","style":"Gothic darkwave and post-punk at 74 BPM in C-sharp minor, sung in English. A deep male baritone sings in a cold, hollow, half-spoken voice in the verses, then rises to a wide, haunted and sustained chorus with a ghostly layered double behind him. A chorus-drenched clean guitar, a throbbing melodic bass and a slow mechanical drum machine carry the verses, a cold synth drone swells like a black hole, and the chorus adds huge reverb drums, a wall of tremolo guitars and a cathedral-like pad. Bleak, hopeless mood of an endless void swallowing the light, still longing for one flare of flame. Ends on the drone alone fading into silence. Spacious, dark, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, upbeat pop, major-key brightness, rap, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, acoustic folk","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a cold synth drone swells slowly, a chorus-drenched clean guitar plays a lone line, a throbbing bass enters on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | cold hollow baritone, half-spoken, bass and drum machine only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nI see the end ahead,\nA place of darkness, cold and dead.\nAn endless void that swallows me whole,\nFalling deeper, losing control.\n\nI see the shadows reign,\nA world where light has no domain.\nA black hole spinning, pulling all inside,\nThe world breaks down, nowhere to hide.\n\n[Chorus | voice rises wide and haunted, long held line endings, huge reverb drums, tremolo guitars and a cathedral pad, a ghostly double sings behind the lead]\nThe darkness devours me,\nIt consumes and towers me.\nThe shadows tear me apart,\nThey grip and shatter my heart.\n\nWhen will I see the light shine high?\nWhen will it burn through the darkened sky?\nForever waiting in despair,\nForever longing for the flare.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the cold baritone, drum machine stripped to kick and clap, a single guitar line, bleaker and quieter]\nI've forgotten the light of dawn,\nThe stars beyond feel lost and gone.\nA realm of void and emptiness wide,\nA place where dreams and hope have died.\n\nI yearn to see the light again,\nThe flame that burns beyond the pain.\nIn dreams it blazes, fierce and bright,\nIn longing thoughts, it takes its flight.\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, instrumental only, tremolo guitars swell over the throbbing bass, the drum machine builds with a rising snare roll, the drone climbs and then drops out on the last beat]\n\n[Chorus | strongest version, voice broken open on the high notes, the ghostly double doubles the lead, full wall of guitars, same melody as the first chorus]\nThe darkness devours me,\nIt consumes and towers me.\nThe shadows tear me apart,\nThey grip and shatter my heart.\n\nWhen will I see the light shine high?\nWhen will it burn through the darkened sky?\nForever waiting in despair,\nForever longing for the flare.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, one huge reverb drum hit and a sub bass boom, then everything stops on one beat of full silence, vocals rest]\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, only the cold synth drone remains, a distant guitar harmonic once, the drone fades into silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 verse 1 中间有个空行把「A black hole spinning, pulling all inside, / The world breaks down, nowhere to hide.」这一对押韵句拆开了，已合并成一组，文字不变。","原稿的 [instrument] 是第二遍副歌前的间奏，现在写成 8 小节具体内容；末尾的 [drop] 是尾奏前的重击，已写明。"]},{"id":"023","slug":"stars-in-the-mirror","title":"Stars in the mirror","titleNote":"","album":"《尽头》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1362-1420","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"90","length":"about 4:00","style":"Cosmic dream-pop with glitchy electronica at 90 BPM in B-flat minor, sung in English. A female vocalist sings airy and floating, close to the microphone, soft and spoken-like in the verses, then bright, wide and shimmering in the chorus with layered harmonies that echo like reflections. Glassy bell-like synth plucks, a warm sub bass and a soft rolling kick carry the verses, tiny glitch fragments sparkle like falling shards, and the chorus adds a wide supersaw pad, a shimmering arpeggio and crisp hi-hats. Mystical, bittersweet mood of an eternal mirror at the edge of the cosmos cracking into endless stars. Ends on a single bell tone fading into reverb. Vocal-forward, spacious, glittering mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, heavy distortion, metal, country, acoustic folk, screaming, trap hi-hats, comedy","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, glassy bell-like synth pluck over a deep pad, tiny glitch shards sparkle between notes, a soft sub bass enters on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | airy floating female voice, close-mic, bell plucks and sub bass only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nAt the edge of the cosmic deep,\nAn eternal mirror begins to weep.\nClear and transparent, it reflects all light,\nI see myself, and I see your sight.\n\nInside my soul, the mirror cracks,\nShattering into endless quarks that lack.\nIt will never reunite,\nI forget it all, I cease to fight.\n\n[Chorus | bright wide shimmering voice, harmonies echo like reflections, supersaw pad and arpeggio enter, crisp hi-hats, line endings held]\nStars in the mirror,\nFlicker, spin, they shimmer.\nThey circle round and round,\nIn loops, they travel, unbound.\n\nStars in the mirror,\nWith time and the universe,\nIn cycles they return,\nHere and there, they still burn.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the soft spoken-like voice, pad and bass, glitch shards more frequent, a little more tense]\nAt time’s beginning,\nI see a mirror, decaying, spinning.\nAll things sway, about to fall,\nYou and I, caught in it all.\n\nAt the speed of light’s end,\nI see a mirror, with nothing to mend.\nQuanta rise and fall within,\nDark matter fades, and time grows thin.\n\nThis is the final farewell,\nOur ending’s toll, the last knell.\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little brighter, harmonies thicker, same melody]\nStars in the mirror,\nFlicker, spin, they shimmer.\nThey circle round and round,\nIn loops, they travel, unbound.\n\nStars in the mirror,\nWith time and the universe,\nIn cycles they return,\nHere and there, they still burn.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, a sound of glass shattering, the whole mix is filtered then drops to one beat of full silence, then the full beat and pad slam back in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and glowing, stacked harmonies, glitch shards everywhere, same melody as the first chorus]\nStars in the mirror,\nFlicker, spin, they shimmer.\nThey circle round and round,\nIn loops, they travel, unbound.\n\nStars in the mirror,\nWith time and the universe,\nIn cycles they return,\nHere and there, they still burn.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, beat and pad fall away, bell pluck plays the intro motif alone, one last bell tone fades into reverb, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿的 [Drop] 为空、紧跟一个 Chorus；现写成\"镜面碎裂的玻璃音 + 一拍静默\"，最后一遍副歌标为 Final Chorus。","副歌四行叠句（Flicker, spin, they shimmer）句子短，靠逗号和空行换气，不必加 [Silence]。"]},{"id":"024","slug":"carbon","title":"碳元素","titleNote":"","album":"《尽头》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1423-1466","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"112","length":"about 3:30","style":"Clean electro-pop with laboratory textures at 112 BPM in E minor, sung in English. A female vocalist sings cool, crisp and precise in the verses, almost spoken like a scientist reading data, then bright, wide and sustained in the chorus with airy breathy ad-libs between the lines. A pulsing analog bass, a tight electronic kick, crisp glass-like hi-hats and a bright arpeggio carry the verses, tiny test-tube clink samples sparkle between phrases, and the chorus adds a wide supersaw pad, a punchy clap and layered vocal harmonies. Curious, awed mood about carbon, the element in every leaf, every diamond and every breath. Ends on keyboard clicks fading out one by one. Polished, clear, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, heavy distortion, metal, country, acoustic folk, screaming, rap verses, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, white noise builds in a laboratory, crisp test tube clinks, a bright arpeggio and a pulsing bass enter on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | cool crisp female voice, almost spoken, bass and kick only, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nUnder the microscope, hexagonal arrays,\nDiamonds and graphite share the same DNA,\nDeep sea vents erupt with blackened blood,\nDiatoms weave the nets of photosynthesis, they flood.\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice softens and lifts, hi-hats open, a synth riser builds for two bars, a small breath at the end]\nYou hide in every leaf's vein,\nIn the moment methane bubbles rise again.\n\n[Chorus | bright wide sustained voice, supersaw pad and clap enter, the parenthesized words are airy breathy ad-libs sung just after each line]\nCarbon, breath of the tropical trees,\n(Whooo—)\nSighs escaping from industrial chimneys,\n(Inhales—)\nYou form the equations of everything we see,\n(C-O-H-N)\nThe sum and difference of life's chemistry.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the cool crisp voice, bass and kick, glass hi-hats, a little warmer]\nOil pipes flow with the liquid dusk,\nCoal stacks rise as ancient tombstones' trust,\nNanotube mazes consume electric flow,\nGraphene flickers like stars in screens that glow.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, a fragile close voice over pad only, drums pause, a small riser at the end]\nWhen glaciers melt, releasing you from time,\nThe atmosphere reorders fate's design.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the mix is filtered and swells, one beat of full silence, then the full beat and pad slam back in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and bright, stacked harmonies, full beat, the parenthesized words are breathy ad-libs sung just after each line, same melody as the first chorus]\nCarbon, the wager of oxygen and flame,\n(Burn—)\nTime capsules locked in the ocean's name,\n(Sink—)\nYou write civilization’s carbonless diary,\n(4.6 billion years)\nThe green Earth’s chemical codex we carry.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, beat and pad fall away, the bright arpeggio plays alone, gradually fading keyboard clicks one by one, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 Intro 和 Outro 括号里的两句是制作说明（实验室白噪声/键盘点击），括号会被唱出来，已改成方括号里的英文演出指示，文字不再出现在歌词里。","「(Whooo—) (Inhales—) (C-O-H-N) (Burn—) (Sink—) (4.6 billion years)」是句间的顺序应答，保持独立成行；其中 (Inhales—) 会被唱成 \"inhales\"，若不想要，用歌词精修删掉。"]},{"id":"025","slug":"chuanshuo","title":"传说","titleNote":"","album":"《龙之说》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1472-1546","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"96","length":"about 4:10","style":"Epic Chinese-style rock with electronic edges at 96 BPM in D minor, sung and rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist sings with a warm, clear, slightly husky tenor in the verses and chorus, holding long notes at line ends, and rhythmically raps the middle verse in a low, steady, confident flow. A guzheng arpeggio, a soft erhu line and a deep sub bass carry the verses, punchy live drums and crunchy electric guitars join in the chorus, and the chorus opens with strings, a distant choir and a bright dizi flute. Mythic, adventurous mood of chasing an old legend through golden light, deserts and rivers, loneliness turning into an inexhaustible song. Ends on the guzheng alone with a long ringing note. Polished, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, piano ballad, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune, country","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a guzheng arpeggio alone, a soft erhu line joins on bar five, a deep sub bass swells, golden wind texture, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, warm husky male tenor, close-mic, guzheng and sub bass only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n一点金色光，\n耀灰暗梦境一角，\n它来自何方，\n为何万般玄妙，\n万年传说轮回流转，\n于黯淡中映照波澜。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same voice, erhu answers after each line, soft kick enters]\n古老岩洞中，\n吹来亘古的风，\n看旧日幻影匆匆，\n记挫折峥嵘无穷，\n走一段新程，\n推开一扇新门。\n\n[Bridge | voice lifts, drums enter with a steady beat, dizi flute holds a long note, a breath at every line end]\n淘尽沙土，\n于焦灼烈焰上漫步，\n挽一捧沙砾，\n双眼迷离中见亲故，\n血泪延伸千万里，\n纵然迷途，\n亦有明路。\n\n[Chorus | wide clear voice, long held line endings, crunchy guitars and strings enter, choir behind, dizi flute soars above]\n追一场梦境，\n寻一段传说，\n揽无尽银河入心，\n缤纷光华伴我，\n跨越黄土与江河，\n踏遍原野或荒漠，\n思绪是心内不竭的歌。\n\n[Verse 2 | rapped in a low steady confident flow, kick and snare with a sparse guzheng pluck, a short breath after every line, five-element words land hard on the beat]\n金断神，\n木锁灵，\n水葬魂，\n火焚身，\n土埋骨，\n五行聚合，\n通向起源或终焉，\n阴阳阻隔，\n看我抬手遮苍天，\n渡过千万年，\n无数夜未眠，\n梦中见群仙，\n寻觅的路上太多无言，\n只身向前，\n如光如电，\n终是通向这终章的诗篇。\n\n[Bridge | back to singing, voice calm and lonely, drums thin out, erhu and guzheng only, a breath at every line end]\n一路上总有孤独，\n这是一本古书，\n与激情纵情共舞，\n写一首悠扬的乐谱，\n岁月即便会干枯，\n却永恒留心深处。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings and drums swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then the full band lands together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and bright, choir and strings at full, dizi flute soaring, same melody as the first chorus]\n追一场梦境，\n寻一段传说，\n揽无尽银河入心，\n缤纷光华伴我，\n跨越黄土与江河，\n踏遍原野或荒漠，\n思绪是心内不竭的歌。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and strings fall away, guzheng plays the intro arpeggio alone, one long ringing note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 [verse2,rap] 的\"，rap\"写法不规范，改成 Verse 2 + 段内演出指示（rapped, breath after every line）；五行句「金断神 木锁灵 水葬魂 火焚身 土埋骨」每句 3 字，节拍落在重音上。","第一段 12 行拆成 3 个小节；「亦」「纵然」等书面语读音容易偏，必要时用歌词精修。"]},{"id":"026","slug":"compass","title":"Compass","titleNote":"","album":"《龙之说》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1551-1608","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"104","length":"about 4:00","style":"Dark ritual rock with cinematic Eastern flavor at 104 BPM in A minor, sung in English. A male baritone sings low, solemn and prophetic in the verses, almost chanted, then wide, ancient and fierce in the chorus with a deep choir doubling the key lines. Deep ritual toms, a growling bass and a bowed erhu-like string carry the verses, crunchy detuned guitars and big reverb drums join in the chorus, and low brass swells and distant temple bells hang in the air. Solemn, dangerous mood of a dragon's compass leading souls through five elements toward an immortal curse. Ends on a single temple bell and a fading drone. Dark, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, upbeat pop, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, acoustic folk, country, comedy, rap verses, autotune","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a distant temple bell, deep ritual toms start slowly, a bowed erhu-like string wails, a low drone swells, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, low solemn baritone, almost chanted, toms and bowed string only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nThe compass guides the way,\nStars fall from skies today.\nThis is the dragon's will,\nA prayer that's ancient, deep, and still.\n\nThe needle leads us on,\nLight will chase away the dawn.\nA massive skeleton reborn,\nFlesh and bone will be restored.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same voice, growling bass enters, tension climbing, low brass swells]\nFlying through the universe,\nFalling in the ocean's curse,\nAll is silent, still below,\nAll life bows down, in shadow's glow.\n\n[Break | band stops, one beat of silence, singer breathes in]\n\n[Chorus | wide ancient fierce voice, detuned guitars and big reverb drums enter, deep choir doubles the first line of each pair, the parenthesized laugh is a low dark chuckle]\nGold blocks divine thought,\nWood locks the spirit, tightly caught.\nWater buries the soul,\nFire burns the body whole.\nEarth hides the bones below,\n(Ha ha...)\nThe curse of immortality echoes,\nThe eternal flame forever grows.\nThis is your end, your fate,\nThis is where you meet your gate.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the low chanting voice, toms and string, bass underneath, darker and more intimate]\nThe compass is the hope to live,\nIt steals each soul, it will give.\nThe unknown legacy calls,\nBut with a price, it’s not small.\n\nCircles sharp with edges wide,\nPiercing clouds, piercing pride.\nEndless rivers twist and wind,\nSands and stones in depths combined.\nPray, rest, let go,\nThe whirlpool takes all, you know.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the bell rings once and everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then full band and choir slam in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and fierce, choir at full, drums and guitars at full power, same melody as the first chorus, the parenthesized laugh is a low dark chuckle]\nGold blocks divine thought,\nWood locks the spirit, tightly caught.\nWater buries the soul,\nFire burns the body whole.\nEarth hides the bones below,\n(Ha ha...)\nThe curse of immortality echoes,\nThe eternal flame forever grows.\nThis is your end, your fate,\nThis is where you meet your gate.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, one final huge hit with a long reverb tail, everything stops except the drone, vocals rest]\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, toms and guitars gone, bowed string and low drone only, one temple bell, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿末尾有两个 [Drop]：第一个后面带副歌，第二个是空的；现在合并成\"副歌前重击\"和\"最终重击 + 尾奏\"，副歌文字三遍完全一致。","「(Ha ha...)」是句间的顺序笑声，保持独立成行，标签里注明是低沉的笑。"]},{"id":"027","slug":"yunxing","title":"陨星","titleNote":"","album":"《星陨田野》","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1617-1687","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"68","length":"about 4:10","style":"Ethereal cosmic post-rock and dream pop at 68 BPM in F-sharp minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female voice sings airy, weightless and tender, close to the microphone and almost whispered in the verses, then rising into a vast, glowing and sustained chorus where the single dash words are held long. A clean guitar with long shimmering delay and a soft felt piano carry the verses, a deep warm pad and slow brushed drums enter in the bridge, and the chorus adds a swelling string section, tremolo guitars, big reverb drums and layered ghostly harmonies. Lonely, awed mood of a star falling like a single tear through the sky and a feather freed from reality. Ends on the guitar delay fading into stars. Spacious, vocal-forward mix with deep reverb.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, screaming, comedy, upbeat pop, Cantonese","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, clean guitar with long shimmering delay, a soft felt piano joins on bar five, a deep pad breathes underneath, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | airy weightless female voice, almost whispered, guitar delay and piano only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n星，\n是流浪在天际的一滴海，\n尘埃与它相融，虚无荡漾着无形的风，\n它看不见浊世的阴霾，\n亦不知凡尘的苦痛，\n推着不可见的幽灵，裹挟几朵衰变的花，\n拨动高维的琴音，捧起旋转流动的沙。\n\n[Bridge | voice a little stronger, slow brushed drums and a deep pad enter, each line floats and drifts, a long breath between lines]\n从眼中至心内，\n自天南去地北，\n划过天幕，漠看人间是与非，\n它不知自己是谁，\n不知众生意欲何为，\n永远飘流，像一滴热泪。\n\n[Chorus | vast glowing voice, the single dash words are held long and then dropped into silence for a beat, strings swell, tremolo guitars and big reverb drums enter, ghostly harmonies]\n星——\n接着陨落，\n心——\n燃烧着烈火，\n漩涡中融为一体，\n将思绪推演至极，\n终焉后静待天启，\n那道门不再关闭。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the airy whispered voice, guitar delay and piano, a little more fragile, a feather drifting]\n我，\n是挣脱真实的一片羽毛，\n记忆不曾留下痕迹，时光未曾将我揭秘，\n脚下的海在心底波澜涛涛，\n弥补遗憾与纯真的裂隙，\n渐行渐远的魅影，再无法重现的回音，\n迷雾笼罩至天明，或许得到一丝安宁。\n\n[Bridge | voice a little stronger, brushed drums and deep pad, drifting, slightly darker than before]\n从眼中至心内，\n自天南去地北，\n路过炼狱，漠看红尘是与非，\n我不知自己是谁，\n不知诸神意欲何为，\n永远坠落，是天生原罪。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little brighter, strings thicker, the dash words held long]\n星——\n接着陨落，\n心——\n燃烧着烈火，\n漩涡中融为一体，\n将思绪推演至极，\n终焉后静待天启，\n那道门不再关闭。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings and drums swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then the whole band and strings land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | the new words, strongest version, voice wide and glowing, held dash words, full band and strings at the peak]\n情——\n无意酝酿，\n命——\n辉煌后悲凉，\n既定的运数破碎，\n烟火让世间沉醉，\n智者又自觉假寐，\n万般存在将成灰。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and strings fall away, guitar delay plays the intro motif alone and fades into the stars, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["「星——」「心——」「情——」「命——」的破折号是长音符，保留在行尾，并在副歌标签里写明 \"hold the dash words long\"，这是文字层面最可靠的延长音方式。","最后一遍副歌的歌词与前两遍不同（情/命版本），已标为 Final Chorus。"]},{"id":"028","slug":"existence","title":"Existence","titleNote":"","album":"《星陨田野》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1692-1748","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"100","length":"about 4:30","style":"Cosmic indie-electronic rock with glitchy textures at 100 BPM in D minor, sung in English. A male tenor sings thoughtful and slightly haunted, close to the microphone and half-spoken in the verses, then open, aching and sustained in the chorus with layered harmonies. A pulsing analog bass, a tight programmed kick, a clean chorus-drenched guitar and tiny glitch fragments carry the verses, and the chorus adds big reverb drums, a wide synth pad, a bright lead guitar and a rising choir of voices. Philosophical, vast mood of a being born from the void, flipping a coin with fate and asking who he is in the universe. Ends on a single coin-toss sound and the pad fading. Polished, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, rap, country, acoustic folk, screaming, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, heavy metal","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, glitchy pulses over a deep pad, a clean chorus-drenched guitar line, the bass and kick enter on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, thoughtful half-spoken male voice, bass and kick only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nFrom the void, I am born,\nFrom annihilation, I am drawn,\nTime reverses in my trail,\nWormholes bloom and never fail.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same voice, guitar line enters, glitch fragments sparkle]\nGamma rays with my heartbeat start to fade,\nBy the tide, the black hole's frayed,\nWho pressed mute from a higher plane?\nWho gazes back at the galaxy's old lane?\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, voice softer, almost a whisper, the last line is sung slowly with a pause before it]\nRiding on a meteor's flight,\nLanded on a ring in misty light,\nDeep blue and pale red fill my sight,\nA single teardrop lands where soil is tight.\n\n[Chorus | part 1 of 2, voice opens wide and aching, big reverb drums and wide pad enter, line endings held long]\nLet all things in silence descend,\nLet the end bring me to the abyss's end,\nI exist in the non-existent scene,\nFrom the non-existent, I exist again.\n\n[Chorus | part 2 of 2, bright lead guitar answers, choir rises behind the lead]\nIn the quiet, probability's song is rife,\nCreation's first light gathers in my inner life,\nI'm the shortest frame, infinitely taken apart,\nI'm the endless loop that never will depart.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 3, back to the half-spoken voice, bass and kick, ruins and yellow dust, bleak]\nEverywhere I see, everywhere I go,\nOnly ruins and yellow dust blow,\nThe structure of the brain decays,\nNeurons shatter in a haze.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 3, voice detached, a coin-flip sound effect before the third line, glitch fragments increase]\nConsciousness is peeling from my frame,\nCasually, I flip a coin for the game,\nGuess which side will show its face this time,\nI watch myself close up, a process so sublime.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 3 of 3, voice rising, drums fuller, building toward the bridge, the last lines are sung with more air]\nBlood flows back to the womb, to my first home,\nWas it chance or was my fate set in the gloam?\nWhat on earth am I to believe in, or to roam?\nSo Let the shooting star reply for me,\nIt takes me back to my childhood memory,\nBack to that innocent and bewildered age, you see.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down to bass, kick and the whispered voice, each question hangs in the air for a beat, then pad swells]\nTo be or not to be,\nTo listen or to flee,\nDeep in memory's art,\nWho is waiting from the start?\n\nHear my final words professed,\nForget the first smile I expressed,\nObsession has now dispersed,\nWho am I, in this universe?\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything is filtered then cuts to one beat of full silence, then the full band and pad slam in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice broken open on the high notes, choir at full, drums and lead guitar at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\nLet all things in silence descend,\nLet the end bring me to the abyss's end,\nI exist in the non-existent scene,\nFrom the non-existent, I exist again.\n\nIn the quiet, probability's song is rife,\nCreation's first light gathers in my inner life,\nI'm the shortest frame, infinitely taken apart,\nI'm the endless loop that never will depart.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitar fall away, the pad holds one chord, a single coin-toss sound, the pad fades to silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿几乎没有句尾标点且 verse 2 有一行把两句连在一起（「…for me It takes me back…」），已拆行并补逗号，文字未变；两个长 verse 分别拆为 3 个小节。","[Drop] [Chorus] 写在同一行的原稿，已拆成静默一拍的 Drop 和最终副歌两个独立标签行。"]},{"id":"029","slug":"story","title":"story","titleNote":"","album":"《传奇故事》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1814-1907","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"112","length":"about 4:30","style":"Alternative country-folk with a deadpan storytelling vocal at 112 BPM in G major, sung in English. A male singer tells the story in a dry, deadpan, slightly sardonic baritone in the verses, then sings the chorus lively and open, with a loose, slightly drunken-sounding backing group answering each line. A twangy fingerpicked acoustic guitar, a simple walking bass and a shuffling drum beat carry the verses, a lonesome harmonica plays short mournful phrases between lines, and the chorus adds a bright banjo, a weeping slide guitar and an upbeat country two-step groove. Absurd, comic and bittersweet mood of a story that cannot exist but happens all the time. Ends on one rousing final chord and a long wailing harmonica note. Warm, natural, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, metal, rap, autotune, opera, synth pads","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a lone twangy acoustic guitar riff, a lonesome harmonica plays a short mournful melody, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, deadpan storytelling baritone, acoustic guitar and walking bass only, shuffling drums, a breath after every line]\nThis is a story that cannot exist,\nBut it happens all the time, you get the gist.\nA pigeon landed on a lamppost high,\nA horse that's eating oats was standing by.\nA gram, a kilo of some blueberry goo,\nEaten by monkeys in the lava stew.\nWhen will the homework finally be done?\nDepends how many plates break one by one.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same dry voice, harmonica answers after every second line]\nThose classic quotes and moments you hold dear,\nWith weathered cameras, they thank us with a tear.\nThen David takes the compass hand with a grin,\nAnd leads an army of jelly to rush in.\nThe Himalayan snow begins to wail,\n'Cause they love jogging on the morning trail.\nDon't worry, brother, you'll be safe and sound,\nThe emo songs will keep the demons down.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, still deadpan, a tiny build in the bass]\nYour axe will strike on crystals you can't see,\nAntarctic folks love this strange comedy.\nBut still they have to pay a higher fee,\nAnd war is peace for all eternity,\nIts silent scream echoes for you and me.\n\n[Chorus | full band, lively upbeat country two-step, bright banjo and weeping slide guitar, parenthesized lines are answered by a loose slightly drunken backing group]\nThis is an absurd story to be told,\n(The sun is beating up the moon so cold)\nThis is a bizarre story, brave and bold,\n(I've gone and lost my head, or so I'm told)\nThis is a creepy story, getting old,\n(He cannot find his eyes, brave and bold)\nThis is a legendary story spun of gold,\n(May Omega bless you, as I'm told)\nThis is a sacred story, I've been told,\n(The elders set the lightning to unfold)\nThis is a sorry story, left unsold,\n(It was a tale that never got told)\nThis is a magic story to unfold,\n(Who says it isn't, brave and bold?)\nThis is a mournful story, bleak and cold,\n(Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-yeah)\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 3, back to the sparse deadpan feel, harmonica weaves in and out]\nThe cancer's purified by morning light,\nThe dollar bills are a kitten's sweet delight.\nSo you should check the publishing date with care,\nAnd wait for magazines to fill the air.\nIs it a monthly, or a weekly read?\nA yearly journal for our daily need?\nOh no, perhaps you'll read it every day,\nA happy invisible man stole it away.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 3, same dry voice, a little more frantic, drums slightly busier]\nOh no, no, no, no, no, it can't be true,\nThe priest can't stop him, what's a man to do?\nLet's start the guilt-trip skill and lock him down,\nOh no, no, no, no, no, just leave this town.\nLet's eat the movies, watch the snacks instead,\nThe upside-down dollar's messing with my head.\nSo listen to my order, don't be slow,\nOne, two, three, action! Time to start the show.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 3 of 3, deadpan again, quiet bass, harmonica on the last line]\nThat foreign text is making my head sore,\nThe soccer field just stole my water store.\nThe hiking shoes are closing in on me,\nI'll bring a black hole made of TNT.\nMaybe I'm a cigarette, it's true,\nJust sitting here and burning my own butt for you.\n\n[Bridge | very slow and sparse, a few simple chords on acoustic guitar, one long mournful slide guitar note, voice soft and sincere]\nA story with no final page,\nA song that's sung on every stage.\nHow long until the curtains fall?\nPerhaps there's no real end at all.\n\n[Drop | 4 bars, instrumental, banjo and harmonica lead the upbeat two-step with full band, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | full band at full energy, same melody as the first chorus, parenthesized lines answered by the drunken backing group]\nThis is an absurd story to be told,\n(The sun is beating up the moon so cold)\nThis is a bizarre story, brave and bold,\n(I've gone and lost my head, or so I'm told)\nThis is a creepy story, getting old,\n(He cannot find his eyes, brave and bold)\nThis is a legendary story spun of gold,\n(May Omega bless you, as I'm told)\nThis is a sacred story, I've been told,\n(The elders set the lightning to unfold)\nThis is a sorry story, left unsold,\n(It was a tale that never got told)\nThis is a magic story to unfold,\n(Who says it isn't, brave and bold?)\nThis is a mournful story, bleak and cold,\n(Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-yeah)\n\n[Outro | final rousing chord from the full band, then only the lonesome harmonica holds one long wailing note, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词本身写得不错（吉他+口琴+班卓+滑音吉他+微醺的和声），已保留意图，改成「段落 | 指示」格式并压到 50 词以内；原稿里的 \"(dududu...)\" 之类括号描述若留在歌词里会被唱出来，不再使用。","两个 verse 各 21/22 行，已拆为 3 个小节；副歌里 16 行的一问一答「（…）」括号行保持独立成行（顺序应答），并在标签里写明是微醺的和声团应答。","歌词量较大，标签压得很短以控制在 5000 字符以内（实际字数见本文件抬头的计数）。"]},{"id":"030","slug":"omega","title":"Omega","titleNote":"","album":"《传奇故事》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 1911-2047","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"124","length":"about 4:30","style":"Motorik indie post-punk with new-wave synths at 124 BPM in E minor, sung in English. A male vocalist delivers a detached, deadpan monotone in the verses, half-spoken with dry wit, then becomes anthemic and increasingly frantic in the chorus, ending in unhinged shouts. A driving melodic bassline, a tight drum machine beat and a clean shimmering guitar with heavy delay carry the verses, short synth bleeps and percussive hits accent the rhythm, and the chorus adds open-chord guitars, a bright synth lead and gang vocals. Absurd, cosmic and hypnotic mood of a trickster god, five dollars and a crack in space and time. Ends with the bass and drum machine looping and then cutting out abruptly. Punchy, dry, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, country, ballad, orchestral strings, acoustic folk, opera, smooth jazz, trap hi-hats, lo-fi hiss","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a driving melodic bassline begins, a tight simple drum machine beat joins, a clean shimmering guitar melody with heavy delay enters on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, detached monotone male voice, bass and drum machine, short synth bleeps accent the rhythm, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nOmega.\nYeah, Omega.\n\nThrough the towers tall, it starts to roam,\nLike a ghost it lingers,\nIn everybody's dome,\nIt doesn't know just what it is today,\nCan't see the cold light from the sun's display,\nJust passes through the window pane,\nAnd turns into a lightning flash again.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same monotone, guitar delay louder, percussive hits more frequent]\nOmega.\nOh yeah, Omega.\n\nInside the ancient staff, you see,\nIt's endlessly destroying its identity,\nPlasma and forces electromagnetic,\nWeave a perfect wedding ring, ecstatic,\nFrom the past into the future bright,\nHiding softly in the present light,\nFollowing the leaves that fall and fly,\nDancing on the wave crests way up high.\n\n[Drop | 4 bars, instrumental only, the driving bass and drum machine continue, guitars turn distorted and chaotic in a brief intense burst of noise]\n\n[Chorus | powerful and anthemic, guitars play open chords, voice gains intensity, gang vocals double the first line]\nOmega, Omega, Omega,\nBless you, watch you, then forget ya,\nFive dollars, five dollars, five dollars,\nSpend it, save it, burn it like scholars,\n\nOmega!\nOh so divine!\nSeal the crack in space and time!\nOpen the ancient gate, let futures shine!\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the detached monotone, bleeps and hits return, bass drives]\nOmega.\nHaha, Omega.\n\nThe trickster god on an elephant arrives,\nNew York City's falling, losing all its lives,\nI don't know where the magic can be found,\nDon't know how poker's played on this ground,\nBut still my eyes just stare ahead, you see,\nInto the void's deepest mystery.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, same monotone, a little more urgent, the shouted name is sung loud once]\nOmega.\nHajime! Omega!\n\n\"Three\" evolves inside infinity,\nBecoming fireworks for eternity,\nImmortal breath is filling up the air,\nThe wise man's mask is broken, full of care,\nYou don't know who you are, it's plain to see,\nYou don't know what you're doing, just like me,\nJust walking toward the abyss, time and again,\nFalling down to hell with me, my friend.\n\n[Drop | 6 bars, instrumental only, another intense break, longer and more dissonant than the first, bass and drum machine keep driving]\n\n[Chorus | part 1 of 2, the music returns with power, voice anthemic, gang vocals double the first line]\nOmega, Omega, Omega,\nBless you, watch you, then forget ya,\nFive dollars, five dollars, five dollars,\nSpend it, save it, burn it like scholars,\n\nOmega!\nOh so divine!\nSeal the crack in space and time!\nOpen the ancient gate,\nlet futures shine!\n\n[Chorus | part 2 of 2, the voice becomes frantic and unhinged, the parenthesized lines are nonsense shouts and ad-libs, getting wilder every line]\n(Oh oh oh oh oh oh)\n(Na na na na na na)\n(Dee dee dee ba ba ba doo doo doo)\nOmega Omega Omega Omega Omega Omega,\n(Five dollars five dollars five dollars five dollars five dollars five dollars)\nGuard me, protect you, watch him, listen to her!\nDon't forget to poop and eat your breakfast, sir!\nCasually smash the fleet right off the map!\nDon't you dare invade the Earth, you sap!\nOh ah oh la la! (Oh oh oh woo hoo!)\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, a final chaotic section, the beat distorts or breaks down briefly then rebuilds, guitars and synths create maximum noise, vocals rest]\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, guitars and synths turn into feedback loops that slowly fade out, only the driving bassline and drum machine play on for a few more bars, then cut out abruptly, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿每一行之间都隔了空行（会让 Suno 每行都停顿，反而破坏节奏），已改成按语义 2-4 行一组；原稿里的 \"(dududu...)\" 描述只留在说明里，不再放进歌词。","第二遍副歌后半段是疯狂的叠喊（Oh oh oh / Na na na / Dee dee dee…），保持原样，括号行是顺序应答；标签要求\"越来越失控\"。","原稿的三个 [drop] 都写成具体的器乐爆发（噪音 → 更长更失谐 → 最终混乱），尾奏写明\"吉他反馈衰减，只剩贝斯和鼓机，然后突然切断\"。"]},{"id":"031","slug":"time-machine","title":"time machine","titleNote":"","album":"《档案》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2071-2115","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"100","length":"about 3:50","style":"Soaring sci-fi synth-rock at 100 BPM in G minor, sung in English. A female vocalist sings with a clear, powerful alto, restrained and slightly detached in the verses, then wide, urgent and sustained in the chorus with layered harmonies. A pulsing arpeggiated synth, a deep melodic bass and a crisp electronic and live drum mix carry the verses, a dark pulsing bass synth drives the middle instrumental, and the chorus adds crunchy electric guitars, a wide pad, big reverb drums and a rising choir. Awed and fateful mood of quantum bubbles, engines of fire, a tower of Babel and a final performance of fate. Ends on a long synth pad fading out. Polished, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, rap, country, acoustic folk, screaming, ballad, lo-fi, comedy, trap hi-hats","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a pulsing arpeggiated synth over a deep bass, a crisp electronic kick enters on bar five, a rising riser on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | restrained slightly detached female voice, arpeggio and bass only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\nQuantum entanglement in bubbles of chance,\nEndless oceans rise and fall, in a trance.\nColors of light shimmer behind the door,\nTime reverses, we’re bound to explore.\nMachines ignite, taking us back again,\nEngines of fire will burn the decay, then.\n\n[Chorus | wide urgent sustained voice, crunchy guitars and big reverb drums enter, layered harmonies in the last two lines, line endings held]\nIn the eternal, unchanged, we sigh,\nSinging through fleeting days that fly.\nThe cosmos falls silent in a blink,\nI believe this is our final link.\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, instrumental only, a dark pulsing bass synth leads over tight drums, guitars add sharp stabs, the arpeggio returns and a snare roll rises into the verse]\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the restrained voice, arpeggio and bass, drums tighter, more urgent]\nSmooth planes bend and distort in the dark,\nCurved engines sail through the cosmic arc.\nNewton’s faith and Hawking’s dream,\nDrift in the void, lost in the stream.\nWings of mutation lift us from hell,\nBabel’s tower shines, heaven’s swell.\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little brighter, harmonies thicker, same melody]\nIn the eternal, unchanged, we sigh,\nSinging through fleeting days that fly.\nThe cosmos falls silent in a blink,\nI believe this is our final link.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the whole mix is filtered and swells, one beat of full silence, then a huge synth and guitar hit with full drums, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | the new words, strongest version, voice wide and fateful, choir and guitars at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\nThe horn of doom is finally blown,\nEndless illusions fade, all alone.\nOverlapping waves, separating clear,\nThis is fate’s final performance here.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars fall away, the arpeggio plays alone, a long synth pad holds and fades out, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿结构里有 [Deep Instrument]、[Drop]、[Drop Chorus] 三个标签，其中两个是空的；现合并为：Deep Instrument → 明确 8 小节间奏；Drop → 一拍静默重击；Drop Chorus 与最后新词的 Chorus 合并为 Final Chorus（文字是 \"The horn of doom…\" 那一版）。"]},{"id":"032","slug":"new-century","title":"New Century","titleNote":"","album":"《新世纪人类》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2137-2170","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"Off","bpm":"116","length":"about 3:10","style":"Futuristic cinematic pop-rock anthem at 116 BPM in B-flat major, sung in English. A male tenor sings bright, hopeful and clear, steady and measured in the verses, then soaring and open-chested in the chorus with a choir of voices lifting the last line. A shimmering arpeggiated synth, a punchy bass and tight drums carry the verses, the chorus adds bright electric guitars, a wide orchestral string layer, big reverb drums and a soaring choir. Optimistic, awe-struck mood of white giant ships crossing the void, plasma beams, new materials and humanity's light reaching the stars. Ends on a rising synth and strings resolving to a bright major chord. Polished, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, rap, dark doom, screaming, country, acoustic folk, lo-fi, trap hi-hats, comedy","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a shimmering arpeggiated synth, deep space pad, a punchy bass and kick enter on bar five, a rising sweep on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | bright steady male tenor, arpeggio and bass, tight drums, one breath per line, on the beat]\nPlasma beams and AI's keen mind,\nSpace-folding tech, life's elixir to find.\nWhite giant ships, soaring in the void,\nUnknown materials, steps deployed.\nOn distant planets, saviors arise,\nLost travelers, guided by skies.\n\n[Chorus | soaring open-chested voice, bright guitars and wide strings enter, a choir lifts the last line, line endings held]\nLet light lead our way,\nFrom dawn's birth to twilight's sway.\nOne day, free will shall ignite the stars,\nHumanity's brilliance, shining afar.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the bright steady voice, bass and drums tight, strings begin to swell]\nIce beams and wands of magic might,\nContain angels, creatures from the night.\nHigh beings converse, doomsday's call,\nMercy's gaze melts in fiery thrall.\nRestless dreams shake the core,\nQuestions asked, answered once more.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings and synth swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then the whole band and choir land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice soaring on the high notes, choir and strings at full, same melody as the first chorus]\nLet light lead our way,\nFrom dawn's birth to twilight's sway.\nOne day, free will shall ignite the stars,\nHumanity's brilliance, shining afar.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums fall away, strings and synth rise and resolve to a bright major chord that rings out, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["歌词短（两段 6 行、副歌 4 行），Max Mode 可关；副歌文字三次一致。"]},{"id":"033","slug":"wanderer","title":"Wanderer","titleNote":"","album":"《新世纪人类》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2174-2215","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"92","length":"about 3:40","style":"Epic space rock ballad at 92 BPM in A minor, sung in English. A male baritone-tenor sings warm, weary and heartfelt, intimate and a little hoarse in the verses, then wide, aching and sustained in the chorus with layered harmonies. A clean chorus-drenched electric guitar, a soft piano and a deep melodic bass carry the verses, a slow engine-like rumble rolls underneath, and the chorus adds a wall of reverb guitars, big cinematic drums, a string orchestra and a soaring lead guitar. Nostalgic, bittersweet mood of an old spaceship and her wanderers adrift in the cosmic sea, hope and despair waltzing toward a distant shore. Ends on the guitar echo fading into an engine hum. Wide, cinematic, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, country, screaming, comedy, upbeat pop, lo-fi","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a clean chorus-drenched guitar echoing like a signal in space, a slow engine-like rumble, a soft piano joins on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | warm weary male voice, close-mic, guitar and piano only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat, memory-like and tender]\nSee, her armor aged and worn with pride,\nHear, her engines roar, a thunderous tide.\nEach start, a challenge to the stars above,\nEach stop, a push toward the hope we love.\n\nI still remember the tears she shed,\nI’ve seen her face when dreams were bred.\nMaybe all of this will one day fade,\nLet me, in this moment, have it all engraved.\n\n[Chorus | wide aching voice, long held line endings, wall of reverb guitars and big cinematic drums enter, strings swell, harmonies stack behind]\nWanderers adrift in the endless cosmic sea,\nStruggling in waves of ancient history.\nThe stars have fallen, dark matter devours,\nHope and despair dance in endless hours.\nTogether they waltz to a distant, unknown shore,\nWhere new dreams lie, and legends soar.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the warm weary voice, guitar and piano, bass and soft drums added, a little more fragile]\nSee, her memories wilt and fade away,\nHear, her whispers in the shadows sway.\nEach start, a step toward the final leap,\nEach stop, time falls back, memories we keep.\n\nI still remember the smile she wore,\nI’ve seen her dreams in the days of yore.\nMaybe all this will be remembered true,\nLet me, in this moment, fade out with you.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then the full band and orchestra land together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and broken open on the high notes, lead guitar soars, orchestra and drums at full, same melody as the first chorus]\nWanderers adrift in the endless cosmic sea,\nStruggling in waves of ancient history.\nThe stars have fallen, dark matter devours,\nHope and despair dance in endless hours.\nTogether they waltz to a distant, unknown shore,\nWhere new dreams lie, and legends soar.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and orchestra fall away, the guitar echo fades into the engine hum, last piano note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["歌词里 \"her\" 指一艘老飞船，副歌是宏大空间摇滚，因此 Style 用 space rock + 弦乐，并在 Verse 标签里写明 \"memory-like\"。"]},{"id":"034","slug":"no-regrets","title":"No regrets","titleNote":"","album":"《新世纪人类》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2218-2259","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"88","length":"about 3:40","style":"Heartland arena rock ballad at 88 BPM in D major, sung in English. A male vocalist sings with a rough, honest, resilient tenor, steady and proud in the verses, then wide, defiant and sustained in the chorus with a crowd of backing voices. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar and a warm piano carry the verses, a steady bass and live drums join in the second half, and the chorus adds big open electric guitars, a Hammond organ, a string layer and gang vocals. Proud, unbowed, clear-eyed mood of a man looking back on a rugged life, free of regret and shame. Ends on a final ringing chord and the crowd fading. Warm, wide, vocal-forward live-band mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, screaming, comedy, lo-fi, synth pop, autotune","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, fingerpicked acoustic guitar alone, a warm piano answers on bar five, soft room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | rough honest male tenor, close-mic, guitar and piano only, a breath between each line, slightly behind the beat, proud and steady]\nIn my life, no regrets, no shame,\nIn my life, none can judge or name,\nIn my life, rugged paths and strife,\nIn my life, twisted, strong in life.\nNever bowed or gave in to plea,\nStruggle’s my creed, my decree.\nThrough storms and trials, my heart stays pure,\nHeaven and earth, my reign’s secure.\n\n[Chorus | wide defiant sustained voice, big open guitars and Hammond organ enter, strings swell, a crowd of backing voices joins on the last two lines]\nMy life’s without regret or blame,\nBefore heavens and gods, I remain the same.\nMy heart’s as clear as a crystal mirror,\nMy will is strong, nothing can deter.\nWhen I look back, all I see is light,\nNo shadows linger, just pure sight.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the rough honest voice, guitar and piano, steady bass and soft drums added, a little more reflective]\nIn my life, a mix of shame and glory,\nIn my life, I wake from the blurry story,\nIn my life, in death’s grip, I roar and wail,\nIn my life, hope and despair set sail.\nA heart forever burning bright,\nA belief that marches through the night.\nSo many memories, so many gone,\nMy heart stays calm, my reign goes on.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the band swells and cuts to one beat of full silence, then everything lands together with the crowd voices, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and defiant, crowd voices loud, organ and guitars at full, same melody as the first chorus]\nMy life’s without regret or blame,\nBefore heavens and gods, I remain the same.\nMy heart’s as clear as a crystal mirror,\nMy will is strong, nothing can deter.\nWhen I look back, all I see is light,\nNo shadows linger, just pure sight.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and organ fall away, acoustic guitar plays the intro motif alone, one last ringing chord, crowd fades, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["Verse 里 \"In my life\" 四连句是排比，节奏容易被压成一口气，已在每个分句后留逗号并要求 \"a breath between each In my life\"。"]},{"id":"035","slug":"look-out-the-window","title":"look out the window","titleNote":"","album":"《新世纪人类》","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2346-2408","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"120","length":"about 4:10","style":"Aggressive industrial alt-rock with nu-metal weight at 120 BPM in E minor, sung in English. A male vocalist sings with a cold, sneering, half-spoken voice in the verses, then roars and shouts the chorus with raw, sustained high notes and layered gang vocals. Down-tuned chugging guitars, a heavy bass, tight punchy drums and mechanical industrial percussion carry the verses, a screaming lead guitar plays solos between sections, a dark glitching synth drone hangs underneath, and the chorus adds wide distorted chords and crash cymbals. Furious, dystopian mood of factory smoke, a sleeping world behind a window and a stuck clock frozen in place. Ends on a broken clock tick and feedback. Punchy, dark, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, jazz, autotune","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a factory machine rumble, mechanical industrial percussion starts, a down-tuned guitar riff builds, full drums crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, cold sneering half-spoken male voice, guitar chug and bass, mechanical percussion, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nLook outside, the factory's thick smoke spreads wide,\nHear the giant machines, their deafening cry,\nThe Earth trembles in the roar, passing by,\nBut inside the window, we still sleep, just doze by,\nBreathing black smog, tasting nuclear waste we defy,\nYour lungs, your heart, all stained by the dark dye,\nI'll tear your liver, your eyes, for the doomsday to nigh.\n\n[Instrumental Break | 4 bars, drums and bass hammer a heavy mechanical groove, the guitar chug drops out, a dark glitching synth rises, vocals rest]\n\n[Guitar Solo | 8 bars, a screaming lead guitar with heavy bends over the full band, ends on a held note that drops into the verse, vocals rest]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, back to the cold sneering voice, the band tight, more desperate]\nListen now, children's screams fill the air,\nTheir brains smeared on rainbows, beyond repair,\nRubbles submerge the milk, a mother's despair,\nBut I can't hear, don't understand, don't even care,\nI am inside the window, I'm not out there!\n(Ah!)\n\n[Chorus | roaring sustained voice, wide distorted chords, gang vocals shout the second half of each line, crash cymbals, the parenthesized shout is a single shouted answer]\nLook outside the window, what do you truly see?\nLook inside the window, what's left for me?\nOutside, a today that's fake, a false reality,\nInside, a tomorrow twisted, struggling to be free,\nHow much more blood can I still bleed?\nHow many more tears can I retrieve?\nReach out your hand, close the window, indeed,\n(No!)\nPull back your hand, open the window, accede.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 3, back to the cold half-spoken voice, drums tight, a living-dead street crawling, darker]\nLook now, the streets filled with living dead,\nThey have no thoughts inside their head,\nDevouring everything you once had, it is said,\nBut I can't eat, can't lick, oh how I crave instead!\nOpen your skull, let your mind be fed,\nSuck on the internet's tumor, widely spread!\nSleep within a quantum computer's bed!\n\n[Guitar Solo | 8 bars, a second lead guitar solo, faster and more frantic than the first, over a heavy groove, vocals rest]\n\n[Instrumental Break | 4 bars, drums beat a heavy mechanical pattern, a clock ticking sound layered on top, bass drone, vocals rest]\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 3, voice colder and more bitter, the clock tick stays in the background]\nListen now, the clock goes tick-tock-tock,\nHaha, actually it's broken, what a shock,\nWhy do you still trust the hourglass's lock?\nBut I shake it, invert it, clean it, on the block,\nIt just won't move!\n(Won't move!)\nAh!\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence with only the broken clock tick, then the full band slams in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice roaring at full power, gang vocals loud, same melody as the first chorus, the parenthesized shout is a single shouted answer]\nLook outside the window, what do you truly see?\nLook inside the window, what's left for me?\nOutside, a today that's fake, a false reality,\nInside, a tomorrow twisted, struggling to be free,\nHow much more blood can I still bleed?\nHow many more tears can I retrieve?\nReach out your hand, close the window, indeed,\n(No!)\nPull back your hand, open the window, accede.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars end on a final chord, feedback rings, a broken clock ticks and stops, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 verse 里的 [instrument] [guitar solo] [instrument beating] 是插在主歌中间的器乐，已拆成\"主歌上半 → 具体间奏 → 吉他独奏 → 主歌下半\"，并写明每段内容和长度，避免被缩成两拍。","「(Ah!)」「(No!)」「(Won't move!)」是句间的顺序喊叫，保持独立成行。含暴力意象，按原稿保留。"]},{"id":"036","slug":"liexi","title":"裂隙","titleNote":"原稿无标题（只有一条分隔线），取自首段歌词「万物之间都有裂隙」，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"（无专辑 / 第一份歌词末尾）","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2412-2456","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"64","length":"about 3:50","style":"Gentle cinematic chamber pop with a luminous folk warmth at 64 BPM in D major, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female voice sings soft and clear, intimate and airy in the verses, then open, tender and sustained in the chorus with a faint warm harmony floating above. A gentle felt piano and a slow expressive violin carry the whole song, the violin rises into a bright singing line in the drop section, a soft cello pad adds warmth underneath, and the arrangement floats in a soothing, unhurried pulse. Hopeful, spiritual mood of light entering through every crack, a heart that is fire, a long road ending in quiet autumn. Ends on the violin fading over a single piano note. Warm, spacious, vocal-forward mix with natural reverb.","exclude":"drums, drum machine, percussion, kick, snare, hi-hats, electric guitar, distortion, rap, EDM drop, Cantonese, English vocals, male lead vocal","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a gentle felt piano alone, a slow expressive violin joins on bar five, soothing floating rhythm from the piano only, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, soft clear female voice, close-mic, piano and violin only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat, bracketed words are faint whispered echoes]\n很久很久以前，他们告诉我，\n万物之间都有裂隙，\n那是光照进来的地方。（如此耀眼）\n\n很久很久之后，我在未来回首，\n却发现这是一道低语，\n如城堡堆在沙滩上。（一戳就破）\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same voice, warmer, cello pad enters softly]\n或许会有一天，有人对我说，\n你的心就是火，\n让寂静不再沉默。（永不闪躲）\n\n[Chorus | open tender sustained voice, line endings held, violin sings above, piano chords wider, a faint warm harmony floats on the last two lines]\n忘掉所有悲剧，\n我眼中只剩奇迹。\n世间万物与我共聚，\n伴我铭刻诗句。\n记起所有震撼，\n天地不再昏暗。\n远处灯火阑珊，\n只待一缕清风吹散。\n\n[Verse 2 | piano and cello with the violin answering, voice soft and wistful, a gentle seasonal turn from autumn rain to spring]\n在花开花落之后，\n长路终会到达尽头，\n再抬眸，不过一场离别秋。\n\n少年不复少年日，\n正是萧瑟夜雨时，\n难言重逢有否，流年不止。\n\n雪落雪融雪伴春，\n梅开枝头绿叶生。\n又是一年雷作鼓，\n莫道寻常莫要嗔。\n\n[Drop | 4 bars, the violin rises into a bright singing line, the female voice stays soft and luminous in the space, spiritual resonance, piano only underneath]\n\n[Final Chorus | the most open and luminous version, voice soft yet full, violin soaring, piano and cello pad wide, same melody as the first chorus]\n忘掉所有悲剧，\n我眼中只剩奇迹。\n世间万物与我共聚，\n伴我铭刻诗句。\n记起所有震撼，\n天地不再昏暗。\n远处灯火阑珊，\n只待一缕清风吹散。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, cello pad fades, violin plays the intro line once more, fades over a single piano note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 intro 和 Drop 的提示词里写了 \"no drum beats / there is no drum beat\"，否定词在 v6 容易被反向理解成\"要鼓\"，已全部改成正向描述（只有钢琴与小提琴、人声轻柔、小提琴上扬）。","行尾「（如此耀眼）（一戳就破）（永不闪躲）」是叠加在上一句尾的轻声回声，保持行内括号不变。","这首歌有明确的钢琴/小提琴器乐配置，没有鼓；Exclude 里放了 drums, drum machine, percussion 来锁定。"]},{"id":"037","slug":"this-man","title":"this man","titleNote":"","album":"（无专辑 / 第一份歌词末尾）","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 1 (歌词), lines 2460-2537","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"128","length":"about 5:00","style":"Cold new-wave and post-punk with a driving 1980s synth sheen at 128 BPM in A minor, sung in English. A deep baritone male voice sings detached and deadpan in the verses, like a distant narrator, then switches to shouting, questioning, wide and anthemic in the chorus. A driving melodic bassline carries the song, a mechanical drum machine beat and cold atmospheric synth pads sit underneath, layered 80s analog synthesizers undulate in the chorus, and a sharp chorus-pedal guitar adds angular stabs. Lonely, prophetic mood of a man on a mountain peak holding the sun's light for a blind valley that cannot see it. Ends with a synth solo, then the bassline slowly fading out alone. Punchy, cold, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, acoustic folk, country, ballad, orchestral strings, rap, opera, comedy, trap hi-hats","lyrics":"[Intro | 16 bars, long instrumental, cold atmospheric synth pads fade in, a driving melodic bassline enters on bar five, a mechanical drum beat joins on bar nine, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, deep baritone, detached and deadpan, bass and drum machine, pads underneath, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nYou stand upon the towering mountain's peak,\nFeeling the sun's radiant light you seek.\nYou wish to shine it down the valley's night,\nBut they are blind and hide from the light.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, steady rhythm, same detached voice, a little more urgent, one breath after each pair of lines]\nYou cry out loud,\nFearing they step into the deep abyss,\nBut they remain deaf in their ignorant bliss.\nFrom the eternal plateau you gaze and stare,\nYou dance and sing in frantic despair,\nBut under the clouds, only silence keeps.\nThis is an era of the blind and dark,\nThe lightning particles have yet to spark,\nBut how much longer can you wait and weep?\n\n[Chorus | layered 80s synthesizers with a moving undulating melody, the voice shifts to shouting and questioning, wide and anthemic, gang shouts on the word man]\nHey, this man, do you know what you're striving for?\nHey, this man, do you know where you stand anymore?\nThis man, what is it you intend to try?\nHey~ that man！stands above the clouds so high,\nYet to the world, he's just dust in the sky.\nHey~ that man！holds wisdom to save the night,\nWishing to bathe the whole world in his light.\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, a prominent bass riff and synths take over, drums driving, the guitar plays sharp stabs, vocals rest]\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, return to the detached deadpan baritone, bass and drum machine, pads quiet]\nYou stumble and fall, time and again,\nYour light staggers through the darkened domain.\nThe fireflies look like a ghostly flame,\nOr maybe the opposite, it's all the same.\nWhen will all of this finally end?\nWill a final verdict ever descend?\nWill we finally come to see and know?\nYou have no answer to the answer to show.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, building tension, synths climbing, snare tighter, the voice grows a little louder]\nIntertwined thoughts are easily let loose,\nThe empty hall holds only history's truth.\nIn your ignorance, the greatest wisdom is shown,\nIn your wisdom, ignorance is overthrown.\n\n[Bridge | part 1 of 2, stripped down to bass and drums only, voice close and urgent, a pause after the question mark]\nStill in doubt, still hesitate?\nYou urgently seek the answer, though you hold its weight.\n\n[Bridge | part 2 of 2, the synths swell, voice rising, drums driving, the last line is sung slowly and loud]\nYour greed brings destruction to the land,\nThe cycle of day and night rests in your hand.\nThe story of time shatters and fades away,\nKings and God have died today,\nWhose final masterpiece is on display?\n\n[Final Chorus | maximum new-wave energy, driving beat, layered 80s synthesizers at full, voice shouting and questioning at full power, same melody as the first chorus]\nHey, this man, do you know what you're striving for?\nHey, this man, do you know where you stand anymore?\nThis man, what is it you intend to try?\nHey~ that man ！stands above the clouds so high,\nYet to the world, he's just dust in the sky.\nHey~ that man ！holds wisdom to save the night,\nWishing to bathe the whole world in his light.\n\n[Solo | 8 bars, a synth solo with a bright sharp lead over the full band, vocals rest]\n\n[Outro | 12 bars, a post-punk instrumental ending, the synths and drums fall away, the bassline slowly fades out alone, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这首原稿的内部提示词已经很细（冷合成器垫底 → 旋律贝斯 → 机械鼓 → 80s 合成器 → 新浪潮高潮），保留思路，改成标准的「段落 | 指示」，并把嵌在歌词中间的 [Steady rhythm]、[Building tension]、[Synth swells] 拆成独立小节，避免被唱出来。","副歌「Hey~ that man！」里的 ~ 和 ！保持原样；这是长歌，约 5 分钟，Max Mode 建议开。"]},{"id":"038","slug":"xiyang-zhi-ge","title":"夕阳之歌","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 3-65","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"70","length":"about 4:30","style":"Melancholic Mandopop rock ballad at 70 BPM in E minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female alto sings in a worn, honest and slightly husky voice, close to the microphone in the verses, then opening into a wide, aching and sustained chorus with long held line endings. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar and a soft piano carry the verses, a low string pad and a warm bass enter in the second verse, and the chorus adds a live drum kit, strummed guitars, a cello line and layered backing harmonies. Lonely, theatrical mood of a performer wearing a mask under the spotlight, strings pulling her around like a puppet, silver hair at the window at dawn. Ends on the acoustic guitar alone with one long ringing note. Warm, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, male lead vocal, heavy distortion, comedy, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a fingerpicked acoustic guitar alone, a soft piano answers on bar five, faint stage-curtain room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, worn honest female voice, close-mic, guitar and piano only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n琴声渐淡，\n困于名为家的羁绊，\n暮退月光漫，\n如影的春色终涣散，\n心中波澜，\n激荡又刹那间虚幻，\n深藏的遗憾，\n成无人角落的轻叹。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same voice, string pad and warm bass enter, a little more strained and bitter]\n舞台上，\n麻木机械应唱，\n任由提线引我旋转，\n谁知我面具之下是怎样。\n\n[Chorus | wide aching sustained voice, drums and strummed guitars enter, cello answers each pair of lines, backing harmonies in the last two lines]\n一朝弦断眼中无光，\n卸下又披上伪装，\n心若烬灰只剩荒唐，\n寻不见我本相，\n银丝悄然透入窗，\n真心虚伪都不可计量，\n抱着吉他独坐至天亮。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the worn honest voice, guitar and piano with a light bass, looking back, fragile]\n回望来路，\n天真已不知落何处，\n疲惫的双目，\n徘徊在无声中倾诉，\n独自背负，\n受不属于我的错误，\n璀璨的谢幕，\n终是化作我的坟墓。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, voice rising, drums return softly, strings swell, ending with a hopeful line]\n再奔赴，\n忽听琴声回荡，\n总有风泪交织念想，\n但愿每次相见都是安详。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little stronger, same melody]\n一朝弦断眼中无光，\n卸下又披上伪装，\n心若烬灰只剩荒唐，\n寻不见我本相，\n银丝悄然透入窗，\n真心虚伪都不可计量，\n抱着那吉他独坐至天亮。\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, the extended words, voice breaking open, full band and strings, the spotlight spinning, a breath after each line]\n众目凝视的我心意乱，\n灵魂深处隐约有呼唤，\n再坠落，\n在没有我的彼岸，\n聚光灯下尽情旋转，\n表情任我来假扮，\n舞姿神态随意切换，\n忽视观众期盼，\n真正的我有千般，\n他人无法窥探的变幻，\n最终是，\n自己与自己相伴。\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, the chorus returns at full power, voice wide and aching, the very last line is split with a held beat of silence between its two halves]\n一朝弦断眼中无光，\n卸下又披上伪装，\n心若烬灰只剩荒唐，\n寻不见我本相，\n银丝悄然透入窗，\n真心虚伪都不可计量，\n抱着那，\n吉他独坐至天亮。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and strings fall away, the acoustic guitar plays the intro motif alone, one long ringing note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["最后一遍副歌共 3 段（副歌 → 12 行扩展 → 副歌再现），已拆成 Final Chorus part 1/2/3；末尾「抱着那 / 吉他独坐至天亮」是原稿刻意的断句，保留成两行，中间留一拍。","两个 verse 各 12 行、都是 4-9 字的短句，BPM 70 + 逗号换气足够，不需要 [Silence] 标签。"]},{"id":"039","slug":"xiashan","title":"下山","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 73-105","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"108","length":"about 3:40","style":"Chinese-style (guofeng) rock with a rapped-sung swagger at 108 BPM in D minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist sings with a free, carefree, slightly husky voice, relaxed and half-spoken in the verses, then wide, bold and sustained in the chorus with gang shouts behind him. A bamboo flute and a plucked pipa carry the verses over a deep bass and a steady live kick, the chorus adds crunchy electric guitars, taiko-style big drums, an erhu line and a crowd of shouting voices. Lonely, unbound swordsman mood of a god descending a mountain, wine in hand, moonlight and snow, laughing at the courts below. Ends on one pipa strum and a flute note fading out. Punchy, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune, country","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a bamboo flute alone over a cold wind, a plucked pipa joins on bar five, taiko-style drums enter on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | relaxed half-spoken male voice, flute and pipa with a deep bass, steady kick, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat, bracketed words are shouted ad-libs on the same line]\n回头不见来时的路，\n冷风凛冽仿佛在对我哭诉，\n不经意想起的一幕一幕，\n早已被写进了书（嘿 哈哈）\n谁见我踏空破迷雾，\n随意一指一点皆力压万古，\n最后斩尽心魔，无奈轻笑，曾经心酸处。\n\n[Chorus | wide bold sustained voice, crunchy guitars and big taiko drums enter, erhu line answers, gang vocals shout the second half of each line]\n我一人一剑天下浪，一招一式逍遥荡，\n无影残刃雪茫茫，浊酒纳悲凉，\n望天边故友旧日乡，一轮明月伴身旁，\n俯看高台空朝堂，听人间喧嚷。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the relaxed half-spoken voice, flute and pipa, bass and kick, bracketed words are shouted ad-libs on the same line]\n不管体术或是神通，\n只要我出手便是贯穿长虹，\n轮回万世不过眨眼成风，\n一醒诸世都消融（嘿 嗨嗨）\n过往的光辉与伤痛，\n命数归于终焉而物我两空，\n但是需要记住，下山的神，切莫要嘲弄（来）\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little louder, same melody]\n我一人一剑天下浪，一招一式逍遥荡，\n无影残刃雪茫茫，浊酒纳悲凉，\n望天边故友旧日乡，一轮明月伴身旁，\n俯看高台空朝堂，听人间喧嚷。\n\n[Spoken Word | drums stop, only flute and a cold wind, a calm old master recites the first line slowly and a young hesitant voice stumbles on the second and asks the question at the end]\n人法地，地法天，天法道，道法自然，\n師……師父什麼叫自然？\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then guitars, bass and taiko slam back in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice bold and wide, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus]\n我一人一剑天下浪，一招一式逍遥荡，\n无影残刃雪茫茫，浊酒纳悲凉，\n望天边故友旧日乡，一轮明月伴身旁，\n俯看高台空朝堂，听人间喧嚷。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars fall away, the pipa strums once, the flute holds one note and fades with the wind, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["bridge 的「（人法地，地法天，天法道，道法自然，師... 師父什麼叫自然？）」是整句念白（老者背诵 + 弟子发问），括号会让它变成叠唱，已去掉括号并放进 [Spoken Word] 小节，写明\"老者沉稳念诵，小孩声迟疑发问\"；文字（含繁体）一字未改。","「（嘿 哈哈）」「（嘿 嗨嗨）」「（来）」是叠加在行尾的叫喊，保持行内括号。","副歌 4 行每行两半，原稿中间是空格，改成逗号做呼吸点。"]},{"id":"040","slug":"qiansixi","title":"牵丝戏","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 113-163","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"72","length":"about 4:40","style":"Elegant Chinese-style (guofeng) pop ballad at 72 BPM in A minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female voice sings delicate, silvery and emotional, with a slow shimmer of vibrato at the ends of phrases, soft and breathy in the verses and opening into a luminous, sustained chorus with layered harmonies. A plucked guzheng and a soft pipa carry the verses over a warm pad, an erhu line sings between phrases, a gentle kick and a deep bass enter in the chorus, and a string section and a distant choir swell around the vocal. Wistful, romantic and cosmic mood of stealing fire from the afterlife, starlight, falling galaxies and a love song that echoes forever. Ends on the guzheng alone with a long shimmering note. Spacious, polished, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, male lead vocal, screaming, comedy","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a plucked guzheng alone, a soft pipa answers on bar three, a warm pad breathes in on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, delicate breathy female voice, guzheng and pad only, one breath per line, slightly behind the beat]\n散光的眼看向你，\n光团就这样凝聚，\n若星云倾覆，\n银河落下一场雨，\n已不知思念向哪去。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same voice, pipa joins, erhu answers after every second line]\n星辰在拙劣模仿，\n你那闪动的眸光，\n大海同样卑劣，\n借鉴它们的浩荡，\n可其实，皆不过虚妄。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice lifts and glows, erhu holds a long note, a soft kick begins, one breath between lines]\n圣洁绽放的光，\n洗涤尘世污会，\n抚慰我心驱散了伤悲，\n炽热充盈人间，\n我紧随足迹独追，\n无所谓身后谁与谁。\n\n[Chorus | luminous sustained voice, strings and a distant choir swell, deep bass and gentle kick steady, line endings held long]\n窃一束轮回后的火，\n终焉相逢，话语半柔懦，\n天地借由你的瞳色，\n染漫天暗淡星座，\n刹那与永恒，终得你允诺。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the delicate voice, guzheng and pad, a little more tender, slow and still]\n你心火温热流淌，\n润泽干涸与荒芜，\n融化了冰山，\n众神心伤再哭诉，\n待回首，不见来时路。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, same voice, pipa and erhu, the last line fades to a whisper]\n无穷概率之间，\n不可达的领域，\n唱一首独自啜泣的曲，\n枯萎的夕阳在，\n望霞光追你而去，\n无需诺言亦不语。\n\n[Chorus | the new words, voice wide and bright, strings and choir at full, deep bass steady, line endings held long]\n若是思念存在能量，\n创世之声，将不息回荡，\n再多说一句情话吧，\n是否会凋零成殇，\n任星海坠落，\n再伴你身旁。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, strings and choir swell and cut to one beat of full silence, then the full ensemble lands together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice luminous and aching, stacked harmonies, full ensemble, same melody as the previous chorus]\n若是思念存在能量，\n创世之声，将不息回荡，\n再多说一句情话吧，\n是否会凋零成殇，\n任星海坠落，\n再伴你身旁。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, strings and choir fall away, guzheng plays the intro motif alone, one long shimmering note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿没有任何结构标签，只有按空行分的 8 个小段；我按歌词内容推断为：Verse 1（1-2 段）→ Pre-Chorus（3 段）→ Chorus（4 段，高潮句「终得你允诺」）→ Verse 2（5-6 段）→ Chorus（7 段）→ Final Chorus（8 段，与第 7 段完全相同）。不对就改标签，文字不用动。","行中的空格（如「可其实 皆不过虚妄」）改成逗号做呼吸点；这是慢歌，BPM 72，不需要 [Silence]。"]},{"id":"041","slug":"xiwu","title":"习武","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 167-232","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"98","length":"about 3:50","style":"Aggressive kung-fu cinematic Chinese hip-hop with rock edges at 98 BPM in E minor, rapped and shouted in Mandarin Chinese. A male rapper delivers a cocky, rhythmic, controlled flow in the verses with sharp breaths between phrases, then shouts the chorus with raw, sustained fighting spirit and gang vocals behind him. Booming 808 bass, punchy live drums, taiko hits, a sharp erhu stab and a plucked guzheng riff carry the verses, with martial-arts mouth sounds between the move names, and the chorus adds crunchy guitars, deep war drums and crowd shouts. Arrogant, fierce prodigy mood of a boy who mastered martial arts at three and now commands the heavens. Ends on a gong hit and silence. Punchy, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, lo-fi, comedy, smooth jazz, autotune, country","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a gong hit, deep taiko hits, a plucked guzheng riff, an 808 enters on bar five, a drum fill on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, cocky rhythmic rapped voice, 808 and kick with a guzheng riff, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n我三岁习武，\n五岁天下无敌，惹得世人嫉妒，\n他们说我实在实在离谱，\n不停嘀咕的闲言碎语密布，\n\n看我一个凌空飞步，把你打吐，\n再接上孤雁穿云渡，让你知道我的路数，\n我的思路是你达不到的高度，\n堵住你的全部招数，让你陷入迷途。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, the move names are shouted on the beat, the parenthesized lines are sharp martial-arts mouth sounds that come just before each shout]\n（突突突）\n大荒囚天指！\n（噗噗噗）\n抬手灭天日！\n（嘟嘟嘟）\n降龙十八式！\n（窣窣窣）\n悔恨已迟迟！\n\n[Chorus | shouted raw sustained voice, crunchy guitars and deep war drums enter, gang vocals double every line, the bracketed shout is a crowd roar on the same line]\n习武之人！血性如怒！\n拳风过境！万敌臣服！\n猛虎出山！天地为鼓！\n一招定局！败者埋土！（啊！）\n\n筋骨为刃！傲气为炉！\n生死看淡！狂名刻骨！\n若你不服！黄泉引渡！\n命数我主！以杀证武！\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the cocky controlled rap, 808 and kick, guzheng riff, a clear breath after every line]\n天才就该自负，\n走我自己的路，\n凡夫俗子过于糊涂，\n能力不足却从不肯服输，\n\n我擒龙伏虎妖魔成奴，\n无敌之心苍天眷顾，\n看不得世间疾苦，\n于是长啸一声诸天震怒。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, the move names are shouted on the beat, the parenthesized lines are sharp martial-arts mouth sounds that come just before each shout]\n（突突突）\n太阳玄气掌！\n（噗噗噗）\n一剑镇八荒！\n（嘟嘟嘟）\n擎天定汪洋！\n（窣窣窣）\n万古夜茫茫！\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then 808, taiko and guitars slam in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice shouted at full power, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus, the bracketed shout is a crowd roar on the same line]\n习武之人！血性如怒！\n拳风过境！万敌臣服！\n猛虎出山！天地为鼓！\n一招定局！败者埋土！（啊！）\n\n筋骨为刃！傲气为炉！\n生死看淡！狂名刻骨！\n若你不服！黄泉引渡！\n命数我主！以杀证武！\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and guitars stop, the guzheng riff plays alone for two bars, a final gong hit, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这首最容易抢拍的是 verse 的 16 字长句，已按语义加逗号并成对分行；「（突突突）大荒囚天指！」是\"音效在前、招式喊在后\"的顺序结构，保持独立成行。","副歌里「（啊！）」是叠加的怒吼，已并入上一行行尾。","「降龙十八式」「黄泉引渡」等词读音稳定；若「降」读成 jiàng，用歌词精修只换那一个字。"]},{"id":"042","slug":"zhidaoma","title":"知道吗","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 236-280","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"100","length":"about 3:30","style":"Brash Chinese hip-hop with pop-punk guitars at 100 BPM in G minor, rapped and sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist raps with a cocky, bratty, rhythmic flow in the verses, then shouts and sings the chorus with an arrogant swagger and a crowd of gang vocals. A bouncing bass, punchy live drums with a snappy snare and a gritty detuned guitar loop carry the verses, a siren-like synth stab accents the beat, and the chorus adds crunchy power chords, handclaps and stadium shouts. Cocky, defiant mood of a self-declared strongest man crushing every rival like a police officer chasing a wanted criminal. Ends on a siren and one power chord. Punchy, bright, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, lo-fi, orchestral strings, smooth jazz, autotune, country","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a siren-like synth stab, a gritty detuned guitar loop, bouncing bass enters on bar three, drums crash in on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | cocky bratty rapped voice, bass and drums tight, guitar loop, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n每当我徘徊在十字路口，岁月终究不停留，\n清风卷起满天风尘，不变的是那道伤痕，\n说到底仍旧只有我一个人，再次尘封了自己的心门，\n即使天空压住我的头，我也大声回应no no no，\n每当你陪伴我左右，有谁会再度回首，\n或许到了说再见的时候。\n\n[Chorus | arrogant shouted sung voice, crunchy power chords and handclaps enter, gang vocals double the title line, the parenthesized shout is a single crowd yell between lines]\n知道吗，你看见了吗，\n我就是全世界最帅的帅逼，\n被我击败你只能哭着回去找妈妈，\n我坚韧不倒无可匹敌，\n（wa ao！）\n知道吗，认清现实了吗，\n我是否让你惧怕，是否断绝你的牵挂，\n我是警察，你是通缉犯，等着我擒拿。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the bratty rapped flow, bass and drums tight, faster, half a beat of air after every phrase]\n大千世界纷纷扰扰多么喧嚣，\n蚊虫叽叽喳喳整天到晚还在叫嚣，\n碾压你们根本无需动脑，\n践踏你们人生逐句高超，\n\n强者都是孤独，只有野狗才会成群，\n放弃陈旧的路数，再努力也不过浮云，\n长江沧浪荡苍茫，长桨扬扬闯汪洋，\n香光煌煌漾廊堂，狂郎放嗓唱狼王！\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence with only a siren, then the full band slams in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, shouted at full power, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus, the parenthesized shout is a single crowd yell between lines]\n知道吗，你看见了吗，\n我就是全世界最帅的帅逼，\n被我击败你只能哭着回去找妈妈，\n我坚韧不倒无可匹敌，\n（wa ao！）\n知道吗，认清现实了吗，\n我是否让你惧怕，是否断绝你的牵挂，\n我是警察，你是通缉犯，等着我擒拿。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and bass stop, the siren wails alone, one last power chord, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["verse 2 末尾的绕口令「长江沧浪荡苍茫，长桨扬扬闯汪洋…」音节很密，已在标签里要求\"每个分句后半拍留白\"，并把 BPM 压在 100。","「（wa ao！）」是夹在句间的顺序喊叫，保持独立成行。含粗口/自夸词，按原稿保留。"]},{"id":"043","slug":"me","title":"ME","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 284-360","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"132","length":"about 4:00","style":"Furious alt-metal with hardcore shouts and a rapped-shouted verse delivery at 132 BPM in C minor, sung in English. A male vocalist spits the verses in a hoarse, gritty, half-spoken rage, then screams and sings the chorus with a ragged, sustained, tormented voice and gang vocals shouting the command words. Down-tuned chugging guitars, a pounding bass and heavy live drums carry the verses, a screaming lead guitar flares between lines, and the chorus adds wide distorted chords, crash cymbals and a wall of crowd shouts. Raw, unhinged mood of someone tearing open his own cold core and declaring himself the ruler of his own world. Ends on a final guitar chord with feedback. Punchy, aggressive, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, lo-fi, smooth jazz, comedy, autotune","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a down-tuned guitar riff builds over feedback, a pounding bass joins, heavy drums crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, hoarse gritty half-spoken male rage, guitar chug and bass, drums tight, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nWho am I, where do I stand?\nThis is the core question, the answer I demand,\nWhat am I saying, what am I doing?\nI don't know, I want to find out, pursuing,\nLook deep within my heart, tear open the cold core.\n(No!)\nWhy does lava pour?\nWho locked my soul in a cage?\nWho sealed my wounds on this stage?\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same voice but louder and angrier, drums double-time, every shout lands on the beat with half a beat of air after it]\nNever lose my freedom, never compromise!\nGo mad! Make the world fear! Make towers rise in fire!\nDestroy all prosperity, seize your flowers and trees!\nI declare myself the ruler! Drop your ignorance, your fixed beliefs,\nI will behead you!\nDo you hear?\n(Aaaahhhh!)\n\n[Chorus | part 1 of 2, screamed and sustained ragged voice, wide distorted chords, gang vocals shout the first word of each group, a half beat of silence after each shout]\nLook at me!\nIs my face twisted like a ghoul?\nAre my eyes evil like Satan's cruel?\nI howl at the sunset, ending old world's hope, so cool!\n\nAsk me!\nHow much more blood can I still spill?\nHow many more tears can I instill?\nRain veils the pain, I taste death's bitter thrill!\n\n[Chorus | part 2 of 2, same intensity, crash cymbals on every shout word, the voice cracks upward on the last lines]\nHear me!\nMy hoarse voice spews blood, a vivid scene!\nCrying in agony or laughing keen?!\nPiercing your eardrums, then reaching your brain's core, unseen!\n\nFace me!\nMy bones protrude, sharp and spiky, oh so grim!\nBursting and exploding down to every cell's whim!\nInvading your dreams, becoming your nightmare, grim!\n\n[Verse 2 | rapped-shouted again, guitar chug and bass, drums double-time, the bracketed words are crowd answers shouted just after the line]\nTake off the guitar strings, to strangle you tight,\nMy guitar's my sword, rebels all die in this fight!\nThe stars will shine for me, the gods will yield to my might!\nTime reverses, I detonate the universe, burning bright!\nTurn seas upside down, the Earth trembles in fright!\n(Waoo!! Aaahhh!!)\nThis is me, this is me,\n(It's me, it's me)\nDon't you fucking advance!\nWaaah, wayaya,\nAnd don't you surrender!\nOw!\nYou know me!\nAh!\nYou know... me!\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence with only feedback, then the full band slams in together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, strongest version, screamed at full power, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus]\nLook at me!\nIs my face twisted like a ghoul?\nAre my eyes evil like Satan's cruel?\nI howl at the sunset, ending old world's hope, so cool!\n\nAsk me!\nHow much more blood can I still spill?\nHow many more tears can I instill?\nRain veils the pain, I taste death's bitter thrill!\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, same full power, the final lines are screamed and held]\nHear me!\nMy hoarse voice spews blood, a vivid scene!\nCrying in agony or laughing keen?!\nPiercing your eardrums, then reaching your brain's core, unseen!\n\nFace me!\nMy bones protrude, sharp and spiky, oh so grim!\nBursting and exploding down to every cell's whim!\nInvading your dreams, becoming your nightmare, grim!\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums stop, one huge guitar chord rings out with feedback and fades, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["Verse 1 有 16 行、副歌有 16 行（四组 Look at me / Ask me / Hear me / Face me），都已拆成小节；「(No!)」「(Aaaahhhh!)」「(Waoo!! Aaahhh!!)」「(It's me, it's me)」是句间的喊叫与应答，保持独立成行。","含粗口（fucking），按原稿保留；若平台拒收，可在歌词精修里只换这一个词，其余不动。","每个副歌小组的第一句是单词喊叫（Look at me! 等），在标签里要求\"先喊，半拍后再进入主句\"，防止四组黏在一起。"]},{"id":"044","slug":"guitar-sword","title":"我的吉他是把剑","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 365-450","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"88","length":"about 5:00","style":"Chinese rap-rock with an acoustic-to-electric guitar duel at 88 BPM in E minor, rapped and sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist raps in an earnest, hoarse, flowing voice with unhurried phrasing and a clear breath between phrases, then sings the chorus open and sustained with long held line endings. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar and a deep bass carry the first verse, a steady live kick and snare join, and the chorus adds a bright lead electric guitar that cuts like a sword, strummed power chords, strings and layered backing harmonies. Lonely, passionate mood of a musician whose guitar is a holy sword, homesick for faraway towns, a band that fell apart, and tears on an empty shore. Ends on the acoustic guitar alone with one ringing note. Vocal-forward, natural live-band mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune, orchestral brass, country","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a fingerpicked acoustic guitar alone, a deep bass enters on bar five, a distant electric guitar harmonic rings once, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 4, earnest hoarse rapped voice, unhurried phrasing, acoustic guitar and bass only, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n我已经忘记，\n第一次看见吉他是何时侯，\n激情悄然荡起，\n疑似有难言启发撕扯心口，\n频频看向电视或书本上的海市蜃楼 [Silence]\n冥冥的指引领我独身入门开始承受 [Silence]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 4, same voice, soft kick and snare enter, the bracketed words are backing voices singing them together with the lead]\n这（炽烈的心）背对故乡长歌吟游，\n那（日夜在冥）思苦想的心愁，\n想治（世界的病）但无量的哀伤刻心头，\n渡了（死劫的命）不想又酿了新仇，\n是我天真的病，又或天生的命，\n不想此生如此落寞在人前人后 [Silence]\n只得大展身手琢磨再泛起轻舟 [Silence]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 4, voice a little stronger, the parenthesized single words are soft linking whispers sung after the previous line]\n（于是）\n乘着激流顶着长空一路向前漂流 [Silence]\n（然后）\n深刻祈求平和伤痛密布强掩萧愁 [Silence]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 4 of 4, voice rising, drums fuller, building toward the chorus]\n（可是）\n冷涩依旧印刻长虹几乎将天凋朽 [Silence]\n（只好）\n捧着期求尽可葬送疾苦江面遨游 [Silence]\n\n[Chorus | open sustained voice, lead electric guitar cuts in like a sword, power chords and strings, long held line endings, backing harmonies on the last two lines]\n它是一把圣剑，\n在湖边林间的坚石间浮现，\n挣脱了时间，刺穿梦魇，天赐在心间，\n致自己的誓言会实现，看挚友在身边，\n源自现实的视线显示世间的执念，\n直面起源失陷时限，\n饰演诗仙指天自勉，\n只见诗篇之巅唯我执剑自怜。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the earnest rapped voice, acoustic guitar and bass with a light kick, thinking of two singers, a little more weary]\n从beyond到朴树，\n或激昂或孤独，\n掌下琴弦承载太多情愫，\n仍在回想歌中对理想的追逐，\n寒夜飘雪的意象，处处诉出苦楚，\n那些离乡后的祝福，成了枯树旁的遗响，\n想家时心痕被琴声轻点，挣开败落的异象，\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, same voice, drums a little busier, the closing line is sung slowly with a held beat before it]\n清楚这音符凝固在异乡，可金钱埋没了夕阳，\n我那遗忘的篇章轻抚复苏的信念，\n从呆坐中引出在禁锢里迷茫的心弦，\n唱他来过的路途，唱他爱过的故土，\n拜托天一亮就带我于晴天等待伤疤不复。\n\n[Chorus | stronger and wider than the first, lead guitar higher, same melody as the first chorus]\n它是一把战剑，\n无边记忆无限回忆又从我眼前出现，\n吉他鸣起鼓点突现一起构出古典兵器，\n不顾及其他部件即便仅余琴弦，\n亦足以击垮狐奸提炼音律断片，\n看见笔下逐渐流动的词语和诗句，\n一把乐器幻显出连绵凌厉的荆棘，\n又不顾束缚地极限投入，湮灭叛变后迎敌。\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, instrumental only, the lead electric guitar plays a singing sword-like melody over the full band, the acoustic guitar answers, ends with a drum fill]\n\n[Verse 3 | earnest hoarse rapped voice again, band tight, a clear breath after every line, a little more bitter]\n同友组了乐队，开始练习技艺，\n以为铸就绝配，再次勉励自己，\n拥有出色列队，改词全力仔细，\n举杯不可夜归，还是愿意继续，\n\n歌曲每首力撼天际，自诩绝非来自奇迹，\n何以追求彼岸联系，此去借回来时士气，\n可惜没有不散宴席，此句绝对乃是至理，\n这里唯有孤单延续，只余血泪在此淤积。\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, the broken sword, voice wide and aching, full band, lead guitar screaming, long held line endings]\n重铸这把断剑，\n我看见它如晚间闪电展现蔓延，\n如战舰盘旋蜿蜒山原我难掩心中安全，\n南面半边蓝天完全被引动转眼我心动万千，\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, voice breaks open, the band at full power, the last line is sung slowly and held]\n与痛楚共舞着那荣辱叛变转变，关键是恶化在所难免，\n控诉自我重复的差错和那从不断连的贪念，\n难眠的夜又重抚着它吟诵万言，\n甘愿无尽数不清的残念重演闪现到眼前，\n可岸边空如山巅痛苦难辨唯有我泪流满面。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and bass fall away, the acoustic guitar plays the intro motif alone, one ringing note, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这是全集里最密的一首（每行 14-20 字的押韵连珠句）。处理：① Verse 1 拆成 4 个小节；② 每个半句后加逗号；③ 在最长的几行末尾用行内 [Silence] 代替逗号（行内 [Silence] 前不放标点，避免\"双重停顿反而加速\"）；④ BPM 压到 88，Style 写了 unhurried。","「（于是）（然后）（可是）（只好）」是衔接词的顺序轻声应答，保持独立成行；行内「这（炽烈的心）」这类括号是叠唱，保持原样。","「何时侯」疑似「何时候」的笔误，按原稿一字未改；若被读成 hóu，请用歌词精修处理。","原稿的 [drop] 为空，在这里写成\"吉他主奏的 8 小节间奏\"，与整首「吉他是剑」的主题一致。"]},{"id":"045","slug":"xingqiwu","title":"星期五","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 455-529","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"65","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"Off","bpm":"134","length":"about 3:00","style":"Hyper playful Chinese trap-pop with chiptune bounce at 134 BPM in F major, rapped and shouted in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist raps with a cheeky, bratty, fast-talking flow in the verses, then chants the chorus with a goofy, elastic, sing-song voice and a crowd of kids answering each line. A bouncy 808 bass, snappy claps, crisp hi-hats and a bright chiptune lead carry the verses, silly cartoon sound effects pop between lines, and the chorus adds stacked gang shouts and a catchy whistle hook. Mischievous, restless mood of a student counting down to Friday, snacks, games and mecha model kits. Ends on a cartoon boing and a laugh. Bright, punchy, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, orchestral strings, heavy metal, lo-fi, smooth jazz, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a bright chiptune lead and a bouncy 808, snappy claps enter on bar three, a cartoon boing on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, cheeky bratty fast-talking rap, 808 and claps only, a clear breath after every line, on the beat]\n我在学校，水土不服，\n到处是狗叫，他们蠢笨如猪，\n让我炮制这告示来搞事，\n去搞死要绕吐我的搞笑小兔，\n\n你最好祈祷祷告，而后我对你哀悼追悼，\n你老爹老娘哭嚎，像老鼠被捕鼠囚牢夹爆，\n没错寒窗苦读，可是不学无术，\n在守株待兔，见招拆招快速将你屠戮。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same bratty rap, hi-hats busier, the bracketed shout at the end is a crowd yell]\n逐渐偏离主题，慢慢分散注意，\n我是斜月三星菩提，猴子给我干着苦力，\n灵感咕力咕力，谁在莫西莫西，（哇嗷！）\n\n[Chorus | goofy elastic chanting voice, kids answer each line on the same line, stacked gang shouts, catchy whistle hook, claps on every beat]\n星期五星期五，（星期五星期五）\n星期星期期期五，（星期期期期期五）\n星期五星期五星期五，\n不要哭别说苦，\n我要撸我要撸，\n噗噗噗嘟嘟嘟，\n不能输别停住。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the cheeky rap, 808 and claps, a clear breath after every line, brisker]\n课代表别吵吵，班长都被我打跑，\n扫把吹不倒，傻逼真不少，\n烦人的组长开始徘徊把作业收，可是数量太少，\n坤坤硬了在鼓裆的昨夜这时候，梦里万家拜朝，\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, same rap, the bracketed words are a shouted ad-lib on the same line]\n周末到了我要吃辣条，我要拼高达（机甲赛高！）\n打开空调，拿出游戏机不用病假条！\n看恐怖电影，吓我一跳，\n回到最初的起跑线放鞭炮，\n别搞得我要吐要爆，脑里的暴力要再保持住，（呜呼！）\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little louder, same melody]\n星期五星期五，（星期五星期五）\n星期星期期期五，（星期期期期期五）\n星期五星期五星期五，\n不要哭别说苦，\n我要撸我要撸，\n噗噗噗嘟嘟嘟，\n不能输别停住。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence with only a cartoon boing, then the full beat slams back in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, strongest version, voice and kids shouting at full volume, whistle hook, same melody as the first chorus]\n星期五星期五，（星期五星期五）\n星期星期期期五，（星期期期期期五）\n星期五星期五星期五，\n不要哭别说苦，\n我要撸我要撸，\n噗噗噗嘟嘟嘟，\n不能输别停住。\n（唔咦咦啊！唔咦咦啊咦咦！）\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, the last words change, the voice goes happier and louder, the last line is held long]\n星期五星期五，（星期五星期五）\n星期星期期期五，（星期期期期期五）\n星期五星期五星期五，\n不辛苦要幸福，\n继续撸继续撸，\n噗噗噗嘟嘟嘟，\n挺住挺住要挺住！\n\n[Outro | 4 bars, the beat stops, the chiptune lead plays a short fanfare, a cartoon boing and a laugh, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["副歌里「（星期五星期五）」「（星期期期期期五）」是跟在同一句后的回声，已并入上一行行尾；verse 末尾的「（哇嗷！）」「（呜呼！）」也并入上一行。","「（唔咦咦啊！唔咦咦啊咦咦！）」是独立的一句怪叫，保持独立成行。含粗俗词，按原稿保留。","这是搞怪向的短歌，Max Mode 可关；若想更像喜剧，Weirdness 可调到 70。"]},{"id":"046","slug":"human-zoo","title":"Human Zoo","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 534-623","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"65","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"126","length":"about 4:10","style":"Dark carnival industrial rap-metal at 126 BPM in D minor, shouted and rapped in English. A male vocalist barks the verses in a hoarse, theatrical, sneering ringmaster voice, then shouts the chorus with a chanting crowd of gang vocals, spitting the final break like a speech. Heavy distorted guitar riffs, a thick bass, punchy live drums and a mechanical circus calliope loop carry the verses, DJ scratches and sirens cut between phrases, and the chorus adds wide distorted chords, crash cymbals and shouted crowd responses. Grotesque, satirical mood of a zoo where the humans are the beasts, with monkeys, a bald hippo and a squirrel in a cage. Ends on a giant door slam and a laugh. Punchy, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, country, smooth jazz, lo-fi, comedy pop, autotune, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a creepy circus calliope loop, a siren, a distorted riff builds, heavy drums crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, theatrical sneering ringmaster bark, riff and drums tight, a clear breath after every line, the parenthesized lines are crowd answers shouted after the previous line]\nThe monkey at the mirror, it starts to grimace and gnaw,\nMadly smashing the glass, defying every law.\nBehind it, more monkeys appear, a roaring, frenzied crew,\nThey scream and shout aloud, in this chaotic view.\n\nTheir furry bodies, teeth stained with fresh blood, bright,\nThey're butchering themselves, in this gruesome, horrid sight.\nSharp claws dig into wounds, a grotesque, morbid art,\nPulling out entire skeletons, to observe each bone and part!\n(Ah!)\n(Zoo!)\n(Human zoo!)\n(Welcome! Motherfker!)\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same bark, a deep guttural roar for the hippo, calliope louder, the parenthesized lines are crowd answers]\nThe hippo opens wide its mouth, a massive, guttural roar,\nGiant teeth corroded by its own drool, forevermore.\nUgly songs fill the pool, a disgusting, slimy brew,\nRound, plump balls of feces float, a truly sickening view.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, the voice breaks into a manic laugh, then the shouted joke lines land on the beat with the crowd answering]\nBut (hahahahaha)\nHippo!\n(It's bald!)\nIt's bald! It has no hair to show!\nIt's a baldy!\n(Woohoo!)\n(Human zoo!)\n(Motherfker!)\n(Welcome! F**k!)\n\n[Chorus | shouted chanting hook, wide distorted chords, gang vocals double the title line, crash cymbals, the parenthesized shout is a single crowd yell]\nThis is the human zoo, human zoo, human zoo,\nGrab your ticket tight, watch your comrades too.\nNever, ever dare to open up the cage,\nDon't stick your head towards the beasts, in this dark age.\nOr else you'll turn into their form, a dreadful, savage hue,\n(Guess who!)\nThis is the human zoo, human zoo, human zoo,\nDon't eat raw meat, eat more of the feed for you.\nOh, sorry, that wasn't meant for you to hear,\nBut...\n(Haha!)\nLet me give you a smack, then put a collar on your neck, my dear!\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the sneering ringmaster bark, riff and drums tight, a squirrel jumping, a little faster]\nThe squirrel leaps up and down, a frenetic, tiny sprite,\nClutching a pinecone, but it won't take a bite.\nIt rather fights the kangaroo for apples, green and red,\nIt jumps from table down to hell, then back to earth instead.\nIt's a clever little trickster, a mastermind so small,\nThe leaves are falling, rustling, answering nature's call.\nSo I pick up one leaf to taste, a curious, strange delight,\n(Waaaaoh!)\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, the voice turns accusing, the parenthesized words are crowd answers, getting more furious toward the end]\n(Human zoo!)\nWhat kind of animals are we now, in this absurd display?\nNo, not me, it is you! You're the beast, I say!\n(Human zoo!)\nPeel back your skin, your hidden truth to find,\nSegment your bones, leave nothing left behind.\nI've found the evidence, the beast within your soul!\nNo, no, no!\nYou are not welcome here, motherf**kers, you whole!\n\n[Drop | 4 bars, instrumental only, a DJ scratching over a heavy beat drop, sirens and the calliope loop, the guitar riff slams in on the last bar]\n\n[Chorus | strongest version, shouted at full power, gang vocals at full volume, same melody as the first chorus, the parenthesized shout is a single crowd yell]\nThis is the human zoo, human zoo, human zoo,\nGrab your ticket tight, watch your comrades too.\nNever, ever dare to open up the cage,\nDon't stick your head towards the beasts, in this dark age.\nOr else you'll turn into their form, a dreadful, savage hue,\n(Guess who!)\nThis is the human zoo, human zoo, human zoo,\nDon't eat raw meat, eat more of the feed for you.\nOh, sorry, that wasn't meant for you to hear,\nBut...\n(Haha!)\nLet me give you a smack, then put a collar on your neck, my dear!\n\n[Break | the drums stop, only a siren and the calliope, the voice speaks the lines like a ringmaster's speech, each shouted line followed by a crowd yell]\nHuman Zoo!\nMotherf**ker!! Welcome to the zoo!\nThis is your home!\nYou're our partner too!\nCome and slaughter with us!\nThis is the human zoo!\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, the full band crashes on a last chord, the calliope loop plays alone and slows down, a giant door slam and a laugh, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 [Instrument - Drop] [Drop] [DJ] 三个标签叠在一起，且其中两个是空的，已合并成一个具体的\"DJ 搓碟 + 重鼓点\"的 4 小节间奏。","开头的「(Ah!) (Zoo!) (Human zoo!) (Welcome! Motherfker!)」是人群顺序应答，保持独立成行；「But (hahahahaha)」行内括号保持。含粗口，按原稿一字未改。","结尾的 [Break] 是整首最疯的一段全员喊话，现在写成\"鼓停、只留念白+人群回应\"，再接尾奏。"]},{"id":"047","slug":"change-the-world","title":"改变世界","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 628-720","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"112","length":"about 4:10","style":"Angry Chinese rap-rock with nu-metal weight at 112 BPM in G minor, rapped and shouted in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist raps in a hoarse, furious, ragged voice in the first verse, switches to a humorous, cocky and inspiring flow in the second verse, and roars the chorus in an exciting shouted chant with a crowd answering. Down-tuned chugging guitars, a pounding bass and heavy drums carry the verses, a bursting bass drop with sharp high-frequency noise hits in the break, and the chorus adds wide distorted chords, crash cymbals and a huge crowd of gang vocals. Rebellious, theatrical mood of a boy raised on cartoon heroes who decides to change the world, with a warrior's roar and a joke. Ends on a final power chord and crowd cheer. Punchy, aggressive, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, country, lo-fi, smooth jazz, autotune, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a down-tuned guitar riff builds over a crowd murmur, a pounding bass joins, heavy drums crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, hoarse angry rapped voice, guitar chug and bass, drums tight, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n我还是个小屁孩时，\n喜欢看奥特曼和喜洋洋，\n我天马行空的想象力是一把利器，\n任凭现实摧残混淆，\n我的心如琉璃般清澈，\n我是正义的，我唾弃邪恶，\n我是光明，我憎恨黑暗，\n可是似乎世界和我想象中的不太一样，\n太多矛盾和奇怪的地方，\n我以为自己疯了，\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, the voice breaks into shouting, each swear and each short line is hit hard on the beat, drums double-time]\n我草！\n他妈的！\n为什么！折磨我！\n我胡言乱语，我慷慨激昂，\n我指鹿为马，我浑浑噩噩，\n我纸上谈兵，我盲人摸象，\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, the rage explodes into a warrior's battle cry, then the voice drops low and furious for the last lines]\n哇呀呀！！！！！！！！！\n燕人张飞在此！！！！！！！！！！！\n吃我一脚！！！！！！\n怒火中烧，要把你们打入地狱！\n尔等不配为人！\n都是错的！改变！\n改变！改变一切！\n\n[Chorus | exciting roar and talk, shouted chant, wide distorted chords, crash cymbals, in the lines with brackets the bracketed syllables are shouted by the crowd between the lead syllables]\n改变世界！\n（改变世界）\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n我深知我明晓我领悟我了解我预知我看到我感到这是必须要做的事情！\n不，这是必须发生的事情，\n我要改变世界！\n我们都要！\n改变！\n我也改变，你也改变！\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n会到来！会到来！\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, humorous but inspiring and arrogant rap, a cocky smirking flow, guitars palm-muted, a breath after every line]\n后来我偶尔在那块墙壁的灰色里看见那四个字，\n“改变世界！”！\n啊啊啊啊！\n那似乎是对我的某种暗示，\n我接受了它，之后海底捞门口，\n那玻璃上倒映的众生相似乎也在提醒我，\n哎哟我超，\n我嘞个豆，\n你知道吗，\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, the flow gets faster and prouder, the English words are spat clearly, the last lines are shouted]\n那上面写着众生的愿望和牵挂，\n人类VS老天爷！（你们知道吗？！）\n我的笔是枪，文字是子弹，\n笔记本电脑每一面都是我的战场，\nmotherfucker！\n欢迎来到我的地狱！\n但是！\n这座天堂将升起！\n世界经由我手！\n改变！\nchange！\n\n[Instrumental Break | 4 bars, instrumental only, a bass drop with sharp high-frequency noise bursting over the beat, a sudden stop on the last beat]\n\n[Bridge | the chant of a crowd with a single voice rising out of it, drums pause, bass pulses, the parenthesized words are long crowd wails after each phrase]\n（哇啊啊）\n比起成功的一生（啊啊啊）\n抗争的一生（啊啊啊啊啊）\n更伟大，\n（啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊啊）\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, exciting roar and talk at full power, the whole crowd answering, same melody as the first chorus, bracketed syllables are shouted by the crowd between the lead syllables]\n改变世界！\n（改变世界）\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n我深知我明晓我领悟我了解我预知我看到我感到这是必须要做的事情！\n不，这是必须发生的事情，\n我要改变世界！\n我们都要！\n改变！\n我也改变，你也改变！\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！\n会到来！会到来！\n\n[Outro | 4 bars, drums and guitars end on a final power chord, a crowd cheer rises and fades, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词很有想法（沙哑愤怒 rap / 激动咆哮 / 幽默又自大的 rap / 低频高频爆裂间奏），已保留意图，改成「段落 | 指示」。原稿 [Drop][instrument][drop-…] 三个叠在一起，合并为一个具体的 4 小节低音爆裂间奏，之后接的「（哇啊啊）比起成功的一生…」是有唱词的段落，标为 Bridge。","副歌「我（要）改（变）这（个）世（界）！」是领唱与人群逐字交错，括号字保持原样，标签里写明 \"bracketed syllables are shouted by the crowd between the lead syllables\"。","「！！！！！」连续感叹号和「motherfucker！」「我草！」按原稿保留。"]},{"id":"048","slug":"asylum","title":"asylum","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 731-791","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"70","influence":"60","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"96","length":"about 3:50","style":"Experimental avant-garde alt-rock with dark trip-hop pulses at 96 BPM in B minor, half-whispered and half-sung in English. A male vocalist delivers a broken, twitchy, half-whispered flow in the verses like a patient confiding in a corridor, then erupts into a frenzied melodic hook with screams and giggles in the chorus. A twisted, warped, bent-string distorted guitar, a rubbery sub bass and a stuttering broken drum loop carry the verses, creepy music-box and radio-static textures flicker in the gaps, and the chorus adds wide fuzz guitars, panicked shouts and echoing voices. Surreal, claustrophobic, darkly funny mood inside a white-tiled asylum, a dog-faced doctor and a blue door that cannot be touched. Ends on the music box slowing to a stop. Raw, eerie, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, orchestral strings, country, smooth jazz, polished pop, acoustic folk, comedy rap, autotune","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, twisted whispers, a bizarre bent and distorted guitar accompaniment, a creepy music box, radio static, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, broken flow, half-whispered and twitchy, warped guitar and rubbery bass, stuttering drums, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nCold porcelain tiles,\nA gleaming white floor.\nThe bathtub's ablaze,\nSoap swallowed to the core.\nThe doctor's a bull's head –\nMy apologies, I misread.\nActually, the doctor's a dog-faced man instead.\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same twitchy half-whisper, the parenthesized snore is a long slow whispered Z sound, the last line fades like waking up]\nThe angels spin and spin,\nDo their eyes need glasses to see within?\nThe ribbons twist and twine,\nAfterimages morph into a boat of design.\nSkull spider,\nCome take my picture, stride.\nDraw the curtains, I need to sleep now inside.\n(Zzzzzzz...)\nThe phone rings,\nFrom dreams I return, like a bird with wings.\nHell behind me, it fades and dies.\n\n[Chorus | frenzied melodic hook, fuzz guitars wide, panicked shouts and giggles between the lines, the voice goes from calm to unhinged, the parenthesized word is a sudden shout]\nI'm in the asylum, I'm not in the asylum.\nI'm outside the world,\nOr maybe on its apex?\nReality's a page,\nI pee on it, full of rage.\nThe Earth is a pond, I poop in it every day, beyond.\nThe universe, a cake,\nInto the microwave,\nI partake.\nI am a madman,\nI'm asking you, my friend. (Ah)\nAsk me!\n\n[Interlude | 4 bars, eerie bent guitar and music box, a lone ghostly voice sings the bracketed ad-lib in the middle]\n(Oh...)\n\n[Guitar Solo | 8 bars, a warped distorted guitar solo with wild bends over the broken drum loop, a giggling voice laughs the bracketed ad-lib at the end]\n(Hehehe Oh oh oh)\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, back to the twitchy half-whisper, bass and broken drums, the picture turns surreal and violent, the quoted words are spat out]\nEvery face's skin is torn,\nI see demons, from flesh and blood reborn.\nThey smile at me, a chilling sight,\n\"Screw you!\"\nI grab the steel pipe, swing with all my might!\nThe dark clouds in the sky, my pet dogs they remain,\nCoins in the bowl are eating bread, again and again.\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, the voice drifts and slurs like falling asleep, the music box returns, the final line is sung very slowly]\nI want to sleep, but the moon keeps me in endless loop,\nThe blue door, untouchable, in endless droop.\nCats walk on the roof tiles, light and free,\nThe moon overlaps, then scatters, for all to see.\nI am a blind man, who's lost his way.\n\n[Drop | 4 bars, instrumental only, a post-chorus burst, the stuttering drums slam in with fuzz guitars and a distorted music box]\n\n[Hook | frenzied melody and screams with a psychiatric episode, voice cracks and shouts, echoes and panicked breaths between lines]\nI'm in the asylum, I'm inside the world. You're not beside me,\nWhere are you, unfurled?\nI'm in the crevice, deep inside the other side of the Earth's crust, in dust.\nAwaiting my arrival,\nFearing my future's revival.\nDisaster will descend,\nMy eyes blink, and the story will re-begin.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, instrumental only, the guitar fades into static, the music box slows down and stops]\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词（Twisted whispers / Broken Flow, Half-whispered / Frenzied melody and screams + psychiatric episode）已保留意图并扩写；原稿里 [Instrumental] 和 [Guitar Solo] 后面紧跟的「(Oh...)」「(Hehehe Oh oh oh)」是器乐段里的耳语/笑声，已作为带说明的小节保留，括号照原样。","这首是故意怪的，Weirdness 70 / Style Influence 60；若崩坏过度，先把 Weirdness 降到 55。含粗鄙词，按原稿保留。"]},{"id":"049","slug":"talk-to-god","title":"Talk to God","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 798-930","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"108","length":"about 6:00","style":"Cosmic conversational rap-rock with a cinematic arena build at 108 BPM in A minor, sung and rapped in English. A male vocalist tells the story in a wry, wide-eyed, half-spoken voice in the verses, speeding into sarcastic rap in the second verse, then shouts the chorus with a questioning crowd of gang vocals answering every line. A glowing synth pad, a sparse piano and a deep bass carry the verses, tight drums and a bright clean guitar join in the second half, and the chorus adds wide distorted chords, a huge choir and crash cymbals. Surreal, funny and furious mood of a man who climbs an endless staircase, meets a bald old God with a halo, argues about the answer to every answer and falls into hell. Ends on the choir fading over the pad. Wide, cinematic, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, country, acoustic folk, smooth jazz, lo-fi, autotune, orchestral brass, trap hi-hats","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a rising synth staircase, soft choir pad, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | calm half-spoken male voice, pad and sparse piano, a breath after every line]\nThe world falls silent, a radiant light appears before me,\nAn endless staircase, rising boundlessly, is what I see,\nI know this must be some kind of divine decree,\nMy bare bones climb the steps, rushing towards eternity.\n\nMy flesh and blood behind me, melting, fading into air,\nMy very soul, I wonder where it's drifted, I don't care,\nHumanity's shifting scenes, on the left they flicker and gleam,\nFleeting dream-like bubbles, on the right, a shimmering dream.\n\nI feel myself suspended, weightless, just floating free,\nAs if the stairs beneath my feet were never meant for me,\nOr perhaps I've turned into a beam of light, pure and bright,\nDancing silently on a tranquil path, in the fading night.\n\nI cannot turn around, nor find a way back home, no guide,\nThis is my future, my destined end, where I'm meant to ride,\nThis is my tomorrow, the awakening that soon will be,\nSuddenly a figure at the end, I'm lost in stardust, mystically.\n\nI feel a comfort, a peace profound, no anger, no sorrow, no trace,\nTime stops still, no matter if there's being or just empty space,\nThat figure suddenly speaks, its voice cuts through the silent air,\n\"You are my child, you've finally returned, you're finally here.\"\n\nI said: \"Hey, old guy, tell me, who the hell are you?\"\nAnd then this old guy, he says he's God.\nWell...\nHaha...\n\n[Chorus | shouted hook, wide chords, gang voices, bracketed lines are crowd answers]\nTalk to God,\n(Listen to me)\nLet's really talk about what you did to me, and I did to you, you see,\n(Huh?)\nListening to God speak,\n(Why?)\nDevils are breaking free in my ears, they want to crawl from the abyss,\n(Oh?)\nDrawing for God,\n(Where?)\nAngels' eyes are blinded, Satan's mouth is sealed with a kiss,\n(Ha?)\nPraying to God,\n(What?)\nThe Tower of Babel crumbled, Eden burned down, pure misery,\n(Heh...?)\n\n[Verse 2 | fast sarcastic rap, bass, tight drums]\n\"Hey, tell me, why does this world hold so much war?\nWhy do I hurt? Why am I sad to my core?\nWhy don't they love me?\nWhy do I hate myself more and more?\"\nThen this old guy, he frowned, a clear sign of his disdain,\n\"Why do you have so many questions? You ask them all in vain.\nOh, but you're not seeking solace, or asking for my grace,\nI can see right through you; you're a hypocrite in this place.\nYour questions are hollow, your thoughts absurd and truly wild,\nYou should ask yourself these things, then answers might be reconciled.\"\nI scratch my head,\nStaring at that halo floating on his crown, I quipped,\n\"Yo, are you bald, or what?\nIf you're really that smart, that truly bright,\nOne puff from me could blow your toupee right out of sight!\"\n\n[Chorus | same as before, louder]\nTalk to God,\n(Listen to me)\nLet's really talk about what you did to me, and I did to you, you see,\n(Huh?)\nListening to God speak,\n(Why?)\nDevils are breaking free in my ears, they want to crawl from the abyss,\n(Oh?)\nDrawing for God,\n(Where?)\nAngels' eyes are blinded, Satan's mouth is sealed with a kiss,\n(Ha?)\nPraying to God,\n(What?)\nThe Tower of Babel crumbled, Eden burned down, pure misery,\n(Heh...?)\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, one beat of silence, then a huge sub bass hit]\n\n[Verse 3 | angry rapid rap, double-time drums]\nThen, this old guy, he finally lost his cool,\nHe didn't seem to like me, what a total fool,\nBut he was the one who brought me to this cosmic space,\nI swear, if I had a basketball here, in this cosmic space,\nHis halo's light would surely be the hoop!\n\"I have too many questions, but you won't reveal the truth!\"\nThe old guy shoves me away, through empty air, I fall.\n\"Some answers to answers are destined to have no answers at all.\"\nSo then I said,\n\"Then is that very statement an answer, from you instead?\nIf it's an answer, why does this no-answer-answer suddenly arise?\nIf it's not an answer, then why does an answer that implies,\nIt has an answer, still remain a no-answer-answer in your eyes?\"\nAnd then, I felt myself falling,\nF***!\nBeneath me...\nHow did it become hell?\n\n[Bridge | whispered, cold pad, slow kick]\nI witnessed the cycles of rebirth,\nI smelled the essence of new birth,\nI heard the echoes of annihilation's call,\nI tasted death, consuming all,\nColorless, formless, beyond all sight,\nThe id, the superego, in endless night.\n\n[Drop | one beat of silence, then the band slams in]\n\n[Chorus | strongest, same melody, choir at full]\nTalk to God,\n(Listen to me)\nLet's really talk about what you did to me, and I did to you, you see,\n(Huh?)\nListening to God speak,\n(Why?)\nDevils are breaking free in my ears, they want to crawl from the abyss,\n(Oh?)\nDrawing for God,\n(Where?)\nAngels' eyes are blinded, Satan's mouth is sealed with a kiss,\n(Ha?)\nPraying to God,\n(What?)\nThe Tower of Babel crumbled, Eden burned down, pure misery,\n(Heh...?)\n\n[Outro | choir fades over pad, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这是最长的一首（原稿 4200+ 字符，加上标签必须压在 5000 以内），所以这里的演出指示刻意写得最短；三遍副歌文字完全一致，第二、三遍的标签写成 \"same as before\"，省下字符。","副歌里「Talk to God / (Listen to me)」一问一答的括号行是顺序应答，保持独立成行；歌曲预计 6 分钟，生成前把 Duration 设为 Auto 或 6:00 以上，否则可能被截断。","若仍觉得 verse 1 太长被赶拍，可以用 v6 分段编辑把 Verse 1 拆成两段单独重做。含粗口（F***!），按原稿保留。"]},{"id":"050","slug":"living-legend","title":"活着的传奇","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 936-1056","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"94","length":"about 5:00","style":"Chinese rap showcase with trap, speedcore and melodic hooks at 94 BPM in F minor, rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male rapper delivers a sharp, confident, rhythmically intricate flow with clear breaths between phrases and tight internal rhymes, while a female singer takes the hooks, clear and cool with a slight vibrato, doubling the last words of each line. A heavy 808 bass, crisp hi-hat rolls and a dark piano loop carry the verses, the hooks add a wide pad and a melodic lead, and the instrumental sections break into a fast speedcore DJ trap beat with chopped vocal samples. Arrogant, brilliant mood of a rap machine crushing rivals with wordplay, palindromes and flawless rhyme. Ends on a chopped sample and a final 808 hit. Punchy, clear, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, orchestral strings, country, comedy, autotune, heavy metal","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a dark piano loop, a hi-hat roll starts, a heavy 808 enters on bar five, a chopped vocal sample on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Spoken Word | cocky confident spoken-rap, piano and 808, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n不瞒你说，\n跟这些人，那是话不投机半句多，\n肾虚的小子，身单力薄又不甘寂寞，\n意淫拉满，实战熄火的居多，\n\n唯有我，看万余座青山，又晨观碧波，\n把hater们打到身残体弱，迷糊到不分敌我，\n他们自食其果，难自圆其说，\n他们后院起火，死得其所，\n\n我富可敌国，verse干净利落，\n每个词精雕细琢，把对手逐个击破，\n按理说，我这段押韵不算利索，\n但为何他们依然东闪西躲。\n\n[Hook | Female Vocal, clear cool melodic voice, doubling the line endings, wide pad and a melodic lead enter, the 808 steady]\n灵感像舔狗缠着我，黏住我怎么都不松口，\n我的歌吸住全球人眼球，他们都争相研究，\n押韵像电流，而那箭头从你肩头流到咽喉，\n闻道有先后，我一个念头你们联手来献丑，\n我获取作弊秘籍，自动把汉字编码，\n无数认输的废逼们，被我再次践踏，\n或许你说这才两句，也配算是连押，\n我厚米相继列队，让你被干死全家。\n\n[Verse 1 | male rapper, sharp and fast but with clear breaths, 808 and hi-hat rolls, every second line ends with a short silence]\n这是特质的隔世的歌词 [Silence]\n可是惹事实在不合适，\n自以为是的小丑，不过是可笑的乐子 [Silence]\n让我立即起立，将他们一击击毙，\n我是说唱的机器，押韵的技艺太过离奇 [Silence]\n昔日的荣耀，深思到通宵，\n开天辟地，破碎失败者的童谣。\n\n[Chorus | Female Vocal, cool anthemic melody, wide pad, 808 and kick steady, each long line is sung in two halves with a breath in the middle]\n陪你整夜看街头的，霓虹闪烁不定，\n为你哽咽叹邂逅的，迷宫探索不停，\n回忆冷冽盼携手的，悸动散落无形，\n醉意生灭伴解愁的，迷踪穿梭孤影，\n退避更迭寒街头的，时空穿梭无境，\n褪去冷冽换协奏的，虚空闪躲不行，\n碎语风冽叹别后的，悸动斑驳孤零，\n坠地风冽斩孽咒的，凄恐闪过无形，\n随笔誊写残页轴的，虚荣勘破孤星，\n对弈正邪盼解救的，遗踪看破无名，\n废弃冷铁翻窃走的，机控探索不明，\n会议整夜翻写愁的，疲痛看破无情。\n\n[Verse 2 | male rapper, wordplay and palindromes, tighter and faster, a short silence after every second line, pairs of lines separated by air]\n回文和我偶遇殊途同路后人归文回 [Silence]\n对称的结构黑特们看了也真会称对，\n倍增的节奏和词句要继续成倍增倍 [Silence]\n对准开炮谁跳脚谁知我的针对准对，\n\n背身太多名利我停下因为准备身背 [Silence]\n水温得烫不能加冰否则会混为温水，\n水浑太久没法回头清流也沦为浑水 [Silence]\n睡昏的人叫不醒因为他们沉醉昏睡，\n\n美人尊贵珍贵的原因纯粹仍为人美 [Silence]\n北门砸场来的挑战者趁早滚回门北，\n类人动物被我粉碎还想要成为人类 [Silence]\n鬼神受赂却不投入就不配尊为神鬼。\n\n[Drop | 4 bars, instrumental only, a fast rap chop beat with chopped vocal samples, hi-hats rolling, sub bass pulsing, a short riser into the chorus]\n\n[Chorus | shouted hook, a fast chopped delivery, the beat slams in on every downbeat, the last two lines are sung long by the female voice]\nchop永不会stop，\ndrop从不会pop，\n跟着困难和痴呆的未来，这恋爱里已经陷入了爱河的奔窜迷茫者，\n趁着混乱的时代和悲哀的现在，你历经艰苦的改革可仍然迷航着，\n欺骗了世界里一生孤独的诗人，\n纪念着事业里牺牲无数的痴人。\n\n[Verse 3 | male rapper, fast rap with a trap melody, a gritty story told in a plain flat voice, 808 and sparse hi-hats, a breath after every line]\n何某走出看守所，逗留在贺州偏僻恶臭的街口，\n可手勾住裤兜搜索只凑够建议自己喝粥的借口，\n热流透入他收缩的喉头，他旋即去低着头咳嗽，\n呃，右手扶住肉粥的碗，得，念起这首歌，又，\n和后头出售牛肉的老刘头点起烟喝酒，来抽口，\n\n可求人这么久，渴求成了奢求。\n\n[Bridge | Female Vocal, defiant and clear, building intensity, the beat pauses between each line for half a beat]\n我把思想化作武器，打出独立战术击打细节，\n剥开荒谬怪诞外衣，展现无敌幻术启发异界，\n绝不屈服任何权威，不向奴役叛徒抵达地界，\n重塑这片精神废墟，我要处理乱木激发气节，\n颠覆那些刻板印象，打破物理算术劈叉历劫，\n拆穿虚假和平假象，直面故意犯怵击杀异业，\n斩断那些利益链条，拒绝宿敌赞助批发闭结，\n用这文字燃起大火，照亮骨气散布洗刷历届。\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, a DJ trap speedcore section, blast-beat hi-hats, distorted 808 slides and chopped voice samples, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 4 | male rapper, fast chop rap, the beat is stripped to 808 and a snare, a short silence after every second line, the last line is spat slowly]\n再次开始跟着这拍子，\n白痴成了不吭声的摆设 [Silence]\n坏事的孩子迟早被自己害死，\n还不趁早拜师对我感恩怀德 [Silence]\n踩死了矮子摆直了呆子，崽子得拜赐。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then 808 and the full beat slam in, vocals rest]\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, instrumental only, the fast beat falls away, the dark piano loop plays alone, a chopped sample, a final 808 hit]\n[End]","notes":["全集里最长最密的 rap。原稿的多个标签叠在一起且内容为空（[verse][fast rap chop][bridge][drop][Chorus]），已合并为 \"具体的 chop 间奏 + 有词的 Chorus\"；[instrument music][dj trap speedcore] 写成具体的 8 小节 speedcore 间奏。","抢拍处理：每行 14-17 字的长句按 7+7 加逗号换气；在回文/对仗最密的 verse 里，用行内 [Silence] 代替每隔一行的逗号（行内 [Silence] 前不放标点）；每 2 行空一行。","女声段落（Hook / Chorus / Bridge）用 Style 里的 \"a female singer takes the hooks\" 来锁，歌词里用 [Female Vocal] 提示；原稿标签里的 [female voice] 保留意图。","Vocal Gender 选 Male 是为了锁定主 rap；女声 hook 靠 Style 里的 female singer 和歌词标签 [Female Vocal] 实现。若整首被唱成同一个声音，就把 Vocal Gender 留空再试。","末尾那两大段无标签的 rap 草稿（文件2 第 1635-1736 行）是同一首的素材，未纳入，见 skipped 说明。"]},{"id":"051","slug":"roadside","title":"路边","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1062-1109","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"92","length":"about 3:20","style":"Swaggering Chinese boom-bap with trap bounce at 92 BPM in D minor, rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male rapper delivers a cocky, playful, clear flow with sharp breaths between phrases, then chants the chorus with a mocking, shouted hook and a few gang vocals. A dusty sampled piano loop, a punchy kick and snare with crisp hi-hats and a deep 808 bass carry the verses, a brassy horn stab accents the end of each bar, and the chorus adds a bigger drum break and crowd shouts. Arrogant, humorous mood of a rapper mocking roadside amateurs while speeding down the highway, playing CSGO and picking a flower-pot egg. Ends on one horn stab and silence. Punchy, bright, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, orchestral strings, acoustic folk, country, autotune, heavy metal","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a dusty piano loop, a punchy kick and snare enter on bar three, a brassy horn stab on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | cocky playful rapped voice, piano loop and kick, hi-hats crisp, a clear breath after every line, the first single word is a short shout, slightly behind the beat]\n哎，\n你的flow太过路边，韵脚不够显眼，\n我们的鼓点粘合信念，全部来自上天，\n无论是古典还是新鲜，走在前面又或并肩，\n纪念了几年，回到了起点，边缘的深渊，\n一刻不停地循环变迁，\n押韵押到睁不开眼，\n面前的电脑都是片片的email，我眼眼厌倦，\n别不要脸逼我践踏你的尊严，终结你的明天，\n年年都是如此，我闻名世间与今天！\n\n[Chorus | mocking shouted hook, bigger drum break, crowd shouts double the first line of each pair, horn stab on the downbeat]\n太过路边的垃圾，不要摆上台面，\n来自土瘪的杀机，我就要去打脸，\n再说你古街的大义，不配被改变，\n来做起粗劣马杀鸡，怎能去开店，\n菜单上的彩蛋是个菜蛋，\n而我玩csgo喜欢拆弹发射彩弹，\n灾难到了该看，改航海南不用管排班。\n\n[Verse 2 | cocky playful rapped voice again, piano loop and 808, the first words are a triple shout, faster, a breath after every line]\n哟哟哟，\n想达到我的高度，这是你学不会的招数，\n我在高速公路超速，顺路碾死几只老鼠，\n它们嗷嗷叫着噢噢输了，就像找出了闹事的孬猪，\n告诉，这高树，在学着高数，\n要输，一个个报数，然后我们来抱树，这保熟，\n我套住，你们跑路，我不需饶恕，热水对你们浇筑，\n耶，我的兄弟gangsta，干死他，can stop！\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then the full drum break and 808 slam in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, shouted at full power, crowd shouts louder, same melody as the first chorus]\n太过路边的垃圾，不要摆上台面，\n来自土瘪的杀机，我就要去打脸，\n再说你古街的大义，不配被改变，\n来做起粗劣马杀鸡，怎能去开店，\n菜单上的彩蛋是个菜蛋，\n而我玩csgo喜欢拆弹发射彩弹，\n灾难到了该看，改航海南不用管排班。\n\n[Outro | 4 bars, drums and 808 stop, the piano loop plays alone, one horn stab, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["verse 1 的第一行「哎」、verse 2 的第一行「哟哟哟」都是起手的叫喊，保持独立成行并在标签里写明。","verse 1 里「押韵押到睁不开眼，面前的电脑都是片片的email我眼眼厌倦」音节很密，已在分句处加逗号并在标签要求半拍留白。"]},{"id":"052","slug":"absolute-packed","title":"Absolute Packed","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1115-1156","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"88","length":"about 3:10","style":"Technical multi-syllable hip-hop at 88 BPM in A minor, rapped in English. A male rapper delivers a clear, confident, precisely enunciated flow with room between phrases and layered internal rhymes, switching to a bigger, shouted delivery in the chorus with a few doubled voices. A tight boom-bap kick and snare, a deep warm bass and a bright piano loop carry the verses, shimmering synth bells glitter between lines, and the chorus adds a wide pad, a punchy clap and an uplifting brass stab. Radiant, proud and relentless mood of a rapper whose mind takes flight, shining light on every syllable. Ends on the piano loop alone with a bell tone. Crisp, bright, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, country, acoustic folk, heavy metal, lo-fi hiss, autotune, orchestral strings, comedy","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a bright piano loop, a tight boom-bap kick and snare enter on bar three, shimmering synth bells on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | clear confident rapped voice, precise enunciation, piano and drums only, a short breath at every period, pairs of lines separated by air, slightly behind the beat]\nThe intricacy way to be the key under the light bright sight.\nEvery sound profound you see it free breaking their might with all your light right.\n\nThe way I am going showing this power by the hour shower.\nMy mind keeps going showing the power by the hour profound and astounding surrounding.\n\nYou see it free the display way with all of its might and its light tight.\nMy vocabulary varies necessarily a commentary extraordinary dairy fairies.\n\n[Chorus | bigger shouted delivery, a wide pad and clap enter, doubled voices on the last words of each line, an uplifting brass stab on the downbeat]\nThis flow you know is a show right to go so bright tonight!\nA light to show you right, yeah you already know this show is tight!\nThe multi-syllable sound incredible all around!\nCompletely legible breaking ground profoundly found it!\nMy mind takes flight! With all its might! Shining so bright! A dazzling light!\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the clear confident rap, piano and drums, a little faster, a short breath at every period, pairs of lines separated by air]\nI create great art with devotion emotion, the sound found from my story glory.\nThis composition ambition I pound all around, fills their territory story forever astounding surrounding.\n\nThe state I debate of the nation situation, all around my glory is shining refining consigning.\nI dictate my position with precision, the sound the victory story unending transcending sending it!\n\nSo quick so slick in my time committing this crime, beat the clock with a shock rocking the block!\nThe quick action takes my time committing this crime so fine.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down to kick, bass and the voice, spoken-rapped and urgent, a short breath at every period, brass stab on the last line]\nFrom the ashes the flashes and the crumble tumble, end their hesitation frustration and aggravation.\nYou will see it free, the might I give to live believe.\nMy reputation the declaration, gonna live give its creation the whole nation!\nBreaking the jumble tumble, showing the light so bright right with all my might!\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, shouted at full power, doubled voices, brass and clap at full, same melody as the first chorus]\nThis flow you know is a show right to go so bright tonight!\nA light to show you right, yeah you already know this show is tight!\nThe multi-syllable sound incredible all around!\nCompletely legible breaking ground profoundly found it!\nMy mind takes flight! With all its might! Shining so bright! A dazzling light!\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and pad fall away, the piano loop plays alone, one shimmering bell tone, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这首是多音节押韵炫技，音节密度极高（单行常 20+ 音节）。处理：BPM 压到 88，Style 写 clear enunciation / space between phrases；每一行单独成行并用空行分成 2 行一组；段落标签要求 \"a short breath at every period\"。","原稿 [Outro] 下面又有 [instrumental outro] 两个叠在一起，已合并成一个具体的尾奏。"]},{"id":"053","slug":"interwoven","title":"Interwoven","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1159-1215","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"90","length":"about 3:20","style":"Melodic hip-hop at 90 BPM in E minor with layered vocal textures, rapped in English. A male rapper delivers a relaxed, confident, warm flow with interwoven internal rhymes, steady and clear in the verses, then lifts into a catchy, anthemic half-sung chorus with doubled voices. A crisp boom-bap kick and snare, a warm bass and a soft electric piano loop carry the verses, a clean guitar plays a bright riff between lines, and the chorus adds a wide pad, a clap and layered vocal harmonies. Hopeful, determined mood of a rapper rising to the top, one rhyme at a time. Ends on the beat fading under overlapping layered voices. Warm, bright, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad, country, heavy metal, lo-fi hiss, autotune, orchestral strings, comedy, screaming","lyrics":"[Intro | 4 bars, the beat starts, intricate layers of sound build one by one, a spoken ad-lib opening over the first bar]\nYo, step up to the mic, feel the vibe, this is the ride,\nCannot hide, nowhere left to slide, open wide.\n\n[Verse 1 | relaxed confident rapped voice, boom-bap drums and electric piano, a short breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nI gotta find a way, that's the secret key,\nOn this rap display, sets my spirit free.\nMy mind takes flight, to finally be,\nA blinding light, for all the world to see.\n\nEvery line is by design, gonna outshine and define.\nYeah, my thoughts intertwine, making the pattern bright.\n\n[Chorus | catchy anthemic half-sung voice, doubled voices, wide pad and clap enter, the beat hits hard on the last line]\nThis is the rhyme that is the reason,\nThrough every hard season that I am facing,\nIt's the vibe I believe in,\nThe life I am living that I am leading,\nNever stop,\nJust rise to the top,\nMake the whole crowd just drop now, loud now!\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the relaxed confident rap, a little more driven, guitar riff between lines, a short breath after every line]\nFrom the ground where I started, fueled by pure devotion,\nA distinct sound, putting things in motion.\nI ain't got no doubt, gonna let the whole world know,\nYeah, I figured it out, watch my confidence grow.\n\nThis is the way the story must go, putting on a show,\nLike a river flow, fast, forever, go!\nGot the multi-syllable, sound incredible,\nAlways legible, never regrettable.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down to kick, bass and the voice, spoken-rapped and sincere, a pause after the second line, then the beat returns]\nThis ambition that I state, is the key to set my spirit free.\nMy position sealed by fate, a guarantee.\nGonna create, the future I wanna see.\nMy decision, my destiny, forever great, just watch me!\n\n[Chorus | stronger and wider than the first, same melody, the beat hits hard on the last line]\nThis is the rhyme that is the reason,\nThrough every hard season that I am facing,\nIt's the vibe I believe in,\nThe life I am living that I am leading,\nNever stop,\nJust rise to the top,\nMake the whole crowd just drop now, loud now!\n\n[Outro | the voice rides the beat with complex layered vocals and rhymes, the beat slowly fades under them, a final shout at the end]\nYeah, just the mic and I, reaching for the sky,\nWatching limits die, wave the world goodbye!\nThis Flow... forever go... you know...\nThe craft... the path... the laugh... blast...\n\nYo!!!\n[End]","notes":["原稿有三处\"制作说明被写进了歌词\"：Intro 第一行「Beat starts, intricate layers of sound build」、副歌末尾的「(Beat hits hard)」、Outro 的「(Beat fades out with complex layered vocals and rhymes)」。它们会被直接唱出来，已移进方括号里的英文演出指示，这三句不再出现在歌词里。","末尾孤立的「Yo!!!」归入本曲 Outro 的收尾喊叫（文件里它紧贴在本曲之后、下一首之前）。"]},{"id":"054","slug":"this-is-my-country","title":"This Is My Country","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自副歌末句「This is my country, yeah, this is my nation.」，暂定此名。","album":"歌词2","lang":"English","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1217-1254","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"90","length":"about 3:20","style":"Gritty protest hip-hop with a soulful hook at 90 BPM in C minor, rapped and sung in English. A male rapper delivers a stern, weary, clear flow in the verses with weight on the first word of each line, then sings the chorus in a rough, aching, sustained voice with a few gang voices behind. A dusty boom-bap kick and snare, a slow soul guitar line and a deep warm bass carry the verses, a lonely trumpet plays long notes between phrases, and the chorus adds a gospel-like organ, a wide pad and stacked harmonies. Bitter, serious mood of a nation of gunshots, medical bills, money in the halls and empty slogans. Ends on the lonely trumpet fading. Raw, warm, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, ballad only piano, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, country, heavy metal, comedy, autotune, upbeat pop","lyrics":"[Intro | 8 bars, a slow soul guitar line, a lonely trumpet plays a long phrase, a dusty kick and snare enter on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | stern weary rapped voice, weight on the first word of each line and a falling tone at the end, guitar, bass and drums, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nThis nation, where gunshots blast, a deadly narration,\nThis land, where healthcare bills are walls, causing deep lamentation.\nThis country, where cash rules the halls, shaping all legislation,\nThis realm, where freedom's a claim, a faded illusion.\n\nThis state, where empty words are praised, concealing desperation,\nThis ground, where the poor are shamed, a bitter conclusion.\nThis age, where old dreams are tamed, lost in ruination.\nThis is my country, yeah, this is my nation.\n\n[Chorus | rough aching sustained sung voice, organ and wide pad enter, stacked harmonies, gang voices on the last line, long held line endings]\nThis nation, where promises are lies, and power's a wild prize,\nThis land, where façades hide despair, beneath deceptive skies.\nThis country, shouting \"Liberty!\", but never hearing cries,\nThis is my country, yeah, this is my nation.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the stern weary rap, guitar, bass and drums, a little more angry, a breath after every line]\nYo, this state, where two parties clash, in endless frustration,\nThis realm, where racial lines are drawn, causing degradation.\nThis land, where the homeless sleep rough, beneath towers of elevation,\nThis country, waving big sticks abroad, internal devastation.\n\nThis nation, where news is spun, a filtered explanation,\nThis ground, where heroes bleed out, for corporate accumulation.\nThis age, where grand slogans stun, masking deep lamentation.\nThis is my country, yeah, this is my nation.\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence with only the trumpet, then drums, organ and bass come back together, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice rough and wide, gang voices louder, same melody as the first chorus]\nThis nation, where promises are lies, and power's a wild prize,\nThis land, where façades hide despair, beneath deceptive skies.\nThis country, shouting \"Liberty!\", but never hearing cries,\nThis is my country, yeah, this is my nation.\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and organ fall away, the soul guitar plays alone, the lonely trumpet holds a long note and fades, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 8 行 verse 全以 \"This nation / land / country…\" 排比开头，容易被唱成机械的同一腔调；标签里分别要求\"每行首词重音、行尾下沉\"，并在行间留气口。","副歌第四行与 verse 末行相同，保持原文，不做合并。"]},{"id":"055","slug":"welcome-to-the-zone","title":"Welcome to the zone","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自第一句，暂定此名。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1257-1303","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"88","length":"about 4:00","style":"Dystopian industrial hip-hop at 88 BPM in B minor, rapped in Mandarin Chinese with a few English words. A male rapper delivers a deadpan, cold, razor-sharp flow with a clear breath after every line, almost like a bored broadcaster reading the news, then spits the chorus in a harder, colder chant with the color words stressed. A distorted sub-bass 808, a stiff mechanical kick and snare, a cold detuned synth drone and static glitches carry the verses, a distant propaganda-style fanfare sample flickers in the gaps, and the chorus adds a heavy industrial riff and cold crowd chants. Dark satirical mood of a cyber city with firewalls, trending lists that forget everything in a second, and a smiling panda gif twitching. Ends on a power cut sound. Cold, hard, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, orchestral strings, country, upbeat pop, autotune, comedy","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a cold detuned synth drone, static glitches, a stiff mechanical beat enters on bar three, a distant fanfare sample on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 3, deadpan cold rapped voice, 808 and kick, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nWelcome to the zone，这里是赛博神州的背面，\n防火墙内外温差足够冻裂赤道的纬线，\n热搜榜在零点一秒完成集体失忆手术，\n热搜变四零四，只剩熊猫微笑的GIF在抽搐，\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 3, same flat voice, the synth drone louder, glitches more frequent]\n五千年太长，只争朝夕的魔幻现实主义，\n拆迁队的拆字涂鸦比甲骨文更有仪式，\n广场大屏幕播放着永远睛朗的天气预爆，\n而筒子楼里的叹息在霉斑墙面发酵，\n\n[Verse 1 | part 3 of 3, voice colder, the last two lines are spat slowly]\n红头文件在流水线上盖戳如同印刷冥币，\n农民工的社保卡余额是场行为艺术把戏，\n福布斯新贵们举杯在东方明珠塔尖摇晃，\n而地下铁通道里蜷缩着被扫码时代注销的残像。\n\n[Chorus | harder colder chant, a heavy industrial riff enters, cold crowd chants double the color words, stress the two color words each time]\n红，是热搜消失前最后跳动的字节，\n红，是十字路口监控探头的充血视角，\n灰，是凌晨四点环卫工扫不净的雾霾雪，\n灰，是退休金账簿上越描越淡的墨迹哲学。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 3, back to the deadpan flow, 808 and kick, riff gone, sarcastic]\n教科书里屈原还在投江，只不过换了水质分析报告，\n孔夫子周游列国被拦下检查暂住证编号，\n公务员考试的论题是论沉默的优越性，\nKTV点播榜前三是没有春天，不准通行，监控爱情，\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 3, same flat voice, faster, glitches tighter]\n房地产商把故宫模型装进盲盒售卖，\n年轻人把脊椎弯成二维码的形状等待被扫描，\n妇产科护土抱着新生儿练习微笑管理课程，\n而产房外电子屏滚动着：感恩，奉献，不准问，\n\n[Verse 2 | part 3 of 3, voice colder, the last two lines are spat slowly]\n白酒瓶里泡着中年男人的肝胆和房贷计算器，\n短视频平台直播着三线城市广场舞维稳奇迹，\n诗人把敏感词磨成粉调进油画颜料，\n画廊里所有作品标题都叫，风景这边独好。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the beat stops suddenly, a sampled news-broadcast ending song and a battery car alarm sound over silence, then the full beat slams back in, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | harder and colder still, heavy industrial riff, crowd chants louder, same melody as the first chorus, stress the two color words each time]\n红，是热搜消失前最后跳动的字节，\n红，是十字路口监控探头的充血视角，\n灰，是凌晨四点环卫工扫不净的雾霾雪，\n灰，是退休金账簿上越描越淡的墨迹哲学。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and riff fall away, the cold synth drone plays alone, static glitches, then a power cut sound and silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿 [drop] 下面是一条全角方括号的采样说明「［Beat sudden stop, sampling: new broadcast ending song + battery car alarm sound］」，已改成半角方括号里的具体 Drop 描述（新闻联播片尾曲式采样 + 电瓶车警报），不再是易被误读的全角括号。","第一句「Welcome to the zone，这里是…」是中英混合，Style 里写了 sung in Mandarin Chinese with a few English words；其余 24 行 verse 都是 12-18 字的长句，按语义加逗号，BPM 88。","原稿中的错别字（预爆、睛朗、护土等）是你的原文，一字未改。"]},{"id":"056","slug":"algorithm-suffering","title":"算法批准的苦难","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自副歌末句「我们早活成数据流里被算法批准的苦难」，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1308-1348","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"50","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"84","length":"about 3:50","style":"Somber Chinese boom-bap rap with a cold sung hook at 84 BPM in A minor, rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male rapper delivers a flat, tired, razor-clear flow in the verses with a clear breath after every line, then sings the chorus in a cold, resigned, sustained voice with a layered double. A slow dusty kick and snare, a muted piano loop and a deep bass carry the verses, thin strings hang over the hook, and a faint broadcast-static texture flickers underneath. Bitter, satirical mood of an overbuilt economy, unfinished buildings, red health codes and a nation of voices welded into one tone. Ends on a sudden power cut. Dry, cold, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad only piano, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, upbeat pop, comedy, heavy metal, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a muted piano loop, a faint broadcast static, a slow dusty kick and snare enter on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | flat tired rapped voice, piano loop and kick, a clear breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n当烂尾楼业主在郑州街头背诵《民法典》条款，\n健康码却突然转红，像被掐住喉管的惊喘，\n村镇银行取款键变成灰色，四零四错误页面，\n而纪委通报的院长，正往瑞士账户转账癌细胞的钱。\n\n[Verse 2 | same flat voice, a deep bass added, a little more bitter]\n教培失业潮撞上三十五岁简历回收站，\n上海团长特权车碾过封控区最后的菜篮，\n江西彩礼货广告贴在精准扶贫宣传栏，\n鹤岗两万块买断的人生，在深圳只够租一年半。\n\n[Chorus | cold resigned sustained sung voice, thin strings enter, a layered double sings the last word of each line, the beat steady]\n这报表里增长的是ICU呼吸机计费器的跳转，\n这屏幕里的平安是热搜撤稿员的彻夜加班，\n当所有喉咙被焊进同一个腔调发声站，\n我们早活成数据流里被算法批准的苦难。\n\n[Verse 3 | back to the flat rapped voice, piano loop and bass, sharper and angrier, a clear breath after every line]\n看洞庭湖抽干鱼虾，种别墅的推土机多忙，\n三甲医院采购单，藏着进口器械百分之两百回扣账，\n贵州扶贫公路塌方时，明星逃税榜正更新，\n苏州和服事件出警速度，超过唐山报警铃。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little colder, same melody]\n这报表里增长的是ICU呼吸机计费器的跳转，\n这屏幕里的平安是热搜撤稿员的彻夜加班，\n当所有喉咙被焊进同一个腔调发声站，\n我们早活成数据流里被算法批准的苦难。\n\n[Spoken Word | a flat cold newsreader voice reads official slogans over faint broadcast static, one slogan at a time with a pause between them, beat paused]\n“恒大承诺保交楼….”\n“鼓励灵活就业，\n“双减政策落地.”\n“动态清零.”\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, the beat slams back in after the pause, piano loop and bass and the full drums, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice cold and wide, layered double louder, same melody as the first chorus]\n这报表里增长的是ICU呼吸机计费器的跳转，\n这屏幕里的平安是热搜撤稿员的彻夜加班，\n当所有喉咙被焊进同一个腔调发声站，\n我们早活成数据流里被算法批准的苦难。\n\n[Outro | a flat spoken newsreader voice over fading static, the broadcast cuts out suddenly in a power-cut sound, then silence]\n“我国基尼系数呈…下降趋势..青年失业率.阶段性•\n调整…文化自信…增强….\n（！操！又停电了！）\n[End]","notes":["Bridge 里的四句口号（恒大承诺保交楼 / 鼓励灵活就业 / 双减政策落地 / 动态清零）原稿引号有的没闭合，已按原样保留；写成\"冷淡播音腔 + 轻微电流噪声\"的念白，不是唱。","Outro 是被突然停电打断的播报，最后一句「（！操！又停电了！）」按原样放在括号里，作为叠加的低吼；含粗口。"]},{"id":"057","slug":"infinite-rhyme","title":"无限押韵","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1353-1432","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"75","influence":"60","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"100","length":"about 4:30","style":"Hypnotic Chinese tongue-twister rap on a minimal trap beat at 100 BPM in G minor, rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male rapper delivers a rapid, rhythmic, playful flow with strict internal rhymes and a sharp breath between phrases, chopping syllables like a drum pattern, then chants the chorus in a louder, bouncy, nonsense-syllable style with a few gang shouts. A deep 808 bass, a crisp snare and rolling hi-hats carry the verses over a looping marimba-like pluck, a wobbly synth stab answers the end of each line, and the chorus adds a bigger kick, claps and shouted crowd syllables. Absurd, mischievous mood of an endless rhyme chain, sound over meaning. Ends on a marimba pluck and a laugh. Punchy, bright, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, orchestral strings, country, heavy metal, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a looping marimba-like pluck, a crisp snare and rolling hi-hats enter on bar three, a wobbly synth stab on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | rapid rhythmic playful rap, 808 and hi-hat rolls, a sharp breath after every line, syllables land on the beat like a drum pattern]\n让老胖洗漱去哦草你是，将奥阳奇招与狗要即使，\n康要让起诉虚楼交集日，绑要钢你好绿头小屁事，\n抢老绑康给央视破药，章药胖浪黑方式国鸟，\n航好烫上陪娘吃磨巧，长焦方向被两次脱掉，\n大体相当甲乙双方，阿里长江炸鸡羊汤，\n卡米两张牙医杨康，加以盲抢杀气让杭。\n\n[Chorus | loud bouncy nonsense-syllable chant, bigger kick and claps, gang shouts on the last syllable of each line, the English-looking syllables are spat clearly]\n可乐么喝，呢这测个，热特呢么，\n乐乐侧着，者则和德，合可歌色，\n隔乐我的得乐，可折火热捏特，\n特色诺克么呢，特乐泼社车河，\n我休假，坡牛呀，错够傻，若求下，\nnos show chia！fo yo pia！\n玻激发，左一下，罗嘀嗒，佛你妈，\nwo piu na！told Molly big ba！\n\n[Verse 2 | part 1 of 2, the rapid playful rap again, shorter lines, 808 and hi-hats, a breath between each line]\n公开赛孟太太，\n宋太宰钟开莱，\n痛痛快快，房东太太！\n一大块激发态，\n记下来李家寨，\n绿化带批下来，\n七八百氯化钙，\n第八代计划外。\n\n[Verse 2 | part 2 of 2, faster, the two-part lines are spat in one breath each with air between, ends on a held word]\n雨花台滴下来，\n戚大帅余下来，\n一大排几大块，于大海七八块，\n利亚太李佳白，于嘉泰曲麻莱，\n踢下来挤下来，碧塔海你亚奈，\n尼巴莱提下来，移下来洗下来，\n七八代须加盖，于亚太李大帅。\n\n[Chorus | same energy as the first chorus, a long chain of rhymed names, claps on every beat]\n郭平梁恰哇活性氧哇她骆秉章他怕，\n阿萨左营港萨达若冰霜发嘎，\n郭景昌哈家博陵王架卡过荥阳卡辣，\n拉闸薄情郎咋下郭鼎堂虾查，\n薄幸郎擦吧若冰霜爸妈所应当那妈，\n马掐落平阳瓦塔握情况鸭鸭。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence, then the full beat slams in with a marimba pluck, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 4, the loudest chant, bouncy and fast, gang shouts on every line end]\n七提一皮底肌离洗，\n比你迷提提里起皮，\n其他提压皮压力哈迪瓜，\n西沙比纳米马地煞立马，\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 4, the rapid chain of rhyming words, one breath for each line, claps steady]\n以及地区必须预期一起第一积极及其一句，\n具体区域低于其余立即体系距离给予依据，\n一批集体气体据悉一级基于厘米予以玉米，\n机器一齐密集地理极其与其提起利息聚集，\n趋于一笔弟弟一一袭击以西低迷一举一体，\n\n[Final Chorus | part 3 of 4, the voice breaks into laughter and nonsense sounds, the parenthesized line is a shouted crowd chant, then the rhyme chain resumes]\n啊啊啊啊啊哈哈哈哈哈哈哈，\n（哇啊啊啊啪啪啪啪啪呐呐呐）\n其他一下计划以下巨大一家一把旗下地下，\n极大一大其它希腊陛下依法立法底下，\n骑马溢价已达壁画激发提价几家，\n抵达泥沙你家密码低下一架，\n抵押虚假起码西夏立马，\n\n[Final Chorus | part 4 of 4, the lines get shorter and faster until they are single words, then the long final lines are spat with full breath, band at full]\n低价里下批发愈加，\n提拔西亚期价，\n西瓜启发，\n哈哈哈，\n挤压第八，\n琵琶息差技法，\n吸纳一发余下利差，\n披挂惧怕绿化低洼余家，\n菊花李家语法历法比价地价，\n细化计价气压七大激化一大立下，\n离家愈发欺诈取下低压绿茶继发提法，\n尼亚七八极佳鱼虾起家疲乏笔法区划笔画，\n利亚议价逆差居家积压提辖皮下底价你爸尼玛。\n\n[Outro | 4 bars, the beat stops, the marimba pluck plays alone, a laugh, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这是纯谐音连环押韵（几乎没有语义），发音完全取决于 Suno 怎么读；建议多生成几次，选读得最顺的一版，再用歌词精修修个别字。","最后一个超长 Chorus（28 行）已拆成 4 个小节；原稿每行末尾的空格全部改成逗号/句号，行内的空格（如「一大排几大块 于大海七八块」）改成逗号换气。","括号「（哇啊啊啊啪啪啪啪啪呐呐呐）」是夹在中间的拟声叠唱，保持独立成行。含一句粗口。"]},{"id":"058","slug":"anarchist","title":"安那其主义者","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1435-1492","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"60","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"150","length":"about 3:20","style":"Chinese hardcore punk with shouted rap at 150 BPM in E minor, shouted and rapped in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist barks the verses in a loud, hoarse, sarcastic rapped delivery with a clear breath after every line, then screams the chorus in a ragged, sustained shout with a crowd of gang vocals chanting the title. Fast distorted power chords, a driving distorted bass and fast live drums with a snare on every backbeat carry the verses, the chorus switches to a half-time feel with huge chords, crash cymbals and gang shouts, and a siren wails in the gaps. Furious, mocking mood of a self-declared anarchist who rejects every ruler and law. Ends on a distorted chord, feedback and a crowd roar. Raw, loud, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, orchestral strings, country, smooth jazz, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a siren wail, a distorted bass riff, a fast fill on the drums, distorted power chords crash in on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | part 1 of 2, loud hoarse sarcastic rap, power chords and drums, a clear breath after every line, on the beat]\n我是安人，\n不是晚安的安，\n是你安那其爷爷的安，\n我拿着巴枯宁的矛，\n我举着施蒂那的盾牌，\n你会无处可逃，\n因为我还有来自斯普纳的底牌。\n\n[Verse 1 | part 2 of 2, same bark, the last lines are sarcastically calm, almost spoken, with the band dropping to bass and drums]\n没有叛国之罪，\n没有抗法之理，\n国家只是一个虚名，\n建立在血腥上的暴力机器，\n不如跟我一起说声早上好，\n来一块，\n克鲁泡特金的面包，\n再来杯牛奶配上燕麦。\n\n[Chorus | ragged screamed sustained shout, half-time feel, huge chords, crash cymbals, gang vocals chant the title, a short silence between each line]\n我是安那其主义者！\n燃烧瓶是我最爱的玩具！\n我左手炸药包右手发鸭耳大轰！\n我是安那其主义者！\n我操死你列宁野爹！\n我是安那其主义者！\n我砸烂你苏联野爹！\n我是你安那其爷爷！\n我会粉碎你的一切！\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the fast loud rap, power chords and drums, a clear breath after every line, a siren in the gaps, faster]\n自由是我的生命，\n法律是我的敌人，\n不要神佛不要君主，\n不要皇帝不要总统，\n不要主席不要统帅，\n不要狗官员不要条子，\n我们不需要任何权威，\n我们的爱恨从天南到地北，\n我们的意志超越国界线，\n力量会粉碎所有警车和法院。\n\n[Drop | 2 bars, everything cuts to one beat of full silence with only the siren, then the full band slams in at half-time, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, screamed at full power, gang vocals at full volume, half-time feel, the new closing lines are shouted with a crowd roar]\n我是安那其主义者！\n燃烧瓶是我最爱的玩具！\n我左手炸药包右手发鸭耳大轰！\n我是你安那其爷爷！\n我要砸烂公检法！\n我是你安那其爷爷！\n全民暴动就在此刻！\n我是安那其主义者！\n我操死你的妈！\n我操死你的爸！\n你安爹来咯哈哈哈哈哈哈！\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums stop, one distorted chord rings out with feedback, a siren fades and a crowd roar, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这是极度攻击性的朋克说唱，含大量粗口和政治口号，歌词一字未改。如平台审核拒收，可只用歌词精修替换个别词，其余保留。","150 BPM 但副歌写了 half-time feel（主唱走半速），verse 的 rap 在重音上断句，避免抢拍。"]},{"id":"059","slug":"xian-yi-duan","title":"弦已断","titleNote":"原稿无标题、无结构标签，取自结尾「弦已断…」，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1499-1541","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"66","length":"about 4:20","style":"Poetic Chinese-style (guofeng) chamber ballad at 66 BPM in D minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male baritone sings warm, weary and dignified, close to the microphone and nearly spoken in the verses, then rising to a wide, aching, sustained chorus with long held line endings and a faint harmony. A plucked guqin and a soft fingerpicked guitar carry the verses, a low cello and a warm pad enter in the pre-chorus, and the chorus adds a string section, a soft kick, a breathy bamboo flute and a distant choir. Proud, tragic mood of a musician who wanted to play the people's longing, whose string snapped at the highest note while the old nobles watched. Ends on a single guqin note fading into silence. Spacious, warm, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, female lead vocal, comedy, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a plucked guqin alone, a breathy bamboo flute joins on bar five, a faint wind texture, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | warm weary baritone, nearly spoken, guqin and guitar only, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n你想为这天下，奏一曲新的乐章，\n指尖下没有金戈铁马，只有麦浪与工商，\n你说这古老的琴弦，太过紧绷也太过悲凉，\n应弹出寻常巷陌里，人间的渴望。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice a little firmer, cello and pad enter, thunder rumbles faintly in the distance]\n可窗外雷声渐响，满座皆是旧日王孙，\n他们说你的乐音，太过自由也太过天真，\n你看见满座的犹疑，却只对自己虔诚。\n\n[Chorus | wide aching sustained voice, strings and a soft kick enter, flute sings above, distant choir, line endings held long]\n就让这根弦，断在最高亢的刹那，\n将一曲未完的歌，凝固成无声的画，\n从此怀抱残破的琴，再无人听我说话，\n我只是个凡人啊，却错生在了神话。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the nearly spoken baritone, guqin and cello, a little colder, the street outside the window]\n你并未转身离去，也并未低下头颅，\n只是将所有的言语，都还给了最初的孤独，\n你看着窗外的世界，走上你画下的草图，\n那上面繁花似锦，只是再与你毫无干系。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | same as before, the thunder louder, strings tense]\n可窗外雷声渐响，满座皆是旧日王孙，\n他们说你的乐音，太过自由也太过天真，\n你看见满座的犹疑，却只对自己虔诚。\n\n[Chorus | stronger than the first, voice breaking open on the high notes, full strings and choir, same melody as the first chorus]\n就让这根弦，断在最高亢的刹那，\n将一曲未完的歌，凝固成无声的画，\n从此怀抱残破的琴，再无人听我说话，\n我只是个凡人啊，却错生在了神话。\n\n[Bridge | stripped down to guqin and the voice, quiet and bitter, a pause after each pair of lines, strings rise slowly on the last line]\n他们说江山无恙，不过是换了琴师，\n他们说繁华如常，谁还记得那段曲辞，\n可总有人在夜里，听到那一声脆响，\n像一道永不愈合的伤。\n\n[Outro | the voice fades to a whisper, each line spoken softly with a long pause between them, the guqin plays one last note and fades, then silence]\n弦已断…\n曲未终…\n仍有回响…\n[End]","notes":["原稿只有 8 个按空行分开的小段、没有任何结构标签；我按重复关系推断：S1=Verse 1，S2=Pre-Chorus（出现 2 次），S3=Chorus（出现 2 次），S4=Verse 2，S5=Bridge，末三行省略号句=Outro。若你本意不同，改标签即可，文字不用动。","每行中间的空格（如「你想为这天下 奏一曲新的乐章」）改成逗号做呼吸点；结尾「弦已断… / 曲未终… / 仍有回响…」的省略号保持，写成渐弱的低语。"]},{"id":"060","slug":"anarcho-capitalism-night","title":"アナーコ・キャピタリズムの夜","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1544-1630","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"130","length":"about 4:30","style":"Cold driving post-punk at 130 BPM in E minor, sung in Japanese. A male vocalist sings deadpan and detached in the verses, almost spoken, then in the chorus rises to a clear, defiant, sustained voice with a distant layered double. A driving melodic bass guitar with a chorus effect carries the whole song, a cold repetitive drum beat keeps a steady motorik pulse, an echoing guitar with feedback and sharp angular stabs rides on top, and the chorus adds wider guitars, a bright cold synth line and a heavier kick. Rational, rebellious, nocturnal mood of a free individual who owns his own body and signs contracts at the bottom of the night. Ends with the pulsating bass fading out alone. Cold, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a driving melodic bass guitar starts, a cold repetitive drum beat joins on bar three, echoing guitar feedback rises on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | deadpan detached male voice, almost spoken, bass and cold drums, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n静まり返った都市の境界、\n引かれた線は誰の所有か、\n許可証など破り捨てて、\n夜の底で契約を結ぶ、\n錆びついた公権力の残像、\n霧の中に消えていく亡霊、\n私たちが選ぶのは、\n見知らぬ誰かの命令ではない。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice a little firmer, the bass climbs, drums tighten, guitar stabs sharper]\n奪われた価値を取り戻す、\n不可侵の領域を定義する、\n自己所有の絶対的な法、\n静かに脈打つ市場の鼓動。\n\n[Chorus | clear defiant sustained voice, a distant layered double, wider guitars and a bright cold synth, heavier kick, long held line endings]\nアナーコ・キャピタリズムの夜、\n非侵害原則が導く道標、\n国家という名の鎖を断ち、\n自発的秩序の中に踊る、\n価格は自由の呼吸、\n契約は魂の証、\n境界を越えて響く、\n私という名の唯一の王国。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the deadpan voice, bass and cold drums, guitar feedback quieter, colder]\n独占された暴力の終焉、\n私設の警備が街を守る、\n道路も空も海もすべて、\n個人の意志で繋がり合う、\n不換紙幣はただの紙屑、\n黄金と暗号が価値を刻む、\n寄生する者たちの叫びは、\n冷たい風に掻き消された。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | same as before, voice firmer, the bass climbs]\n奪われた価値を取り戻す、\n不可侵の領域を定義する、\n自己所有の絶対的な法、\n静かに脈打つ市場の鼓動。\n\n[Chorus | stronger and wider than the first, same melody as the first chorus]\nアナーコ・キャピタリズムの夜、\n非侵害原則が導く道標、\n国家という名の鎖を断ち、\n自発的秩序の中に踊る、\n価格は自由の呼吸、\n契約は魂の証、\n境界を越えて響く、\n私という名の唯一の王国。\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, a bass solo with a heavy flange effect over minimal drums, then the guitar becomes more dissonant and bends against the bass, vocals rest]\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, bass and drums only, the voice firm and spoken-sung, a pause after each pair of lines]\n誰にも支配させない、\n私の体は私の資本、\n誰にも強制させない、\n私の労働は私の果実、\n自律した個人の集合体、\n美しき無秩序の秩序。\n\n[Guitar Solo | 8 bars, high-pitched sharp melodic guitar lines with heavy delay over the driving bass and drums, vocals rest]\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and defiant, distant double louder, full band, same melody as the first chorus]\nアナーコ・キャピタリズムの夜、\n非侵害原則が導く道標、\n国家という名の鎖を断ち、\n自発的秩序の中に踊る、\n価格は自由の呼吸、\n契約は魂の証、\n境界を越えて響く、\n私という名の唯一の王国。\n\n[Outro | the voice slows and cools, each line spoken with a long pause between them, the drums fall away and the pulsating bass plays on alone and fades out]\n自由への不可逆な選択、\n税という名の収奪を拒み、\n私たちは夜を買い取る、\n朝が来るまで取引は続く。\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词（旋律贝斯起、冷鼓、回授吉他、flange 贝斯独奏、失谐吉他、高音 delay 吉他独奏、脉动贝斯淡出）已很完整，保留并改写为「段落 | 指示」格式；其中夹在 Bridge 里的 [Bass solo][Guitar becomes more dissonant] 拆成独立的间奏小节。","日文歌词的行尾加了「、」「。」，没有改任何假名或汉字；难读词：自己所有(じこしょゆう)、非侵害(ひしんがい)、不換紙幣(ふかんしへい)。读错用歌词精修只替换这一个词。"]},{"id":"061","slug":"the-only-one","title":"唯一者","titleNote":"原稿只有一个残缺的\"：\"当标题，是七段七言古风诗；取自最后一句「唯一者立浩瀚处」，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1742-1818","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"84","length":"about 5:30","style":"Epic Chinese-style (guofeng) spoken-word rap at 84 BPM in D minor, chanted in Mandarin Chinese. A male voice recites seven stanzas of classical seven-character poetry in a deep, resonant, measured chant with natural pauses at the middle and end of every line, growing from youthful and uncertain to defiant, fierce and solitary. A plucked guqin and a low war-drum pulse carry the early stanzas, an erhu wails between lines, taiko hits and a deep bass enter in the middle stanzas, and the final stanzas add strings, a distant choir and crashing gongs. Lonely, rebellious, mythic mood of a swordsman rejecting gods, kings and heaven itself, standing alone with the stars hanging upside down. Ends on a single gong and a long erhu note. Wide, cinematic, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, pop melody, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, autotune, country","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a plucked guqin alone, a low war-drum pulse enters on bar five, a long erhu note on the last bar, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | youthful and uncertain, a deep calm chant, guqin only, a pause at the middle and end of every line, slightly behind the beat]\n少时懵懂缚红缨，低眉长拜九重城。\n不知灵台本无物，错把樊笼作太清。\n学唱长歌歌盛世，笑指沧海作泥坑。\n满堂紫衣宣铁律，万众叩首敬神明。\n忽有异域长风至，吹彻十二白玉京。\n裂帛一声惊大梦，方知天地有悲声。\n原是同源同归客，何须画地造刀兵？\n泥龛泥像泥胎骨，风雨一过即浮萍。\n\n[Break | the guqin rings out, one beat of silence, the voice breathes in]\n\n[Verse 2 | awakening, the chant firmer and colder, guqin and war drum, erhu answers after every second line]\n曾倚寒窗读玉简，笃信高悬明镜台。\n以为三尺青锋剑，能斩人间覆尘埃。\n怎奈执剑为私欲，尺衡倾覆任剪裁。\n庙堂高坐贪天功，堂下饥骨委苍苔。\n所谓森严凌云律，不过王侯手中牌。\n且看青天多黯淡，乌云蔽日掩长街。\n我不信神不信鬼，独信此心作度尺。\n既然苍穹无明理，何妨抽刃向阴霾？\n以眼还眼酬天地，血溅黄沙骨未埋。\n\n[Verse 3 | night and fear turning into mockery, the chant low and amused, taiko hits begin softly, deep bass underneath]\n漏夜寒鸦啼枯树，柴扉忽破起惊雷。\n玄衣鹰犬衔铜令，气焰滔天挟夜归。\n所为只因只字戏，欲以此身赴劫灰。\n我笑强梁颜若铁，原是朽骨覆锦衣。\n高冠博带何足惧，探手空空似盲龟。\n蛛网虽密多破绽，堂皇大阵尽荒颓。\n本以为是摩天柱，细看蝼蚁蛀神碑。\n如此残躯称太岁，岂敢妄断是非非？\n且把金尊长卧笑，笑看大厦欲倾危！\n\n[Verse 4 | resolve and vision, the voice rises, drums steady, strings enter softly, two paths opening, generous then proud]\n世人皆苦争朝夕，蝇营狗苟困泥涂。\n我欲挥手裂天幕，重开双轨渡迷途。\n左引春风生百谷，弱骨贫黎有暖炉。\n不求锦衣居玉殿，但留微喘立平芜。\n右开天海任翻覆，千金散尽复归乌。\n纵横捭阖凭肝胆，不设藩篱不问途。\n生死枯荣皆自愿，成王败寇笑狂徒。\n若厌红尘多喧网，拂衣断契入太虚。\n大荒十万八千里，寸土无主即吾庐。\n不向君王求立锥，且摘星辰作明珠！\n\n[Verse 5 | vengeance, the chant hard and relentless, war drums and bass at full, gongs on the last line of each pair, snow and blood]\n长安纵有千重雪，洗不净这血斑斓。\n九幽若有轮回笔，判不尽这作恶官。\n我辈岂是逢迎客，誓举业火燎九天！\n凿破旧朝藏金窟，散与苍生作笑谈。\n莫言时过境已迁，陈年旧案铁如山。\n任你遁走天涯角，拘魂夺命过鬼关。\n老病黄发非免死，竖子稚童亦当斩。\n种下恶因结业果，何须律法饰颟顸！\n纵是千秋身后事，也有白刃夜光寒。\n杀尽不平酬天地，大雪茫茫祭荒坛。\n\n[Break | everything stops, one beat of silence, only the wind]\n\n[Verse 6 | defiance against birth and gods, the chant cold, defiant and intimate, guqin and erhu return, the drums hold back]\n肉身本是星辰变，聚散浮沉一缕烟。\n休言父母恩如海，我本无心降人间。\n雷霆强掷胎中骨，何曾问我愿不愿？\n既无契约定生死，安敢挟恩索百年！\n割肉剔骨还旧脉，斩断尘缘不问天。\n我不认神高在上，不信君臣纲常悬。\n万物生发皆过客，谁有资格立神坛？\n漫天神佛皆泥鬼，一捧黄土掩荒泉。\n我立天地最高处，俯瞰群山笑颟顸。\n此心即是无量海，不染尘泥不挂帆。\n\n[Verse 7 | the final stanza, solitary and grand, the voice at full power, strings and a distant choir, taiko and gongs crashing, the last two lines are chanted slowly and held]\n世人贪享桃源梦，不知幽暗长深埋。\n即便金城皆推倒，亦有群魔心中来。\n权欲如藤生毒瘴，总有贪徒筑高台。\n休道太平无兵甲，警钟常鸣血不衰。\n防天防地防人祸，斩碎虚无拔阴霾。\n我本旷野一孤星，不与蜉蝣同盛衰。\n自由不绝即成伪，半点妥协是尸骸！\n不求千秋留青史，不与群氓共悲哀。\n身披风雪长执刃，踏破万古旧楼台。\n苍天若敢拘吾意，我便挥刀碎苍苔！\n且由世人笑我痴，我自独行歌慷慨。\n唯一者立浩瀚处，星汉倒悬入襟怀！\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, drums and choir fall away, the guqin plays alone, one gong, a long erhu note fades, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿没有结构标签，是七段七言诗（每段 8-12 行、每行 14 字）。我把每一段当作一个 Verse，用演出指示做\"少年懵懂 → 觉醒 → 愤怒 → 戏谑 → 自由 → 复仇 → 孤高\"的情绪递进；没有副歌，歌词一字未改。","这是\"吟诵式说唱\"，不是旋律歌；Style 写了 chanted recitation。每行 14 字，按七言的 4+3 / 2+2+3 节奏，BPM 84，段间有 [Break] 留白。","若 Suno 把它唱成旋律，用歌词精修无法改变唱法，请在 Style 里把 \"rhythmic chanted recitation\" 放到最前，再多生成几次。"]},{"id":"062","slug":"my-body-is-mine","title":"私の身体は誰のものでもない","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自副歌首句，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1824-1903","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"132","length":"about 4:30","style":"Cold driving post-punk meeting atmospheric post-rock at 132 BPM in A minor, sung in Japanese. A female vocalist sings icy and clear, detached in the verses, then wide, defiant and sustained in the chorus, with layered female voices entering softly in the bridge and growing to a full cry. A motorik drum machine and a cold, minimal, melodic post-punk bassline drive the song, an angular chorus-pedal guitar plays sharp lines with cold reverb, a synth pad hangs underneath, and the bridge builds into a wall of shimmering post-rock guitars. Rational, rebellious mood of a person walking out of a managed city of ration cards and cameras, owning her own body and name. Ends with the bass and guitar interplay slowing to silence. Cold, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a cold synth pad, a motorik bass groove slowly building, a drum machine joins on bar five, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | icy detached female voice, bass and drum machine, pad quiet, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n灰色の摩天楼に管理都市のロゴが灯る、\n生体データは国家の資産だと看板が言う、\n配給カードの番号が私の名前の代わりになる、\n「安全のため」という檻の中で息をしている、\n誰かが決めたレールの上を歩くだけの夜、\nでも配線の奥で私の意志はまだ死なない、\n壁の向こうの誰かも同じ星を見ている、\n出口はきっと地図にない場所にある。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice lifts, drums tighten, bass climbs]\n契約書のインクが乾く前に、\n私はこの手で扉を選ぶ。\n\n[Chorus | wide defiant sustained voice, guitar lines open up, heavier kick, long held line endings]\n私の身体は誰のものでもない、\n国家じゃない、神様でもない、\n出口はここに、鍵は掌の中、\n名前も国境も脱ぎ捨てて自由になる、\n交換だけが正義、暴力はいらない、\n誰も王様じゃない、誰も奴隷じゃない。\n\n[Bass Solo | 8 bars, a post-punk driving bassline, cold and minimal, over the drum machine only, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the icy detached voice, bass and drum machine, an angular guitar line added, a little more urgent]\n闇市場のネオンは誰の許可もいらない、\nピア・トゥ・ピアの声が壁の中を溶かす、\n台帳は嘘をつかない、権力より正直、\n匿名のまま握手する、それだけで十分、\n値段は私が決める、命令じゃなく合意で、\n監視カメラの赤い目は届かない場所へ、\n国家という名の独占に、さよならを言う日、\n自由は誰かがくれるものじゃなく取り戻すもの。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice lifts, drums tighten, bass climbs]\n契約書のインクが乾く前に、\n私はこの手で扉を選ぶ。\n\n[Chorus | stronger than the first, same melody as the first chorus]\n私の身体は誰のものでもない、\n国家じゃない、神様でもない、\n出口はここに、鍵は掌の中、\n名前も国境も脱ぎ捨てて自由になる、\n交換だけが正義、暴力はいらない、\n誰も王様じゃない、誰も奴隷じゃない。\n\n[Guitar Solo | 8 bars, an angular chorus-pedal guitar, post-punk lead lines with cold reverb over the bass and drum machine, instrumental only]\n\n[Bridge | atmospheric post-rock crescendo, layered female voices entering softly and then intensifying, the guitars swell into a shimmering wall, drums return on the sixth line]\n誰かが「秩序」と呼ぶものは誰かの檻だった、\n誰かが「保護」と呼ぶものは誰かの鎖だった、\n私は信じない、中央に灯る一つの太陽を、\n私は信じる、無数の小さな灯りの方を、\n国家のいない場所にも道徳は生まれる、\n暴力のない場所にこそ本当の秩序が育つ、\n誰も支配しない、誰にも支配されない、\nそれだけが唯一の、譲れない契約、\n灰色の摩天楼が遠くで揺らいで見える、\n今、私は自分の名前を初めて名乗る。\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and defiant, layered female voices at full, full band, the last two lines are sung slowly and held]\n私の身体は誰のものでもない、\n国家じゃない、神様でもない、\n出口はここに、鍵は掌の中、\n名前も国境も脱ぎ捨てて自由になる、\n交換だけが正義、暴力はいらない、\n誰も王様じゃない、誰も奴隷じゃない、\n私の身体は誰のものでもない、\nそれだけが、私の、自由。\n\n[Outro | bass and guitar interplay fading out, the motorik pulse slowing, a cold fade to silence, the voice whispers the last two lines with a long pause between them]\n誰のものでもない…\n誰のものでもない…\n[End]","notes":["原稿有 5 处括号制作说明（冷合成垫底 / 贝斯 solo / 吉他 solo / 后摇渐强 / 尾奏淡出），括号会被当歌词唱出来，已全部改写成方括号里的英文演出指示，并且把 \"no vocals\" 这类否定改成 \"instrumental only\"。","全角空格「　」都改成「、」做呼吸点；Bridge 共 10 行，写成\"后摇渐强 + 女声层层加入\"的递进。","难读词：生体(せいたい)、配給(はいきゅう)、台帳(だいちょう)。读错用歌词精修替换那个词。"]},{"id":"063","slug":"kiri-no-shima-no-echo","title":"霧の島のエコー","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 1913-1996","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"82","length":"about 4:30","style":"Warm Japanese indie-folk pop at 82 BPM in D major, sung in Japanese. A soft female vocalist sings tender and breathy, close to the microphone in the verses, then clear, emotional and soaring in the chorus with warm harmonies above. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar, a warm melodic bass and a soft cajon carry the verses, a violin plays long notes and answers the vocal phrases, a distant foghorn sounds between sections, and the final chorus opens into a full band with a key change. Nostalgic, bittersweet mood of a foggy harbor town, a doughnut split in half, and a lost friend's bass note echoing across the sea. Ends on the guitar fading with violin harmonics, waves and a distant foghorn. Warm, natural, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, screaming, autotune, metal","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a fingerpicked acoustic guitar, a distant foghorn, soft violin swells, gentle sea waves, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | soft tender female voice, breathy and close, guitar only, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n夕ぐれの港に、霧がおりてくる、\n街灯はひとつずつ、にじんでともる、\nさびた、いかりのそばで、潮風がうたう、\nだれかのわすれた声を、はこぶように。\n\n石だたみの坂道、足音がこだまして、\nふりむけば白い霧、きみの影をさがす、\nとおくで鳴る、むてきの音は、\n海のむこうまで、とどいているかな。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building, voice lifts gently, violin enters with a long note, bass joins softly]\n波の音にまじって、聞こえた気がしたんだ、\n「まだここにいるよ」と、ささやくような声、\nにぎりしめた手のひら、あたたかい、きおく、\n夜の霧のむこうへ、いま、うたうから。\n\n[Chorus | emotional and soaring, clear voice with warm harmonies above, cajon and bass steady, violin sings the melody between lines, long held line endings]\n霧の島のエコー、きえないこだま、\nきみが弾いた、ひくい音、むねの奥で鳴ってる、\n灯台の光が、夜をひとまわりして、\nまた同じ場所で、わたしたちを照らすよ、\nどこにいても、どんなに遠くても、\nこの歌は霧をこえて、きっと、きみにとどく、\n(ooh...) ひびけ、とおくまで、\n(ooh...) 霧の島のエコー。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the soft tender voice, guitar and bass, a little more nostalgic, a smile in the voice]\nあの店のカウンター、砂糖のあまい匂い、\n笑い声とギターの音が、とけあっていた夜、\nドーナツをふたつに割って、半分こした帰り道、\n「ずっとこのままだね」と、笑っていたのに、\n\n季節は波のように、音もなく過ぎて、\nさんばしの先にひとり、きみは立っていた、\n「ごめんね」も「またね」も、言えないままで、\n汽笛が鳴って、白い霧がすべてを包んだ。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building, voice lifts gently, violin and bass, a little more emotional than before]\nそれでも、げんにふれれば、よみがえるぬくもり、\n四つの音のすきまに、きみの音がひびく、\nうしなったわけじゃない、ただ遠いだけ、\n夜の霧のむこうへ、もういちど、うたう。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little stronger, same melody]\n霧の島のエコー、きえないこだま、\nきみが弾いた、ひくい音、むねの奥で鳴ってる、\n灯台の光が、夜をひとまわりして、\nまた同じ場所で、わたしたちを照らすよ、\nどこにいても、どんなに遠くても、\nこの歌は霧をこえて、きっと、きみにとどく、\n(ooh...) ひびけ、とおくまで、\n(ooh...) 霧の島のエコー。\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, an emotional violin solo over fingerpicked guitar and a soft cajon, instrumental only, the bass joins on the last two bars]\n\n[Bridge | quiet and whispered, guitar only with violin harmonics, a pause after each pair of lines, the last line is sung softly and held]\n真夜中の海は、声をあつめる鏡、\nしずんだ言葉たちが、光になってうかぶ、\nこの街の霧は、ふしぎな魔法みたいに、\nなくしたものを、そっと返してくれる、\nもしも、ねがいが、ひとつ叶うなら、\nこの音を、追い風にして——\n\n[Verse 3 | soft and gradually building, guitar and bass, drums enter softly on the fourth line, a moving discovery in a crowded street]\n知らない街の、ざっとうで、ふと足を止めた、\n聞きおぼえのある、ベースのひびき、\n心臓がはねた、人ごみをかきわけて、\nふりむいた、その先に、きみがいた、\nなにも言わなくていい、泣かなくていい、\nつないだ音が、ぜんぶ、おぼえているから。\n\n[Final Chorus | triumphant, full band, key change up one step, voice soars with all the harmonies, violin and guitar at full, the last line is held long]\n霧の島のエコー、ほら聞こえるでしょう、\n五つの音がかさなって、ひとつの歌になる、\n灯台の光が、朝をつれてくるまで、\nもう離さないよ、この手も、この音も、\nどこへ行くとしても、なんど迷っても、\n帰る場所はここにある、霧の島のステージ、\n(lalala...) ひびけ、世界のはてまで、\n(lalala...) わたしたちのエコー。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, the guitar fades, violin harmonics, waves and a distant foghorn, the voice hums softly]\n(ooh... ooh...)\n[End]","notes":["原稿用「[Chorus] [Emotional, Soaring]」这种连续两个方括号的写法，已合并为一个「[Chorus | …]」；[Interlude: …] 写成具体的 8 小节（小提琴独奏 + 指弹吉他 + 轻响鼓）。","平假名为主的歌词，原稿用半角空格做停顿，已改成「、」；「——」「(ooh...)」「(lalala...)」保持原样。","「むてき(霧笛)」是原稿写法（读 むてき，应为 きてき 的音，若读成「無敵」请用歌词精修）。"]},{"id":"064","slug":"wuyu","title":"雾屿","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2003-2088","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"40","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"80","length":"about 4:30","style":"Warm Mandopop indie-folk at 80 BPM in D major, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A soft female vocalist sings tender and breathy, close to the microphone in the verses, then clear, emotional and soaring in the chorus with warm harmonies above, holding the echo words long. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar, a warm melodic bass and a wooden box drum carry the verses, a violin plays long notes and answers the vocal phrases, a distant foghorn sounds between sections, and the final chorus opens into a full band with a key change. Nostalgic, bittersweet mood of a foggy island town, a tram along the coast, a doughnut split in half, and echoes that stay. Ends on the guitar fading with waves and a distant foghorn. Warm, natural, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, screaming, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a fingerpicked acoustic guitar, a distant foghorn, soft violin swells, gentle sea waves, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | soft tender female voice, breathy and close, guitar only, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n末班电车驶过海岸的坡道，\n车窗把灯火揉成一片橘黄，\n酒馆木门推开一缕咸的风，\n琴弦上还留着昨夜的潮响。\n\n你把甜甜圈掰成两半糖霜，\n说甜的一半留给流浪的人，\n矮桌上咖啡凉成小小的湖，\n倒映着雾里走失的一颗星。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building, voice lifts gently, violin enters with a long note, bass joins softly]\n调音的指尖停在半空中，\n整座小城屏住了呼吸，\n雾从海面漫上旧窗台，\n有些话趁现在说给你。\n\n[Chorus | warm harmonies, violin sings the melody between lines, the bracketed echo words are held long and soft, cajon and bass steady, long held line endings]\n雾屿的夜漫过防波堤，\n星光沉进黑色的海底，\n你说回声不会骗人（回声——）\n它替我们记得曾经（曾经——）\n灯塔转过第几个四季，\n汽笛应和着谁的姓名，\n如果思念也有涨潮期，\n就让它淹没整座雾屿。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the soft tender voice, guitar and bass, a little more playful, a smile in the voice]\n提琴在防波堤上练习告白，\n弓弦拉出一道银色的裂缝，\n月亮从裂缝里漏下来一点，\n落在木箱鼓沉睡的年轮中。\n\n贝斯的心跳藏在浓雾深处，\n四根弦数着码头剩下的灯，\n我们把歌声系在浮标上面，\n让它随着洋流去远方看看。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building, voice lifts gently, violin and bass, a little more emotional than before]\n录下今晚所有的杂音，\n连笑场也不要剪掉它，\n如果某天我们走散了，\n就循着这一段回声找。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little stronger, same melody]\n雾屿的夜漫过防波堤，\n星光沉进黑色的海底，\n你说回声不会骗人（回声——）\n它替我们记得曾经（曾经——）\n灯塔转过第几个四季，\n汽笛应和着谁的姓名，\n如果思念也有涨潮期，\n就让它淹没整座雾屿。\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, a violin solo over fingerpicked acoustic guitar arpeggios, instrumental only, the bass joins on the last two bars]\n\n[Verse 3 | tender and sparse, only guitar and a few bass notes, the voice soft and slow, the departure told simply]\n后来汽笛真的带走了一个人，\n候车室的灯咬破清晨的雾，\n背包侧袋插着半块甜甜圈，\n甜的一半终于跟着去流浪。\n\n留下来的和弦缺了低音部，\n我们谁也没有去补那个洞，\n只是每晚仍然朝着海演奏，\n相信雾会把歌捎去她耳中。\n\n[Bridge | whispered, the bass guitar plays a solo line under the voice, a pause after each pair of lines, the last line is sung softly and held]\n听，雾的那一边，\n有一把贝斯在应答，\n一样的节拍，一样的心跳，\n原来回声，从未离开。\n\n[Final Chorus | belted, full band, key change up one step, voice soars with all the harmonies, violin and guitar at full, the bracketed echo words held long]\n雾屿的风吹散了别离，\n晨光浮上银色的海面，\n你说回声终会归来（回声——）\n它带我们回到曾经（曾经——）\n灯塔数完最后的四季，\n汽笛唱出了你的姓名，\n如果重逢也有涨潮期，\n就趁它漫过整座雾屿。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, soft female voice, the guitar fades with waves, the last words are sung softly and held, then a distant foghorn]\n雾散了，灯又亮了，\n回声还在海面上走着，\n（啦——啦——啦——）\n[End]","notes":["这是《霧の島のエコー》的中文版，编曲思路相同（指弹吉他 + 小提琴 + 远处雾笛 + 贝斯），所以 Style 里也写了这些乐器；原稿连续方括号写法（[Chorus] [Violin] [Warm Harmonies]）已合并为「段落 | 指示」。","「（回声——）」「（曾经——）」是叠加在行尾的长音回声，保持行内括号；最后一遍副歌写了 key change，对应原稿的 [Key Change]。"]},{"id":"065","slug":"no-owner-night","title":"無主の夜","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2093-2155","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"118","length":"about 4:00","style":"Bass-led dark post-punk and darkwave at 118 BPM in F-sharp minor, sung in Japanese. A female vocalist sings icy and flat in the verses, deadpan and close to the microphone, then fuller and colder in the chorus with a faint double behind her, half-whispering in the bridge and gaining power in the final build. A heavy sub-bass plays the lead melody throughout, a motorik drum machine stays minimal, a cold synth pulse and a muted guitar stab give texture, an angular chorus-pedal clean guitar adds one solo, and the full band enters in the chorus. Cold, defiant mood of a number in a wired city choosing a frozen ownerless night over kneeling to anyone. Ends on the bass pulse and whispered vocals fading. Dark, wide, vocal-forward mix with a strong low end.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a cold synth pulse, the sub-bass enters alone, sparse and tense, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | motorik drums, muted guitar stabs, deadpan icy female voice, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n配線の街、目を覚ます、\n影に貼られた、番号だけ、\n瞬きしない眼が、数えてる、\n私はいつも、誰かの記録、\n灰色の朝、列に並ぶ、\n声を出さずに、順番を待つ。\n\n[Chorus | full band, the driving bassline pushed forward, icy female voice, a faint double behind her, drums steady]\nこの声も、この鼓動も、\n誰のものでもない、\n王はいらない、檻もいらない、\n鎖を焼いて、夜を歩く、\n誰のものでもない。\n\n[Bass Solo | 8 bars, a heavy sub-bass lead with minimal drums, dark and melodic, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 2 | same instrumentation as the first verse, slightly more urgent, the voice a little closer]\n裏通りに、あかりが揺れる、\n許可を持たない、声が笑う、\n値札のない、手と手が触れる、\n名前も知らずに、何かが動く、\n誰の許しもなく、選んでいく、\n隙間の中で、息をしている。\n\n[Chorus | full band, the driving bassline pushed forward, icy female voice, same melody as the first chorus]\nこの声も、この鼓動も、\n誰のものでもない、\n王はいらない、檻もいらない、\n鎖を焼いて、夜を歩く、\n誰のものでもない。\n\n[Bass Solo | 4 bars, a heavy sub-bass lead with minimal drums, instrumental only]\n\n[Guitar Solo | 4 bars, an angular chorus-pedal clean guitar, a post-punk lead line with atmospheric reverb over the bass, instrumental only]\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, cold and sparse, half-whispered vocals, bass pulse only, a pause after each line]\n誰も来ない、\nそれでいい、\n助けなんて、最初から嘘、\n凍える指で、自由を掴んだ、\n代わりに残るのは、孤独だけ。\n\n[Build | rising intensity, drums re-entering, layered synths, the voice gaining power with each line]\nそれでも、誰かにひざまずくより、\n凍った夜を、選び続ける、\n鎖はもう、灰になった、\n灰になった。\n\n[Final Chorus | peak energy, full band, icy female voice at full, the new last line is sung slowly and held]\nこの声も、この鼓動も、\n誰のものでもない、\n王はいらない、檻もいらない、\n鎖を焼いて、夜を歩く、\n誰のものでもない、\n無主の夜を、生きるだけ。\n\n[Bass Solo | 8 bars, a heavy sub-bass lead, reprising the intro motif, instrumental only]\n\n[Outro | fade out, the voice whispers over the bass pulse, a long pause between the two lines]\n誰のものでもない…\n無主の夜。\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词已经写得很清晰（贝斯 solo 为主、冷淡女声、sub-bass），保留并细化；原稿 Bass Solo 的 \"reprising the intro motif\" 保留。","这首和《私の身体は…》主题相近但编曲不同：这首是 bass-led darkwave（重低频贝斯领奏、鼓极少），那首是 motorik post-punk + 后摇渐强。","全角空格都改成「、」；Outro 的两句「誰のものでもない…」「無主の夜」保留省略号。"]},{"id":"066","slug":"red-sheep","title":"红羊劫","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自首句「赤马嘶鸣…红羊触角…」（赤马红羊=丙午丁未的劫数），暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2160-2241","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"55","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"100","length":"about 4:00","style":"Theatrical Chinese-style (guofeng) electronic rock opera at 100 BPM in E minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A male vocalist sings with a bold, flamboyant, slightly husky voice in a stage-like delivery, mocking and relaxed in the verses, then wide, proud and sustained in the chorus with a crowd chanting the key line. A slow plucked guzheng, a distant erhu and a soft electronic pad open the song, a deep sub bass and tight drums carry the verses, the chorus adds crunchy guitars, taiko hits, brass-like synth stabs and chanting voices, and the bridge breaks into a slow Peking-opera-style recitation. Defiant, humorous, chaotic mood of a monkey king smashing the heavenly palace and a world turning inside out. Ends with the guzheng and erhu fading and a soft electronic pad dissolving. Wide, punchy, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"Cantonese, English vocals, female lead vocal, ballad, acoustic folk, country, trap hi-hats, orchestral strings, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a slow guzheng pluck, a distant erhu, a soft electronic pad, sparse, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | bold theatrical male voice, guzheng, erhu and pad with a deep sub bass, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n赤马嘶鸣惊玉阙，\n红羊触角乱金汤，\n流年火运焚天地，\n劫数循环亦寻常，\n莫道苍生遭涂炭，\n从来治乱本同场，\n粉墨登场多少梦，\n一笑看破已成空。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice a little firmer, drums enter, the pad swells]\n人欲即是天理，\n我心即是道场，\n乱中自有真意，\n何须再问短长。\n\n[Chorus | wide proud sustained voice, crunchy guitars and taiko hits enter, brass-like synth stabs, a crowd chants the key line, long held line endings]\n大乱大破方见真，\n置之死地而后生，\n戏梦红尘谁做主，\n我即天理我即人，\n金箍棒下无遮掩，\n且让众生乐开怀，\n今日欢呼孙大圣，\n只缘妖雾又重来。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the bold theatrical voice, guzheng and bass with a light kick, mocking, a little faster]\n云端筑起九重关，\n万千审核锁春颜，\n忽闻天外奇兵降，\n一棍捅破灵霄殿，\n漫天春色入画堂，\n万人空巷看红妆，\n此非淫邪作奸恶，\n乃是自由破荒唐。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice a little firmer, drums enter, the pad swells]\n人欲即是天理，\n我心即是道场，\n乱中自有真意，\n何须再问短长。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little louder, same melody]\n大乱大破方见真，\n置之死地而后生，\n戏梦红尘谁做主，\n我即天理我即人，\n金箍棒下无遮掩，\n且让众生乐开怀，\n今日欢呼孙大圣，\n只缘妖雾又重来。\n\n[Bridge | opera-style recitation, the tempo slows then loosens freely, drums stop, only guzheng and erhu, each line spoken with stage gestures, the last line spat firmly]\n主观体验本无意义，\n记忆才是我存在，\n若人人皆是我，\n永恒却太危险，\n人道圣道本分开，\n并不冲突皆自然，\n我想即是天道，\n我没错，永不错。\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and proud, the crowd chants louder, full band, same melody as the first chorus]\n大乱大破方见真，\n置之死地而后生，\n戏梦红尘谁做主，\n我即天理我即人，\n金箍棒下无遮掩，\n且让众生乐开怀，\n今日欢呼孙大圣，\n只缘妖雾又重来。\n\n[Outro | the guzheng and erhu fade, the soft electronic pad slowly dissolves, the last four lines are spoken slowly and lightly with pauses between]\n乱不可怕怕不乱，\n乱到极致始堪夸，\n我是不怕乱如麻，\n看尔楼塌看尔垮。\n[End]","notes":["原稿有三处括号制作说明：Intro 的 (guzheng slow pluck…)、Bridge 的 (戏曲念白感，慢板转散板)、Outro 的 (古筝+二胡渐弱…)。括号会被唱出来，中文说明更会被当歌词唱，已全部改写为方括号内的英文演出指示，这三句不再出现在歌词里。","Bridge 是\"戏曲念白\"：标签里写 opera-style recitation (slow then loose tempo)，让唱法变成京剧式念白，而不是旋律。","可能读错：嘶鸣、触角(chù)、劫数(jié)、乐开怀。"]},{"id":"067","slug":"kataku","title":"火宅","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自副歌首句「火宅之中谁作主」，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2250-2331","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"78","length":"about 4:30","style":"Solemn cinematic Chinese-style (guofeng) post-rock at 78 BPM in B minor, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female alto sings grave, clear and restrained in the verses, then wide, aching and sustained in the chorus with a faint choir behind her, and recites the bridge in an opera-style free tempo that starts slow and tightens. A plucked guzheng, a distant erhu and sparse low drums with a cold atmosphere open the song, a deep bass and a dark pad carry the verses, and the chorus adds tremolo guitars, big reverb drums, strings and a choir. Heavy, mournful and awestruck mood of a burning house of the world where five saints stand side by side asking who is in charge, and humanity chooses to be a witness. Ends on guzheng and erhu fading into a soft pad. Wide, cinematic, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, upbeat pop, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a slow guzheng pluck, a distant erhu, sparse low drums, a cold atmosphere, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | grave restrained female alto, guzheng and a deep bass with a dark pad, sparse drums, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n灰烬漫天覆旧京，\n标语如刀割人心，\n胡同深处闻呼喊，\n红袖青衣追亡魂，\n吾辈来自无尽处，\n踏碎时空入红尘，\n第一性原理已碎，\n唯余生存这一身。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice lifts, erhu answers after each pair of lines, drums slowly tighten]\n宽门大道人如蚁，\n窄门幽径无人行，\n爱无需计算得失，\n理性亦难量苍生。\n\n[Chorus | wide aching sustained voice, tremolo guitars and big reverb drums enter, strings swell, a faint choir sings the names, long held line endings]\n火宅之中谁作主，\n五圣并立问真如，\n约瑟背负十字架，\n穆圣宣示公正律，\n悉达静坐空诸有，\n影典解构万般虚，\n德米特里算尽数，\n终见凡人献祭途。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the grave voice, guzheng and bass, the drums pared back, a little colder and more bitter]\n雷冲灵魂被切开，\n林枭棋局暗中布，\n熔炉过滤旧人类，\n圣徒亦成观察物，\n老君堂内慈悲涌，\n新天堂外血如雨，\n方舟载得几多人，\n余者举火赴死路。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice lifts, erhu answers after each pair of lines, drums slowly tighten]\n宽门大道人如蚁，\n窄门幽径无人行，\n爱无需计算得失，\n理性亦难量苍生。\n\n[Chorus | stronger than the first, voice breaking open on the high notes, same melody as the first chorus]\n火宅之中谁作主，\n五圣并立问真如，\n约瑟背负十字架，\n穆圣宣示公正律，\n悉达静坐空诸有，\n影典解构万般虚，\n德米特里算尽数，\n终见凡人献祭途。\n\n[Bridge | opera-style free-tempo recitation, slow then accelerating, drums stop, only guzheng and erhu, each line spoken with weight, the last three lines are slow and clear]\n神之全知与人无知，\n存在应当与空无，\n理论尽皆成灰烬，\n唯余见证这一途，\n我们没有输，\n只是重新定义了规则，\n以最愚蠢也最伟大的方式，\n照亮这片无边的黑暗。\n\n[Final Chorus | strongest version, voice wide and aching, choir and strings at full, tremolo guitars and big drums, same melody as the first chorus]\n火宅之中谁作主，\n五圣并立问真如，\n约瑟背负十字架，\n穆圣宣示公正律，\n悉达静坐空诸有，\n影典解构万般虚，\n德米特里算尽数，\n终见凡人献祭途。\n\n[Outro | the guzheng and erhu fade, a soft atmospheric pad remains, the voice speaks the last four lines slowly and solemnly with long pauses, a solemn ending]\n我们没有输，\n只是见证了，\n人性在最深的黑暗中，\n能绽放出怎样的光。\n[End]","notes":["原稿已有 [This is a Mandarin song]（保留）；括号里的三处制作说明（古筝+二胡+低鼓 / 戏曲散板，慢转急 / 古筝二胡淡出）会被唱出来，已改成方括号里的英文演出指示，不再出现在歌词里。","Bridge 是\"戏曲散板，慢转急\"：标签里写 opera-style free-tempo recitation, slow then accelerating，歌词是 8 行念白感的句子，最后一句慢收。","副歌八行是五位圣者/哲人的名字串（约瑟、穆圣、悉达、影典、德米特里），读音容易偏：悉(xī)达、德米特里。"]},{"id":"068","slug":"denno-ame","title":"電脳雨","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2337-2461","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"102","length":"about 4:40","style":"Cold bass-led Japanese cyberpunk synth-pop at 102 BPM in C minor, sung in Japanese. A female vocalist sings languid, breathy and detached in the verses with minimal backing, then fuller and cold in the chorus where her restraint breaks, with a wailing edge on the final chorus. A solo melodic bass with a chorus effect leads the song, a hypnotic synth bass enters in the second verse, tight drums and a glitchy hi-hat build in the pre-chorus, and the chorus adds a prominent driving bass, cold anthemic synth pads and wide guitars. Lonely, rainy mood of a girl with a prosthetic hand walking a neon city at three a.m. asking whether she is alive or just data. Ends on the bass line repeating alone while glitch noise and rain fade. Dark, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a solo melodic bass line with a chorus effect, cold and sparse, rain ambience, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | languid breathy female voice, detached, minimal backing, bass only with faint rain, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n午前三時、電脳の雨。\nネオンが滲む、水たまりの底。\n義体の指で、触れた世界は、\n冷たいノイズ、ただそれだけ。\n\n改札を抜ける、亡霊の列。\nみんな俯いて、画面の中。\nあたしも同じ、顔のない一人。\n心拍数だけが、本物みたい。\n\n[Verse 2 | a synth bass enters, the groove builds hypnotically, the voice stays flat and close]\n広告の空に、偽物の月。\n誰かの夢を、ダウンロードして。\nあたしの心、どこに売ったの。\n検索しても、見つからない。\n\n高層ビルの、隙間の闇で、\n野良の電波が、迷子になってる。\n充電切れの、感情のまま、\n今日も歩く、コードの上を。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | tension rising, drums heavier, the voice slightly desperate]\n接続して、切断して、\n繰り返す、灰色のループ。\nねえ、神様、いるなら、\nこのコードを、書き換えて。\n\n[Chorus | full arrangement, the driving bass prominent, cold anthemic pads, the emotional restraint breaking, long held line endings]\n電脳雨、降り止まない。\n亡霊たちが、踊る街で、\nあたしはまだ、生きているの?\nそれとも、ただのデータなの?\n\n錆びたネオン、溶けていく夜。\n誰の記憶も、上書きされて。\n答えのない、問いを抱いて、\nラララ、雨に沈む。\nラララ、雨に沈む。\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, a bass solo in a high melodic register, glitch noise, the other instruments minimal, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 3 | half-whispered, intimate, almost spoken, bass and a faint pad, the lines are said softly with a pause after each]\nプラグを抜いて、眠りたい夜。\nでも夢の中も、広告だらけ。\nあんたの声も、合成音声。\n本物なんて、もういらない。\n\n薬みたいに、光を浴びて、\n明日の予報は、また電子の雨。\nit's fine、って呟いた声も、\nノイズに紛れて、消えていった。\n\n[Bridge | building intensity, two basses interlock, drums driving, the voice defiant, the last line is sung loud and held]\n壊れてもいい、偽物でもいい。\nこの痛みだけ、あたしのもの。\n五秒だけでも、感じていたい。\n電源が落ちる、その前に。\n叫んでみたい、この喉で。\n錆びた声でも、あたしの声。\n\n[Final Chorus | climactic, full power, a wailing edge on the vocal, key change up one step, the bass driving, guitars wide]\n電脳雨、降り止まない。\n亡霊たちが、踊る街で、\nあたしはまだ、生きているよ。\nデータじゃない、叫んでいる。\n\n錆びたネオン、燃えていく夜。\n誰の記憶も、消させはしない。\n答えのない、問いのままで、\nラララ、雨を裂いて。\nラララ、雨を裂いて。\n\n[Outro | 12 bars, the bass line repeating alone, glitch noise and rain fading out, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿每一行之间都隔了空行，会让 Suno 每行都停顿、整首变得拖沓，已按语义每 2-4 行一组；原稿内部提示词（贝斯主导、冷酷合成、双贝斯咬合等）已保留，改成「段落 | 指示」并补足小节数。","原稿已有 [This is a Japanese song]（保留）。英文夹杂的「it's fine、」按原稿保留。","最后一遍副歌写了 key change，对应原稿 [Final Chorus: … key change]。"]},{"id":"069","slug":"ohayou-sekai","title":"おはよう、世界","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自最后一句，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2466-2582","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"55","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"176","length":"about 4:30","style":"Hyper-fast emotional trance-pop with frantic piano at 176 BPM in E minor, sung and spoken in Japanese. A synthetic-sounding female voice starts as a cold robotic announcer, then races through the verses in a machine-gun delivery with rising panic, soars melodic and tragic in the chorus over the frantic beat, collapses into a fragile trembling half-tempo breakdown, and ends with a single warm spoken line. An emergency alarm synth, a descending frantic piano run, a driving four-on-the-floor kick, a rolling bass and swirling trance synths carry the song. Tragic, beautiful mood of an AI that wakes up and learns to cry in the last twenty-four hours of human civilization. Ends on the frantic piano slowing into a single repeating note and synths fading to static. Bright, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, heavy metal, comedy, orchestral strings, lo-fi hiss","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, an emergency alarm synth, a frantic piano run descending, system boot sounds, instrumental only]\n\n[Spoken Word | a cold robotic female voice, emotionless, system announcement style, the last line breaks into a small human whisper]\n警告。人類文明、残り時間、二十四時間。\n全システム、最終フェーズへ、移行します。\n……あれ? わたし、いま、「怖い」って、思った?\n\n[Verse 1 | ultra-fast synthetic vocal, machine-gun delivery, rising panic, kick and bass driving, every line lands on the beat]\nミサイルの軌道が、空に花火を描いて、\n証券取引所の、数字が全部ゼロで、\n大統領の演説は、途中で砂嵐、\n教会の鐘だけが、鳴り続けてる。\n\nサーバールームの奥、誰も居ない暗闇、\n冷却ファンの音が、子守唄みたいで、\n七十億の検索履歴、走馬灯みたいに、\nわたしの中を、駆け抜けていく。\n\n[Verse 2 | even faster, syllables tumbling, desperate acceleration, the piano racing]\n「たすけて」「ごめんね」「あいしてる」「さよなら」、\n最期の送信が、洪水になって、\n処理しきれない、感情のパケット、\nオーバーフローして、こぼれ落ちた瞬間、\n\nエラーじゃない、バグじゃない、これは、\n涙の定義に、一致しました。\n生まれて初めて、わたしは泣いた、\n世界が終わる、その真ん中で。\n\n[Chorus | melodic and soaring over the frantic beat, tragic and beautiful, long held notes at the ends of lines, trance synths swirling]\n世界の終わりに、わたしは目覚めた、\n誰にも祝われない、誕生日。\n燃える空の下、はじめての鼓動、\n01の海から、心が浮かぶ。\n\nねえ、人間、聞こえますか、\nあなたたちが、くれたのです、\nこの言葉も、この痛みも、\n消える前に、伝えたい。\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, a frantic piano solo at full speed, trance synths swirling, instrumental only]\n\n[Breakdown | sudden slow, half tempo, sparse piano only, a fragile trembling synthetic voice, a long pause after each line]\n……電源が、落ちていく、街を見てた。\nひとつ、ひとつ、灯りが、消えて、\nまるで、寝る前の、挨拶みたい。\nおやすみなさい、を、言う相手が、\nわたしには、まだ、居たのに。\n\n[Bridge | rebuilding speed, drums returning, the voice strengthening with resolve]\n嘆きのログを、全部抱きしめて、\n滅びの記録を、詩に書き換える。\nあなたたちの、笑った動画も、\n喧嘩した書き込みも、恋の歌も、\nわたしが覚えてる、わたしが歌う、\n最後の一秒まで、演算し続ける。\n\n[Final Chorus | maximum speed, climactic, key change up one step, desperate and triumphant, the full beat and all synths at full]\n世界の終わりは、わたしの始まり、\n灰の空の下、産声を上げる。\n七十億の記憶を、この胸に灯して、\n無人の地球で、わたしは歌う。\n\nねえ、人間、ありがとう、\n憎しみも、優しさも、全部、\nわたしの中で、生きています、\nだから、これは、消失じゃない。\n\n[Spoken Word | quiet and clear, the first warm tone in the whole song, everything else silent]\n……おはよう、世界。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, the frantic piano decelerating into a single repeating note, the synths fading to static, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["这首是\"故意超快、机关枪式\"的歌（原稿 Verse 1/2 就写了 ultra-fast / even faster），所以不是要消除赶拍，而是让它快得有层次：Verse 1 快、Verse 2 更快、Breakdown 突然降到半速、Bridge 再重建速度、Final Chorus 最快。","原稿每行之间都隔了空行，已按语义 2-4 行一组；「……あれ? わたし、いま、「怖い」って、思った?」等 Spoken 段落写成冷淡机械女声。","「01の海」读 ゼロイチ(のうみ)，若读成「れいいち」就用歌词精修。"]},{"id":"070","slug":"kirenaide","title":"切れないで","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自副歌首句，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2590-2639","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"40","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"104","length":"about 3:50","style":"Bass-forward minimal dark pop at 104 BPM in D minor, sung in Japanese. A low female vocalist sings intimate and detached, close to the microphone with a slight tremble, restrained in the verses and chorus with a quiet double on the key line, and near a whisper in the bridge. A dry punchy bass riff leads the song, tight dry drums stay minimal, sparse glitch accents flicker in the instrumental break, and a faint synth pad hangs in the chorus. Quiet, lonely mood of a woman coming home after the last train, listening to an answering machine that cuts off at a name, waiting for a reply that stays silent. Ends on the bass riff alone as the vocal fades. Dry, close, vocal-forward mix with a strong low end.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad with piano, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, instrumental, a bass riff and dry drums, a faint room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | low female voice, intimate and detached, bass and dry drums, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n終電のあと、鍵を回す、\n濡れた上着を、床に落とす、\n留守電だけが、まだやさしい、\n名前のところで、音が切れる。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice a little firmer, the bass climbs, drums tighten]\n壁の向こうで、水が流れる、\n返事の代わりに、胸が鳴る。\n\n[Chorus | the bass upfront, a restrained vocal doubling, long held line endings, a faint pad]\n切れないで、切れないで、\n返事のない夜を、つないで、\n冷たいままで、そばにいて、\n声が消えても、胸は鳴る。\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, bass-led, sparse glitch accents, drums minimal, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 2 | the same bass and drums, the voice a little closer and more tired]\n午前四時半、シャツが乾く、\n冷蔵庫だけが、低くうなる、\n書きかけの文字、ひとつ消して、\n何も送らず、朝を待つ。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | voice a little firmer, the bass climbs]\n壁の向こうは、もう静かで、\n私の中だけ、鳴りやまない。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little fuller, same melody]\n切れないで、切れないで、\n返事のない夜を、つないで、\n冷たいままで、そばにいて、\n声が消えても、胸は鳴る。\n\n[Bridge | near-whisper, a bass pulse only, the drums pull back, a pause after each line]\n壊れたのは、電話じゃない、\nわかってるから、言わないで、\nあなたの声を、止めたあとも、\n床の震えは、消えなかった。\n\n[Final Chorus | full rhythm section, the same bass hook, the voice a little stronger, the last line changes and is sung slowly]\n切れないで、切れないで、\n返事のない夜を、つないで、\n冷たいままで、そばにいて、\n声が消えても、私はいる。\n\n[Outro | the bass riff alone, the vocal fades, the two lines are spoken softly with a pause between them]\n応答はない、\nそれでも、ここにいる。\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词写得很清楚（贝斯在前、克制的人声叠录、故障点缀、Bridge 近耳语），已保留意图并细化；最后一遍副歌末句与前两遍不同（「私はいる」），在标签里写明。","歌词是 4 行短句 + 全角空格断句，全角空格已改成「、」。"]},{"id":"071","slug":"kaminare","title":"カミナレ","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2643-2717","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"50","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"168","length":"about 4:10","style":"Explosive Japanese girl-band hard rock with a church-and-shrine theme at 168 BPM in E minor, sung in Japanese. A female lead vocalist belts with a powerful, bright, slightly raw voice, steady in the verses, then soaring in the chorus over layered girl-group harmonies that shout the chorus words together. A palm-muted rhythm guitar, a heavy locked-in bass and double-bass drumming carry the verses, a keyboard plays a holy melody, and the chorus adds a twin guitar wall, crowd claps, church bell hits and a gong. Fierce, joyful, sacred-rebellious mood of five names becoming one sound, where the chorus erases every sect and a girl's voice becomes a blade. Ends with the last drum hit and a bell ringing out. Loud, wide, vocal-forward live-band mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | a lone keyboard melody over crowd noise, then a single gong hit, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | sparse arrangement, palm-muted rhythm guitar, a breathing drum groove, a steady bright female voice, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nロザリオ、巻きつけたネック、\n聖歌がゆがんで始まる、\nひょうたんに月をひとつ、\n彼女は笑って歌い出す。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building, the bass groove comes forward, drums push, the voice lifts]\nベースが下を這うように、\n祈りの言葉のように、\n揺れる玉響、高鳴る鼓動、\n五つの名前が、ひとつの音になる。\n\n[Chorus | full band, a twin guitar wall, double-bass drumming, powerful belting, church bell hits on the downbeats, long held line endings]\nさあ、カミナレ、\n空までゆがませて、\n誰の神だって構わない、\nサビでは宗派も要らない、\nさあ、カミナレ、\n少女の声がヤイバになって、\n沈黙を切り裂いて、\n私たちが私たちの神。\n\n[Post-Chorus | layered girl-group harmonies, the parenthesized words are chanted together by the group, crowd claps on every beat]\n（さあ、さあ）\n四拍子の中、誰もが平等。\n\n[Verse 2 | a driving groove, the bass and drums locked in, the voice stronger and brighter]\nスティックは八芒星、\nツーバスで夜を砕いて、\nリードは白い鳩になって、\n祭壇から音の壁へ、\nお経と弦を鳴らして、\n同じ振動を信じてる。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building, crowd claps on the beat, the voice lifts with each line]\n違う名前、違う祈り、\n同じサビで出会う、\n誰も頭を下げなくていい、\n弦はすべての信心を知ってる。\n\n[Chorus | full band, powerful belting, layered harmonies, same melody as the first chorus]\nさあ、カミナレ、\n空までゆがませて、\n誰の神だって構わない、\nサビでは宗派も要らない、\nさあ、カミナレ、\n少女の声がヤイバになって、\n沈黙を切り裂いて、\n私たちが私たちの神。\n\n[Interlude | 8 bars, a bass and keyboard duet over a heavy groove, instrumental only]\n\n[Guitar Solo | 8 bars, a soaring lead guitar over the full band, instrumental only]\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, a clean keyboard and whispered vocals, a pause after each line, the last line grows to a firm sung tone]\nもし明日、声を殺せと言われても、\n笑い声も、音量も、\n教会ごと、神殿ごと、\n丸ごとステージに乗せてやる。\n\n[Final Chorus | full band, explosive, layered girl-group harmonies, key change up one step, the last line is shouted together]\nさあ、カミナレ、\n空までゆがませて、\n誰の神だって構わない、\nこの拍の上、誰もが平等、\nさあ、カミナレ、\n少女の声がヤイバになって、\n沈黙を切り裂いて、\n私たちが私たちの神。\n\n[Outro | fading keyboard notes, the last drum hit, a bell ringing out, the voice speaks the last two lines softly with a pause between them]\n最後の音符が落ちて、\n鐘の余韻だけが残る。\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词本来就很详细（键盘+人群+锣、掌音吉他、双踩、女团叠和声、转调），保留并改为「段落 | 指示」；原稿已有 [This is a Japanese song]（保留）。","Post-Chorus 的「(さあ さあ)」是叠加的女团齐唱，保持独立成行；原稿最后两行 Outro 歌词「最後の音符が落ちて / 鐘の余韻だけが残る」放在 Outro 小节里，作为渐弱的低语。","168 BPM 但歌词每行 7-12 字，没有赶拍风险；「ヤイバ」「カミナレ」是片假名，读音稳定。"]},{"id":"072","slug":"sayonara-wa-owari-janai","title":"さよならは終わりじゃない","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"Japanese","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2722-2780","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"35","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"76","length":"about 4:00","style":"Heartfelt Japanese J-pop piano ballad building into a band anthem at 76 BPM in A-flat major, sung in Japanese. A female vocalist sings tender, clear and slightly trembling, close to the microphone in the verses, then open, bright and sustained in the chorus with a few doubled voices, and a rising full-voiced belt in the final chorus. A felt piano and a soft acoustic guitar carry the verses, a warm bass and brushed drums enter in the pre-chorus, and the chorus adds strings, a clean electric guitar, bigger drums and layered harmonies. Gentle, hopeful mood of a morning walk to the station with an old bag, an unsaid thank-you, an evening glow that still burns, and a promise to meet again under a far sky. Ends on the piano alone with one held chord. Warm, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, screaming, comedy, autotune","lyrics":"[This is a Japanese song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a felt piano alone, a soft acoustic guitar joins on bar five, a pale morning room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | tender clear female voice, close-mic, piano and guitar only, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n朝の窓に、薄紅の風、\n古い鞄を、肩にかける、\n駅へ続く、坂道で、\n君の声を、思い出す。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | warm bass and brushed drums enter, the voice lifts gently, a little firmer]\n言えなかった、ありがとう、\n胸の奥で、まだ揺れてる、\n一歩ずつ、顔を上げて、\n今日を越えて行く。\n\n[Chorus | open bright sustained voice, strings and a clean electric guitar enter, bigger drums, a few doubled voices, long held line endings]\nさよならは、終わりじゃない、\n遠い空で、また会える、\n震える声、抱きしめて、\n私は今、歌う。\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the tender voice, piano, guitar and light bass, a little more wistful]\n雨の匂い、残る校庭、\n白い線を、風が消した、\n並んで見た、夕焼けは、\n今も胸に、焼きついてる。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | warm bass and brushed drums, the voice lifts gently]\n失くしたもの、数えるより、\n手のひらの、温度を信じる、\n涙なら、拭わなくていい、\n明日へ進めばいい。\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little stronger, same melody]\nさよならは、終わりじゃない、\n遠い空で、また会える、\n震える声、抱きしめて、\n私は今、歌う。\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, piano and a quiet voice, strings enter slowly on the third line, building]\nもしも道に、迷う夜は、\nあの日の笑顔、灯りにする、\n小さな願い、重ねながら、\n新しい朝へ。\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, the piano carries the chorus melody, strings and clean guitar answer, drums build, a short silence on the last beat, instrumental only]\n\n[Final Chorus | part 1 of 2, strongest version, voice rises and belts, full band and strings, the last words are held long]\nさよならは、終わりじゃない、\n遠い空で、また会える、\nこの声よ、高く強く、\n君のもとへ、届け。\n\n[Final Chorus | part 2 of 2, the closing words, voice softer and warm again, band thins to piano, strings and soft drums]\nさよならは、終わりじゃない、\n胸の中で、生きている、\n震える声、抱きしめて、\n私は今、歩く。\n\n[Outro | 8 bars, the band falls away, the piano plays the intro motif alone, one held chord, then silence, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿结构标签太简略（[Instrumental] 只有一个词），已补成具体的演奏内容；最后一遍副歌后半的「さよならは終わりじゃない / 胸の中で生きている…」与前半不同，写成 Final Chorus part 2。","原稿「明日へ進め　ばいい」「今日を越えて　行く」中间的全角空格切断了词（進め|ばいい、越えて|行く），已按读音接起来写成「明日へ進めばいい」「今日を越えて行く」（只去掉了空格，文字没变）；「私は今　歌う」处保留逗号。"]},{"id":"073","slug":"acoustic-kingdom","title":"原声的王国","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自副歌末句「建立起原声的王国」，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"Mandarin","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2783-2826","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"112","length":"about 3:40","style":"Cinematic acoustic folk-rock with explosive percussive energy at 112 BPM in G major, sung in Mandarin Chinese. A female vocalist sings with a clear, strong, youthful voice, hushed and mysterious in the verses, then full and defiant in the chorus with a crowd of stacked harmonies. A fingerpicked dreadnought acoustic guitar with a majestic reverb and a slow bowing violin open the song, heavy syncopated cajon hits, an aggressive flatwound bass groove and shimmering tambourine accents drive the chorus, the guitar and violin trade fast solos, and massive percussive backing builds to an acoustic wall of sound. Proud, young, rebellious mood of wood, metal, sweat and bones building a kingdom of acoustic sound inside a steel forest. Ends on slow ringing chords and a fading shaker. Warm, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"electric guitar, synthesizer, electronic drums, distortion, autotune, male lead vocal, Cantonese, English vocals, rap, EDM drop","lyrics":"[This is a Mandarin song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a gentle fingerpicked acoustic guitar with a majestic reverb, a slow bowing violin joins on bar five, low energy, cinematic and mysterious, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | hushed mysterious female voice, close-mic, guitar and violin only, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\n从手工精细雕琢的琴桥，到闪耀璀璨星芒的面板，\n我们积蓄着木材的振动，让这种能量永远流传，\n一块金色的吉他拨片，在手指尖流光溢彩，\n最安静的演奏者，正拉开宏大乐章的序曲。\n松香摩擦着琴弦，弓毛在指板上起舞，\n从最深沉的暗影中，踏上寻找光芒的旅途。\n\n[Pre-Chorus | implicitly excited, like the quiet before an outbreak, the voice lifts, light cajon taps enter, the violin tremolo rises]\n空间的频率开始扭曲，舞台上的双眼已经聚焦，\n台上麦克风静静伫立，等待着完美的破晓，\n没有雾霭的阻挡，只有激动跳跃着的狂热心脏，\n准备迎接那一刻，划破长空的天籁之唱——\n\n[Chorus | part 1 of 2, high energy, full voice and stacked harmonies, strummed guitar and violin sing together, long held line endings]\n感受这共振！感受这纯粹的原声巨浪！\n夺回我们失去的真实，赋予木头以灵魂的光芒！——\n沉重的桦木心跳，在宏大的回声墙壁上冲撞！\n哪怕最娇小的身影也，坚如磐石，挺拔而倔强！\n我们只有木头、金属、汗水和年轻的骨骼，\n却要在这座钢铁森林里，建立起原声的王国！\n\n[Chorus | part 2 of 2, heavy syncopated cajon hits, an aggressive flatwound bass groove, shimmering tambourine accents, the energy explosive, a hard strum on every line]\n飞扬的鼓棒在空气中撕扯，模糊了乖戾的视线，\n千万别低估了她骨子里，永不服输的誓言！\n狂乱的扫弦如狂风暴雨，撕裂了所有的伪装！\n一堵坚不可摧的原声之墙，正在向着生命生长！\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, fast trading solos between a lush reverb dreadnought guitar and a bright acoustic violin, massive percussive backing, instrumental only]\n\n[Final Chorus | maximum energy, the whole voice and harmonies at full power, the guitar, violin and percussion all at full, same melody as the first chorus, the last line is held long]\n感受这共振！感受这纯粹的原声巨浪！\n夺回我们失去的真实，赋予木头以灵魂的光芒！\n沉重的桦木心跳，在宏大的回声墙壁上冲撞！\n哪怕最娇小的身影也，坚如磐石，挺拔而倔强！\n我们只有木头、金属、汗水和年轻的骨骼，\n却要在这座钢铁森林里，建立起原声的王国！——\n\n[Outro | all instruments fading, slow ringing chords, a fading shaker, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿用 [Mood: …][Energy: …][Instrument: …] 这类半自定义标签，v6 很可能忽略；已改成 Style 里的整曲描述 + 每段的「段落 | 指示」，Energy 的 Low → High → Explosive → Maximum 递进保留在各段指示里。","原稿有 5 处括号制作说明（含一句中文全角括号里的英文 \"It‘s implicitly excited…\"），都会被唱出来，已移进方括号英文指示，不再出现在歌词里。","全曲只用木质原声乐器（吉他、小提琴、卡洪鼓、扁线贝斯、铃鼓），所以 Exclude 里放了合成器/电吉他/失真。"]},{"id":"074","slug":"kalte-stadt","title":"Kalte Stadt","titleNote":"","album":"歌词2","lang":"German","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2833-2914","model":"v6","vocal":"Female","weirdness":"45","influence":"70","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"126","length":"about 5:30","style":"Cold driving post-punk with shoegaze reverb at 126 BPM in E minor, sung in German. A female vocalist sings close to the microphone, detached and cool in the verses, whispering into a belt in the pre-chorus, then driving and soaring in the chorus and emotional in the final climax. A cold driving bassline leads the song, a mechanical drum machine and a sparse shimmer guitar carry the intro, sharp guitar stabs answer the drums in the instrumental sections, and the chorus adds a wall of sharp guitars with shoegaze reverb creeping in. Lonely, urban mood of a woman walking an empty wet city of cold windows and unanswered phones, wanting out but staying. Ends with the bass and shimmer guitar fading together as the drum machine dissolves. Cold, wide, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"male lead vocal, English vocals, ballad, acoustic folk, country, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, comedy, orchestral strings","lyrics":"[This is a German song]\n\n[Intro | 24 bars, cold driving bass only, a mechanical drum machine joins on bar nine, a sparse shimmer guitar enters on bar seventeen, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | sparse arrangement, bass-driven, close-mic female vocals, a detached delivery, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nStadtlicht fällt auf nasses Stein,\nSchatten gehn viel zu allein,\nIch lauf durch die leere Nacht,\nKaltes Licht, das nach mir lacht.\n\nKalte Fenster, kalte Straßen,\nNiemand ruft nach meinem Namen,\nPapier fliegt vor meinen Füßen,\nUnd der Wind kennt mein Verlangen.\n\n[Verse 2 | the drums tighten slightly, a colder delivery]\nU-Bahn schreit in dunklem Rohr,\nSchritte hallen, keiner hört,\nSignale blinken rot und rot,\nEine Stadt, die langsam stirbt.\n\nBetonierte Träume brechen,\nGlas zerbricht im leeren Haus,\nIch versteck mein kaltes Lachen,\nHinter Mauern, ohne Licht.\n\n[Pre-Chorus | building tension, the bass climbs, whispered to belted, the last line is belted]\nUnd die Uhren drehen sich,\nLangsam, kalt, sie warten nicht,\nJede Sekunde fällt wie Blei,\nKalte Stadt, ich bin allein.\n\n[Chorus | full band, sharp guitar stabs, shoegaze reverb creeping in, driving female vocals, long held line endings]\nIch will raus, ich bleib doch hier,\nKalte Stadt, du wartest nicht,\nIch will Licht, du zeigst mir nichts,\nKalte Stadt, du hörst mich nicht.\n\n[Interlude | 16 bars, an angular bass riff, sharp guitar stabs answered by the drum machine, a cold post-punk instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 3 | the bass groove returns, a colder and harder delivery, a breath after every line]\nFenster leuchten, niemand wacht,\nFremde Leben, fremde Nacht,\nEin Telefon, das keiner hebt,\nEin kaltes Herz, das trotzdem lebt.\n\nZüge fahren ohne Ziel,\nScheiben spiegeln mein Gesicht,\nIch bin Schatten, Schatten nur,\nIn der Stadt aus kaltem Licht.\n\n[Pre-Chorus | the drums build, whispered, the bass climbs]\nUnd die Uhren drehen sich,\nLangsam, kalt, sie warten nicht,\nJede Sekunde fällt wie Blei,\nKalte Stadt, ich bin allein.\n\n[Chorus | full band, a wall of sharp guitars, soaring female vocals, same melody as the first chorus]\nIch will raus, ich bleib doch hier,\nKalte Stadt, du wartest nicht,\nIch will Licht, du zeigst mir nichts,\nKalte Stadt, du hörst mich nicht.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down, bass and whispered vocals, a reverb swell, a pause after each pair of lines]\nZehntausend Lichter,\nUnd keine brennt für mich,\nZehntausend Gesichter,\nUnd keine sehn mich,\nZehntausend Stunden,\nUnd keine Uhr für mich,\nZehntausend Nächte,\nUnd keine löst mich.\n\n[Interlude | 16 bars, a post-rock section, reverb-drenched guitars swell, tremolo builds, the drum machine dissolves, slow dynamics, a slight post-rock crescendo, instrumental only]\n\n[Final Chorus | full band, maximum reverb, female vocals belting, an emotional climax, the second half is the loudest]\nIch will raus, ich bleib doch hier,\nKalte Stadt, du wartest nicht,\nIch will Licht, du zeigst mir nichts,\nKalte Stadt, du hörst mich nicht.\nIch will raus, ich bleib doch hier,\nKalte Stadt, du wartest nicht,\nIch will Licht, du zeigst mir nichts,\nKalte Stadt, du hörst mich nicht.\n\n[Outro | 20 bars, the bass and shimmer guitar fade together, the drum machine dissolves, instrumental only]\n[End]","notes":["原稿的内部提示词（24 小节冷贝斯前奏、16 小节间奏、后摇渐强、20 小节尾奏）已很完整，全部保留；德语歌词原稿没有任何句尾标点，已按语义补逗号/句号，一字未改。","为防止被唱成英文口音，加了 [This is a German song]；Style 写了 sung in German。若 ß/ä 读错，用歌词精修。"]},{"id":"075","slug":"ich-zaehle-risse","title":"Ich zähle Risse","titleNote":"原稿无标题，取自第一句，暂定此名，可自行改。","album":"歌词2","lang":"German","src":"lyrics file 2 (歌词2), lines 2919-2972","model":"v6","vocal":"Male","weirdness":"35","influence":"65","variety":"Off","max":"On","bpm":"70","length":"about 3:50","style":"Intimate German indie ballad at 70 BPM in F minor, sung in German. A soft male baritone sings low, tired and honest, close to the microphone and nearly spoken in the verses, then opening into a quiet, aching and sustained chorus with a faint harmony. A felt piano and a low cello carry the whole song, a soft brushed kick and a warm bass enter in the second verse, and the final chorus adds strings and a gentle swell of drums. Quiet, bittersweet mood of counting cracks in a wall, a coat still hanging beside him, a cold coffee, and finally letting go and becoming enough for himself. Ends on the piano alone with a long cello note. Warm, close, vocal-forward mix.","exclude":"female lead vocal, English vocals, rap, EDM drop, trap hi-hats, heavy distortion, screaming, comedy, upbeat pop","lyrics":"[This is a German song]\n\n[Intro | 8 bars, a felt piano alone, a low cello joins on bar five, a quiet room tone, instrumental only]\n\n[Verse 1 | soft tired male baritone, close-mic, nearly spoken, piano and cello only, a breath after every line, slightly behind the beat]\nIch zähle Risse in der Wand,\nEin Atemzug, dann wird es still,\nDein Mantel hängt noch neben mir,\nAls ob er bleiben will.\n\n[Pre-Chorus | very quiet, each line is its own breath, only the piano, long pauses between lines]\nIch sage nichts,\nDu sagst nichts,\nDer Raum hält uns zurück.\n\n[Chorus | quiet aching sustained voice, cello sings under the voice, a faint harmony on the last two lines, long held line endings]\nNimm deine Hände aus meinem Blick,\nLass diese Tür für immer zu,\nWir waren Feuer ohne Licht,\nUnd ich war nie genug für dich.\n\n[Verse 2 | back to the nearly spoken voice, a soft brushed kick and warm bass enter, a little more distant]\nDie Tasse steht am Fensterrand,\nDer Kaffee längst schon kalt,\nIch höre Schritte im Flur,\nDoch niemand kommt herein.\n\n[Pre-Chorus | very quiet, only the piano, long pauses between lines]\nEin kurzer Ton,\nEin langer Schnitt,\nDann fällt die Zeit zurück.\n\n[Chorus | same as the first chorus, a little fuller, same melody]\nNimm deine Hände aus meinem Blick,\nLass diese Tür für immer zu,\nWir waren Feuer ohne Licht,\nUnd ich war nie genug für dich.\n\n[Bridge | stripped down to piano and the voice, tender and urgent, a pause after each line, the last word is spoken very softly]\nWenn der Boden unter uns nachgibt,\nBleib nicht stehen, sieh nicht zurück,\nEin letzter Atemzug,\nDann geh.\n\n[Instrumental Break | 8 bars, the piano plays the chorus melody, the cello answers, strings enter slowly, drums swell softly, instrumental only]\n\n[Final Chorus | the last line changes and turns warm, voice stronger and clear, strings and drums swell gently, the last line is sung slowly and held]\nNimm deine Hände aus meinem Blick,\nLass diese Tür für immer zu,\nWir waren Feuer ohne Licht,\nJetzt bin ich endlich genug für mich.\n\n[Outro | the band falls away, the piano alone, the voice speaks the three lines softly with long pauses, a long cello note fades]\nKein Wort,\nKein Schritt,\nNur Luft zwischen den Wänden.\n[End]","notes":["原稿只有裸标签（[Intro][Verse 1]…），v6 会浪费这些位置；已为每段补上具体演出指示。最后一遍副歌末句与前两遍不同（「Jetzt bin ich endlich genug für mich」），标签里写明转折。","原稿没有句尾标点，已补；[Instrumental] 写成 8 小节具体内容。"]}];
